<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#AuthorityDomain> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Desired state is layer 2 of the 4-layer model. It changes only through\naudited controller decisions; absence is never destructive intent." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cluster desired state" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/authority_domains.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/cluster_controller/cluster_controller_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "deleting desired state based on installed-state observations" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "doctor or node-agent direct writes to desired state — observers never write the layer they observe" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "treating a missing control-plane key as a stop or delete command" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasTruthLayer> "desired" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "cluster doctor (observation only)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "node agent (convergence)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "repository (release resolution)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayWrite> "cluster controller (release pipeline, platform-upgrade)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustMutateVia> "controller typed RPCs / release workflows — every desired-state change belongs to a workflow run" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustReadVia> "controller RPCs or direct etcd read of controller-owned keys (read-only)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownerService> "cluster controller (cluster_controller.ClusterControllerService)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "DesiredService records (/globular/resources/DesiredService/*)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "ServiceRelease records (/globular/resources/ServiceRelease/*)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "release waves and per-node apply gates" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#AuthorityDomain> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "RBAC is deny-wins: explicit deny overrides allow, ownership, and every\nshortcut, and propagates down resource paths." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RBAC permissions" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/authority_domains.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/rbac/rbac_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "backend trusting a proxy/user header or peer certificate instead of the originating principal" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "bypassing the interceptor chain (auth → RBAC → audit)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "owner / service-account / bootstrap shortcuts that skip the explicit-deny check" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasTruthLayer> "desired" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "interceptor chain (every authorized RPC)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "services validating access" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayWrite> "rbac service via typed RPCs" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustMutateVia> "rbac typed RPCs (SetResourcePermissions etc.) — never direct store writes" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustReadVia> "rbac validation RPCs (ValidateAccess / ValidateAction) through the interceptor chain" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownerService> "rbac (rbac.RbacService)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "explicit deny records" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "resource permissions and ownership records" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "role bindings and cluster roles" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#AuthorityDomain> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Remediation is the most dangerous mutation surface. The observe/mutate\nsplit (doctor observes, workflow mutates) is the boundary that keeps\nevery observation pass side-effect free." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Remediation execution" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/authority_domains.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "auto-executing hard-blocked actions (ETCD_PUT, ETCD_DELETE, NODE_REMOVE)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "doctor rule executing mutation inside Evaluate — rules are diagnostic-only" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "remediation bypassing the gate (leader + evidence trust + approval token + risk class)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasEvidenceFreshnessWindow> "stale or unverifiable evidence must block autonomous execution — re-resolve the finding from last-known findings before acting" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasTruthLayer> "runtime" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "operators and agents (status, history)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayWrite> "cluster doctor leader (plans, approvals — never direct mutations)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayWrite> "workflow service (run state)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustMutateVia> "StartRemediationWorkflow → workflow actors → node agents — the doctor decides, the workflow coordinates, node agents execute" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#observesVia> "doctor rule Evaluate(snapshot) — findings only, evidence-backed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownerService> "workflow service (workflow.WorkflowService) with cluster-doctor actor callbacks" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "HealDecision / remediation history records" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "remediation plans and approvals" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "remediation workflow runs and step receipts" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#AuthorityDomain> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Installability is a lifecycle fact, not a storage fact. INC-2026-0012\n(skeleton manifests) and INC-2026-0013 (mislabeled pinned bytes) both\ncame from treating storage state as metadata truth." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Repository artifact metadata" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/authority_domains.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/repository/repository_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "direct Scylla writes to publish_state from outside the repository service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "looking in MinIO for packages — packages live in POSIX CAS, Scylla is the index" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "object presence in MinIO or CAS as installability authority — installability comes from lifecycle metadata" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasTruthLayer> "repository" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "cluster doctor (observation only)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "controller (resolve/release pipeline)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "node agent (install path)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayWrite> "repository service via publish workflow" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustMutateVia> "repository typed RPC / publish workflow (transitionArtifactState gated by IsTransitionAllowed)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustReadVia> "repository resolver RPCs (Scylla-first discovery)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownerService> "repository (repository.PackageRepository)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "artifact manifest" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "artifact publish state (publish_state column in Scylla)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "desired build id references (deletion/revocation hard roots)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "release index (release-index.json BOM)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#AuthorityDomain> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Runtime evidence is layer 3/4 observation. It informs findings and\nconvergence but owns no desired truth; freshness and scope are part of\nevery assertion's meaning." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Runtime evidence" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/authority_domains.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/collector/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/node_agent/node_agent_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "consuming a partial snapshot as if complete — consult snap.Errors first" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "treating missing evidence as evidence of failure (absence has a scope)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsBypass> "treating runtime observation as desired-state authority — installed/running never implies should-be-installed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasEvidenceFreshnessWindow> "evidence must carry source, observed time, and trust level; stale evidence degrades to hints, never to PASS or FAIL verdicts" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasTruthLayer> "runtime" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "cluster doctor (cross-layer findings)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayRead> "controller (convergence decisions)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#mayWrite> "node agent (its own node's observations only)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#observesVia> "doctor collector snapshots (with snap.Errors completeness markers)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#observesVia> "node-agent heartbeat (Phase 1 local + Phase 2 etcd, lean)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownerService> "observed component (node agent inventory, systemd, process probes) — evidence carries no desired-state authority" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "installed-package observations (/globular/nodes/*/packages/*)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "node heartbeat and status" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#ownsState> "runtime health probes and process fingerprints" .
