<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.etcd.key_authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Etcd is cluster authority for desired state and topology. Awareness must know which keys carry which meaning. Empty etcd does not automatically mean the local runtime is invalid." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.etcd.key_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/authority_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.etcd.key_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "authority" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.gateway.xds_readiness> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.gateway.xds_readiness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Gateway readiness must not be based only on the gateway process being up. It must include xDS application proof and route endpoint health. A running Envoy with a broken route is not a healthy gateway." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.gateway.xds_readiness> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/service_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.gateway.xds_readiness> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "routing" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.installed_state.cross_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.installed_state.cross_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Installed-state must never be trusted alone. It must be cross-checked against release-index, etcd desired state, systemd unit presence, binary existence, and runtime health." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.installed_state.cross_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/authority_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.installed_state.cross_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "authority" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.local_config.authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.local_config.authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Local config is evidence, not final authority. Config files may drift from release-index, etcd desired state, rendered service config, installed-state, and runtime state. Drift must be classified precisely." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.local_config.authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/authority_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.local_config.authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "authority" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.mcp.reachability_and_trust> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.mcp.reachability_and_trust> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MCP is the agent interface and remote witness endpoint. Reachability alone is not enough — the certificate must chain to the cluster CA. MCP must also have the awareness bundle loaded to produce meaningful structured facts." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.mcp.reachability_and_trust> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/service_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.mcp.reachability_and_trust> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "interface" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.minio.topology_contract> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.minio.topology_contract> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MinIO must not run without an approved ObjectStoreDesiredState contract. Starting MinIO outside the desired pool or without a rendered distributed.conf creates a split-brain objectstore." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.minio.topology_contract> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/service_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.minio.topology_contract> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "topology" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.pki.identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.pki.identity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A node can be reachable but not trusted. PKI is part of Day-1 readiness — missing certificates block MCP trust, gRPC auth, and service mesh participation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.pki.identity> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/authority_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.pki.identity> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "identity" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.release_index.authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.release_index.authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The release-index is the release spine. It pins platform version, build_id, service packages, infra packages, the awareness bundle, and checksums. Divergence from the release-index must be classified precisely." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.release_index.authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/authority_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.release_index.authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "authority" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.repository.artifact_source_authority_matrix> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.repository.artifact_source_authority_matrix> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The repository layout has a declared artifact/source authority matrix. Package identity, package recipes, authored web assets, release assembly, install execution, generated workspaces, staging paths, fallback mirrors, and outputs each have one owner and one role. Mirrors, staging paths, and outputs may support build or install flows, but they are never source authority." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.repository.artifact_source_authority_matrix> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/contracts/authority_contracts.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#contract/contract.repository.artifact_source_authority_matrix> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "authority" .
