<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_artifact_identity_as_installation_proof> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_artifact_identity_as_installation_proof> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Treating 'the entrypoint binary is on disk and its checksum matches the manifest' as sufficient to write status=installed. It looks like a strong proof — it is a cryptographic match against the published artifact — but it establishes ARTIFACT IDENTITY, not transaction completion. Every step that can fail an install (native-dependency validation, port allocation, config write, unit render, receipt stamp) happens AFTER the bytes are unpacked, so a failed install satisfies this check. Equally forbidden: strengthening the same inference with more identity evidence (build_id, package_sha256, unit-file presence). Unit presence in particular is NOT a substitute — on node-4 the unit file was rendered before the failing native-deps check. The only admissible proof is an owner receipt." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_artifact_identity_as_installation_proof> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Accept a matching entrypoint checksum as proof that an install succeeded" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_artifact_identity_as_installation_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/installed_state_requires_successful_owner_install_receipt> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_artifact_identity_as_installation_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_artifact_identity_as_installation_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fnode_agent%2Fnode_agent_server%2Fheartbeat.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_corrupt_lkg> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_corrupt_lkg> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reject LKG files with invalid checksums; log the failure; retain the previous valid state; emit a doctor alert for operator review." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_corrupt_lkg> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Load and apply a LKG file that fails checksum or generation validation rather than rejecting it and retaining the prior valid state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/accept_corrupt_lkg> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
