<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/add_column_only_to_create_table_without_backfill_alter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Ship an idempotent ALTER TABLE ADD for the new column (tolerating \"column already exists\") in the ordered migration statements after the CREATE, and bump the schema version so it re-applies on already-migrated clusters. A manual ALTER on the live cluster is RECOVERY only; the code must carry the backfill so every upgrade path gets the column." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/add_column_only_to_create_table_without_backfill_alter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Add a column to a CREATE TABLE statement (relying on CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) without shipping a matching idempotent ALTER TABLE ADD, or treat a one-off manual ALTER on a single cluster as the permanent fix." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/add_column_only_to_create_table_without_backfill_alter> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/scylla.added_column_requires_backfill_alter_for_upgrades> .
