<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/add_mutating_tool_to_remote_aggregator_allowlist> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Mutating tools require local privilege checks, approval gates, and audit trails. Remote callers via the aggregator bypass all of these. Corrupted distributed state produced by remote mutation has no trace and no recovery path. aggregator_policy.go explicitly documents: \"All entries are read-only local tools that do not mutate state.\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/add_mutating_tool_to_remote_aggregator_allowlist> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Only allowlist read-only tools. Mutating operations must be invoked locally or through typed controller RPCs with RBAC enforcement and audit logging." .
