<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_absolute_paths_when_under_local_root_string_prefix> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_delete_of_virtual_root> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_digest_change_on_republish> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_duplicate_singleton_directives> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_duplicate_singleton_directives> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Run deploy.ValidateSystemdUnit at both template-render init() and\non the rendered output of every GenerateSpec call. Fail spec\ngeneration when duplicates are detected." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_duplicate_singleton_directives> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Generate (or accept) systemd units containing duplicate singleton\ndirectives (Type=, User=, Group=, Restart=, etc.). systemd uses\nlast-wins; the earlier value is silently masked. A previous incident\nshipped a duplicate Type= via this exact failure mode." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_duplicate_singleton_directives> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/systemd.effective_unit_must_match_rendered_unit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_duplicate_singleton_directives> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_file_scheme_in_upload_url> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_human_to_overwrite_seed_to_silence_finding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_human_to_overwrite_seed_to_silence_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Treat the bundle as the authoritative source: re-run the seeder workflow\nto upsert back to the bundle's sha256. Investigate WHY the drift happened\n(misconfigured CLI tool, bypassed RBAC check, manual edit on disk). The\nfinding is the signal, not the problem." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_human_to_overwrite_seed_to_silence_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When the doctor flags ops_knowledge.seed_drift, have a human operator\noverwrite the seed-tagged entry directly so the finding stops firing,\nwithout investigating why ai-memory diverged from the bundle." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_human_to_overwrite_seed_to_silence_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_human_to_overwrite_seed_to_silence_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ops_knowledge.seed_integrity> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_human_to_overwrite_seed_to_silence_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_mcp_to_write_awareness_yaml_files> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_metadata_ip_upload_target> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_node_agent_to_read_other_nodes_plans> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_official_publisher_to_use_dev_channel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_official_publisher_to_use_dev_channel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use publisher=local@<cluster-id> or org@<domain> for any DEV-channel\nartifact. The official publisher is exclusively for STABLE channel releases\nproduced by the official release pipeline." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_official_publisher_to_use_dev_channel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An operator publishes a test build with publisher=core@globular.io\nand channel=DEV to avoid changing the publisher. This pollutes the\nofficial namespace with a non-authoritative build and could be confused\nwith a real official artifact by resolution logic." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_official_publisher_to_use_dev_channel> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.local_publish_requires_local_identity> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_official_publisher_to_use_dev_channel> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_parent_traversal_segments> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_reconcile_tick_to_starve_terminal_commit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_reconcile_tick_to_starve_terminal_commit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use a dedicated completion lane not subject to reconcile-tick acquisition; completion always runs to terminal before new ticks are admitted." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_reconcile_tick_to_starve_terminal_commit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allow a reconcile tick to prevent or delay the terminal commit of an already-running reconcile phase by acquiring shared resources first." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_reconcile_tick_to_starve_terminal_commit> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_reconcile_tick_to_starve_terminal_commit> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/reconcile.global_work_must_not_starve_completion> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_reconcile_tick_to_starve_terminal_commit> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_reverse_artifact_state_transition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allow_wildcard_fallback_when_caller_passed_explicit_version> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/allowing_default_branch_to_silently_return_false_without_canary_log> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_migration_without_idempotency_guard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_topology_drift_without_generation_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_topology_drift_without_generation_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Include the topology generation in every drift plan; validate at execution time that the plan generation still matches the live generation before applying." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_topology_drift_without_generation_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Apply a topology drift action without checking the topology generation, allowing stale drift plans to modify live topology." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_topology_drift_without_generation_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_topology_drift_without_generation_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/topology.reconciler_must_respect_safety_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_topology_drift_without_generation_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_weight_changes_without_human_approval> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_weight_changes_without_human_approval> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use awareness.learn_from_fix to propose weight adjustments. Wait for human\nreview and approval of the proposal. Only then promote the change to\npath_weights.yaml and rebuild the graph." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_weight_changes_without_human_approval> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Directly modify path_weights.yaml without going through the learn_from_fix\nproposal workflow and without human review. Weight changes alter the ranking\nof all decision paths for every future preflight call." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_weight_changes_without_human_approval> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.weight_learning.human_approval_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_weight_changes_without_human_approval> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/apply_weight_changes_without_human_approval> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_accepted_after_evidence_digest_changed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_authorizes_different_action_class_than_minted> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_authorizes_different_target_than_minted> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_ignores_finding_id_binding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_missing_audience_or_expiry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_replayed_after_successful_execution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_replayed_after_successful_execution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Approval is bound to evidence at approval time. The evidence (this JTI has not been used) must survive failover, or the binding is a phantom." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_replayed_after_successful_execution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Persist consumed-JTIs in etcd/ScyllaDB with TTL. Every approval consumer re-checks the persisted store before honoring." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_replayed_after_successful_execution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Accept an approval token a second time after the first execution succeeded" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_replayed_after_successful_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_replayed_after_successful_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_validator_accepts_any_non_empty_string> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_token_validator_skips_signature_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_validity_assumed_durable_across_failover> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_validity_assumed_durable_across_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Approvals carry an evidence digest. The consumer re-derives the digest from current state at consume-time and refuses if it doesn't match." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_validity_assumed_durable_across_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The binding outlives the evidence by default; the consumer must actively re-check or the binding becomes a phantom." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_validity_assumed_durable_across_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assume an approval granted by one leader is still valid after a new leader takes over" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_validity_assumed_durable_across_failover> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approval_validity_assumed_durable_across_failover> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_objectstore_transition_without_operator_consent_record> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_objectstore_transition_without_operator_consent_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always require a fresh admission record. Reject stale or absent approvals. Gate destructive transitions only on unexpired, operator-signed admission records." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_objectstore_transition_without_operator_consent_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Destructive transitions can destroy production data. The admission system in objectstore_admission.go requires explicit operator consent (admitted disk records) before any destructive action. Implicit approval from state observation bypasses this gate and can trigger irreversible data loss." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_objectstore_transition_without_operator_consent_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Proceed with a destructive objectstore topology transition (pool wipe, node removal, standalone→distributed) without a matching operator-signed admission record in etcd." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_objectstore_transition_without_operator_consent_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/objectstore.membership_requires_explicit_desired_state> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_objectstore_transition_without_operator_consent_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_objectstore_transition_without_operator_consent_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_controller%2Fcluster_controller_server%2Fobjectstore_admission.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/approve_transition_then_immediately_revoke_to_clear_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/archive_desired_pinned_artifact_without_safety_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/archive_without_desired_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_cds_progress_implies_lds_progress_because_they_share_an_ads_stream> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_install_path_can_reach_repository_service_for_blob_bytes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_installed_means_running> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_installed_means_running> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "After confirming installed-state in etcd, check systemd unit status via node-agent inventory; treat both as required for a healthy service declaration." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_installed_means_running> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat the presence of an installed-state record in etcd as proof that the corresponding service is currently running and healthy." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_installed_means_running> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_installed_means_running> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/runtime.installed_state_not_liveness> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_installed_means_running> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_migration_already_ran_without_verification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assume_substrate_fix_resolves_workload_failure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assuming_publish_implies_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assuming_publish_implies_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Publishing an artifact does not create desired state. Desired state is written by platform-upgrade via ServicesDesiredSet; verify that DesiredService exists for each node before expecting installation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assuming_publish_implies_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assume that because a service artifact is published (AVAILABLE in the repository), its DesiredService record already exists in etcd and nodes will install it automatically." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/assuming_publish_implies_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
