<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_accept_cross_cluster_local_artifact_as_official> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_accept_cross_cluster_local_artifact_as_official> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cross-cluster sync must preserve publisher and channel fields.\nLocal/dev/hotfix artifacts may only be imported with explicit trust\npolicy or operator approval via `globular pkg override`. They must\nnever silently replace the receiving cluster's official desired state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_accept_cross_cluster_local_artifact_as_official> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "During cross-cluster sync, Cluster B's local build (local@cluster-b,\nstorage@1.2.43+local.cluster-b.1) is imported and the sync logic\npromotes it to official stable to simplify the merge. The receiving\ncluster's official desired state now points to non-official bytes." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_accept_cross_cluster_local_artifact_as_official> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.official_identity_immutable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_accept_cross_cluster_local_artifact_as_official> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.remote_local_artifact_must_not_override_stable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_accept_cross_cluster_local_artifact_as_official> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_clear_escalation_without_operator_approval> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_clear_escalation_without_operator_approval> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Escalation is a safety gate. Auto-clearing on restart resets the cooldown counter and allows the healer loop to auto-dispatch an action that was previously hard-stopped. The escalation must only be cleared by an explicit operator API call." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_clear_escalation_without_operator_approval> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Persist escalation state in etcd. Only clear via an operator-authenticated API call. On leader acquisition, reload escalation state from etcd." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_clear_escalation_without_operator_approval> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Automatically clear the requires_approval escalation flag on a timer or on doctor restart without requiring explicit operator intervention." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_clear_escalation_without_operator_approval> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_clear_escalation_without_operator_approval> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fremediation_gate.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_lower_replication_factor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_lower_replication_factor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Keyspace RF can only increase automatically; any RF decrease requires an explicit operator-approved workflow with quorum impact analysis." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_lower_replication_factor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Automatically lower Scylla keyspace RF below policy when storage nodes decrease. RF must only ever increase automatically, never decrease." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_lower_replication_factor> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_lower_replication_factor> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/scylla.critical_keyspace_replication_policy> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_lower_replication_factor> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_promote_profiles_to_satisfy_quorum_floor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_promote_profiles_to_satisfy_quorum_floor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Treat profiles as controller-owned placement intent set only from explicit requests. Report observed capacity and survivability posture as evidence; never coerce profiles onto nodes to satisfy a global quorum floor. Destructive storage/topology changes still gate on their component-specific safety contracts and operator approval." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_promote_profiles_to_satisfy_quorum_floor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Automatically assign or promote storage (or other) profiles onto the first-N nodes to manufacture a preferred quorum size, turning an abstract preferred quorum into a hidden admission action that mutates controller-owned placement intent without an explicit request." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_promote_profiles_to_satisfy_quorum_floor> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.quorum_is_quality_not_constraint> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_promote_profiles_to_satisfy_quorum_floor> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/profile.intent_is_controller_owned_placement_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_promote_profiles_to_satisfy_quorum_floor> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_remediation_without_cooldown> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_rollback_on_crash> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_rollback_on_crash> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When a service crashes, create an incident and halt convergence for that package.\nNever install a lower version unless the operator explicitly runs a rollback command\nwith Force=true. Auto-rollback masks root causes and can compound incidents." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_rollback_on_crash> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Automatically install an older package version when the current version crashes\nor fails its health check, without explicit operator approval." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_rollback_on_crash> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/auto_rollback_on_crash> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/back_up_format_json_to_minio_itself> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/backfill_causal_chain_without_symptoms> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/backfill_causal_chain_without_symptoms> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Only finalize a causal rule when you have the actual log output from the incident.\nExtract the exact symptom keywords that appeared in logs (trigger_keywords and\nsequence[*].keywords must be literal log fragments, not paraphrases)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/backfill_causal_chain_without_symptoms> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Create a causal_rules.yaml entry retroactively, from memory or logs, without\nthe actual symptom keywords that were observed during the incident. Without\nreal symptom keywords, the rule can never match a future incident's log output." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/backfill_causal_chain_without_symptoms> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.knowledge.causal_rules_evidence_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/backfill_causal_chain_without_symptoms> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/backfill_causal_chain_without_symptoms> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/backfill_release_index_field_after_publish> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/binary_hash_check_skipped_for_known_service> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blame_verification_for_persistence_block> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blind_reconcile_retry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blind_reconcile_retry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Classify the failure using FailureClass before retrying. Transient failures get capped retries with exponential backoff. Deterministic failures (wrong config, version mismatch, disk full) create an incident and halt." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blind_reconcile_retry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Retry the same install action on every reconcile tick without classifying whether the failure is transient or deterministic." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blind_reconcile_retry> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/convergence.no_infinite_retry> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blind_reconcile_retry> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blind_reconcile_retry> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_authority_on_cache_availability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_authority_on_cache_availability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Authority publication runs unconditionally; derived-state failures emit their own alerts but must not block the authority lane." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_authority_on_cache_availability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Refuse to publish authoritative state because a cache, projection, or secondary index is unavailable. Authority must publish regardless of derived-state health." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_authority_on_cache_availability> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/derived_state.must_not_block_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_authority_on_cache_availability> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.critical_path_no_non_critical_dependency> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_authority_on_cache_availability> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_controller_loop_on_external_query> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_controller_loop_on_external_query> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Run external queries in a goroutine with select on timeout; return a timeout error to the reconcile loop immediately if the deadline is exceeded." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_controller_loop_on_external_query> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allow a slow or unresponsive external backend (Scylla, DNS, etcd) to block the main controller reconcile loop indefinitely without a timeout gate." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_controller_loop_on_external_query> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_queries.must_be_bounded> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_controller_loop_on_external_query> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.critical_path_no_non_critical_dependency> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_controller_loop_on_external_query> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_join_or_rollout_on_global_storage_count_floor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_join_or_rollout_on_global_storage_count_floor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Allow join, rollout, and profile assignment to proceed while reporting capacity and survivability as risk posture. Gate ONLY component-specific DESTRUCTIVE storage operations behind explicit safety checks and operator approval; that is data-safety gating, not a global quorum admission floor." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_join_or_rollout_on_global_storage_count_floor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Refuse node join, Day-1 workload rollout, profile assignment, or non-destructive convergence solely because the observed storage-node count is below a preferred or global floor — reusing a capacity/quorum report field as an enforcement predicate." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_join_or_rollout_on_global_storage_count_floor> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.quorum_is_quality_not_constraint> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_join_or_rollout_on_global_storage_count_floor> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/quorum_safety_before_storage_mutation> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_join_or_rollout_on_global_storage_count_floor> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/block_workflow_server_startup_on_missing_day0_log> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/blocked_operations_list_quietly_emptied> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/boolean_completeness_flag_without_source_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/boolean_completeness_flag_without_source_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "`InventoryComplete` must be set true only when every source returned without error AND the source-time is fresher than the completeness TTL. Surface per-source errors in `InventoryErrors []SourceError` so the consumer can detect partial inventory." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/boolean_completeness_flag_without_source_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "`InventoryComplete = len(x) > 0` or other heuristic proxies stand in for \"enumeration succeeded\". A systemd query failure that yields zero units flips the flag false; a stale cache that yields stale units flips it true. No source-time, no source-confidence marker." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/boolean_completeness_flag_without_source_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/infra.heartbeat_observer_only_not_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/boolean_completeness_flag_without_source_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.absence_scope_must_be_explicit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/boolean_completeness_flag_without_source_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/boolean_completeness_flag_without_source_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bootstrap_flag_persists_without_clearing_path> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bootstrap_flag_persists_without_clearing_path> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Pair every bootstrap flag with either (a) a typed RPC that clears it on phase transition with audit trail, OR (b) a level-triggered sweep that verifies the flag is still appropriate." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bootstrap_flag_persists_without_clearing_path> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The marker outlives its phase by default. Without an explicit clearing path or freshness check, the relaxed semantics leak forever." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bootstrap_flag_persists_without_clearing_path> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Set a bootstrap.enabled flag with no actor responsible for clearing it" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bootstrap_flag_persists_without_clearing_path> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bootstrap_flag_persists_without_clearing_path> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.write_creates_completion_obligation> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bootstrap_flag_persists_without_clearing_path> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/build_id_mismatch_demoted_to_warning> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bulk_applying_bom_without_installed_state_gate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bump_immutable_timestamp_on_observe> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bump_immutable_timestamp_on_observe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An anchor timestamp identifies WHEN the underlying material was written. Observing or refreshing the record does not change the material; bumping the anchor lies about that. The verifier reads max(InstalledUnix, UpdatedUnix) against the running PID's start mtime to detect \"the apply happened but the restart didn't take\"; a wall-clock-now value is always > PID start, so every correctly-running self-hosted service starts failing service.old_pid_after_upgrade.\nLive regression: heartbeat.go Phase 2 stomped the proof writer's PID-anchored UpdatedUnix every 30s. Fixed in v1.2.164." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bump_immutable_timestamp_on_observe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Preserve existing.UpdatedUnix on observe-only operations. Only bump when the record's underlying material actually changed (different version, different build_id, different checksum). For self-hosted services on the allowlist, the proof writer is the authority on these fields; downstream observers must preserve the proof writer's anchor. Observe-only operations should not write to anchor fields at all." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bump_immutable_timestamp_on_observe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "On every observation (heartbeat tick, status read, snapshot pass) bump an InstalledUnix / UpdatedUnix / similar anchor field to time.Now() because \"we touched the record\". Or: on every routine refresh of a record, set the timestamp to now regardless of whether the underlying material changed." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bump_immutable_timestamp_on_observe> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.has_single_canonical_source_and_is_immutable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bump_immutable_timestamp_on_observe> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
