<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_cycle_with_direct_storage_write> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_cycle_with_direct_storage_write> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "If the owning service is broken, fix the service first (via the layer-appropriate hot-deploy alternative above). If the typed repair RPC does not exist, add it with explicit precondition gates before reaching for `etcdctl put`. Document the gates in code and require the operator to read the gate output before approving." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_cycle_with_direct_storage_write> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Break a circular dependency by writing directly to etcd / ScyllaDB / MinIO as the operator instead of calling the owning service's typed repair RPC. The write bypasses the owner's canonicalization, watch invalidation, and preconditions; cluster_doctor sees the inconsistency as drift; the next reconcile clobbers the write." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_cycle_with_direct_storage_write> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.truth_read_via_owner_rpc_not_direct_storage> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_cycle_with_direct_storage_write> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.circular_dependency_must_have_break_glass> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_cycle_with_direct_storage_write> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_cycle_with_direct_storage_write> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_dep_block_dispatch_gate_to_unstall_a_specific_node> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Query cluster-doctor via ListFindings, ExplainFinding, or GetHealthReport, and render or react to the response. If the doctor lacks a rule for the case at hand, add the rule to cluster_doctor_server/rules/ — do not implement the rule elsewhere.\nSingle-layer queries are NOT bypasses and remain in their owner: \"does this artifact exist?\" answered by repository; \"is X installed on node N?\" answered by node-agent; \"am I up?\" (local readiness) answered by the service itself (systemd Type=notify, gRPC health endpoint). The doctor enters when the question crosses layers or nodes." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cluster-doctor is the canonical answerer for cross-layer health (invariant:cluster_doctor.is_the_authority_for_health_state_queries). Parallel implementations drift over time as the underlying rules evolve (the doctor gets the rule update; the parallel implementation does not); disagree under partial-data conditions (different fallbacks); and hide bugs (when two answers diverge, operators don't know which is right). A single authority for the cross-layer verdict is the only way to keep findings consistent across the cluster's surfaces." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compute a cross-layer health verdict outside cluster-doctor. Examples: a controller routine that classifies \"this release is degraded because L3 says installed but L4 says inactive\" inline instead of consuming a doctor Finding; a CLI command that pulls L1+L2+L3 data and renders a verdict locally; an ai-watcher rule that decides cluster-wide health state from raw layer reads." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster_doctor.is_the_authority_for_health_state_queries> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster_doctor.observer_only_never_writes_etcd> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fai_executor%2F> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fai_watcher%2F> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_controller%2Fcluster_controller_server%2Frelease_pipeline.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_controller%2Fcluster_controller_server%2Frelease_runtime_convergence.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Frules%2F> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fglobularcli%2F> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_doctor_for_cross_layer_health_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fmcp%2F> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_file_service_for_files_under_a_safelist_of_paths> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_filter_public_ips_in_a_specific_provider_for_testing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_hard_blocked_action_blocklist> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_hard_blocked_action_blocklist> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Surface these as operator recommendations only. The operator executes them via CLI after reviewing the rationale. Never add them to the auto-dispatch list." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_hard_blocked_action_blocklist> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "These three action types affect global cluster state irreversibly. No amount of evidence trust, operator approval, or cooldown logic makes autonomous execution of etcd writes or node removal safe — the blast radius is too large and the actions cannot be undone by the doctor itself. They must remain permanently blocked from auto-execution." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_hard_blocked_action_blocklist> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Remove or bypass the hard-blocked action type list (ETCD_PUT, ETCD_DELETE, NODE_REMOVE) to allow autonomous remediation of these action types." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_hard_blocked_action_blocklist> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_hard_blocked_action_blocklist> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Ffailure_policy.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_hard_blocked_action_blocklist> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fremediation_gate.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_registry_digest_binding_for_embedded_catalog> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_registry_digest_binding_for_embedded_catalog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always validate the embedded catalog's manifest digest against packages/registry.yaml via scripts/validate-package-authority.py before trusting it; reject missing or stale manifests rather than proceeding." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_registry_digest_binding_for_embedded_catalog> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Load or trust the embedded packagecatalog mirror without validating its manifest digest against packages/registry.yaml, silently accepting a stale or drifted mirror as if it were current." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_registry_digest_binding_for_embedded_catalog> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repo.installer_embedded_assets_are_generated_mirrors_only> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_registry_digest_binding_for_embedded_catalog> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_repository_authority_with_runtime_observation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_safety_check_with_unconditional_force_true> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_scope_gate_for_bootstrap_convenience> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Dial through globular_client wrappers (which attach clientInterceptor automatically), or attach a UnaryClientInterceptor + StreamClientInterceptor at dial time that read cluster_id from security.GetLocalClusterID() and inject it via metadata.AppendToOutgoingContext when missing. cluster_doctor's dialOptionsForInternalService is the canonical local pattern for the second form." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Server-side interceptors enforce a cluster_id outgoing-metadata header after Day-0 initialization. A dial that lacks the injecting interceptor produces calls that the server rejects with rpc error: code = Unauthenticated desc = \"cluster_id required after cluster initialization\". The failure is silent until something downstream of the call surfaces it — e.g. the doctor's collector starves of repository evidence and the resulting drift goes unsurfaced, or the controller's circuit breaker opens on the cascading failures. The bug was the cluster_doctor dialing repository, ai-memory, and awareness-graph this way; collector had a `if c.clusterID != \"\"` guard that silently skipped when the propagation path didn't populate the field." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Construct an internal-service gRPC client with raw grpc.NewClient / grpc.Dial and only WithTransportCredentials, without attaching a UnaryClientInterceptor that injects cluster_id metadata." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/grpc.backbone.contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fserver.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/bypass_shared_client_for_internal_dials> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fglobular_client%2FClientInterceptors.go> .
