<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_desired_version_or_build_id_by_hand_to_clear_error> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_desired_version_or_build_id_by_hand_to_clear_error> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Repair repository metadata/build_id mapping and let controller reconcile desired state from authoritative records; never hand-edit desired build identifiers." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_desired_version_or_build_id_by_hand_to_clear_error> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manually editing desired version/build_id in etcd to hide an orphaned desired build_id mismatch instead of repairing repository identity and desired-resolution links." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_desired_version_or_build_id_by_hand_to_clear_error> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.desired_build_id_must_resolve> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_desired_version_or_build_id_by_hand_to_clear_error> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_mcp_port_as_workaround> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_mcp_port_as_workaround> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kill the orphan with an ExecStartPre pkill guard and keep port 10260 as the canonical MCP port. Port changes invalidate all existing client configurations and etcd service records." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_mcp_port_as_workaround> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Change the MCP server's listen port from 10260 to a different port to avoid the orphan-held port conflict, leaving the orphaned process alive and the original port occupied." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_mcp_port_as_workaround> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.identity_computation_must_be_invariant> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_mcp_port_as_workaround> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/runtime.installed_state_not_liveness> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_mcp_port_as_workaround> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_official_digest_to_accept_local_build> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_official_digest_to_accept_local_build> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use a local identity lane: publish with publisher=local@<cluster-id>,\nchannel=DEV, version=1.2.43+local.<cluster>.1. The official artifact\nremains unchanged. After validation, promote through the official\nrelease pipeline with a new version." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_official_digest_to_accept_local_build> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A local build fails the official namespace seal because its digest\ndiffers from the published artifact. Fix attempt: update the stored\ndigest in the ledger to match the incoming local bytes.\nThis destroys official immutability and lets any cluster silently\ncorrupt the official stable identity without detection." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_official_digest_to_accept_local_build> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.official_identity_immutable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/change_official_digest_to_accept_local_build> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
