<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_bypasses_parent_authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_duplicates_existing_capability> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_hides_degraded_or_unknown_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_inverts_parent_direction> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_makes_remediation_unbounded> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_replaces_source_of_truth> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_skips_audit_or_operator_approval> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_turns_convenience_into_authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/child_intent_turns_observation_into_mutation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ci_self_stamps_version_bypassing_repository> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ci_self_stamps_version_bypassing_repository> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CI calls the repository to allocate the release version (release capability); the repository validates monotonicity and records identity + build_id." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ci_self_stamps_version_bypassing_repository> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "If CI stamps the version from the git tag and uploads without the repository allocating/validating it, the repository is no longer the single source of truth and monotonicity is not centrally enforced." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ci_self_stamps_version_bypassing_repository> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not let CI self-stamp the version and bypass repository allocation" .
