<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_bulk_apply_state_via_direct_etcd_writes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Multi-step mutations across failure boundaries need durable coordination, not inline execution." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_bulk_apply_state_via_direct_etcd_writes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The CLI computes a workflow request and dispatches it to the workflow service. The workflow persists the intent BEFORE executing any side effect. INC: platform_upgrade_bypassed_workflow_authority." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_bulk_apply_state_via_direct_etcd_writes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CLI command bulk-applies state changes by writing etcd keys directly" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_bulk_apply_state_via_direct_etcd_writes> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_bulk_apply_state_via_direct_etcd_writes> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_bulk_apply_state_via_direct_etcd_writes> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_writes_cross_kind_desired_record> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_writes_cross_kind_desired_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The service CLI hard-refuses non-SERVICE kinds; infrastructure uses its first-class typed desired path. The desired store rejects cross-kind writes." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_writes_cross_kind_desired_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "kind is identity. `globular services desired set --force` writing a SERVICE ServiceDesiredVersion for an INFRASTRUCTURE package produces a permanent kind-mismatch dispatch block. Bypassing the kind check to make the write succeed is the \"relax the identity check\" anti-pattern." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_writes_cross_kind_desired_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not write a desired record of the wrong kind (no --force kind bypass)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_writes_cross_kind_desired_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/desired.keyed_by_kind_and_name> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_writes_cross_kind_desired_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.identity_tuple_must_be_unique> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cli_writes_cross_kind_desired_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/clients_must_not_permanently_bypass_gateway_for_cohosted_services> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/clients_must_not_permanently_bypass_gateway_for_cohosted_services> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Direct-port access is diagnostic / degraded-mode evidence only — never the permanent path. Repair the gateway route: declare the hosted service in registration metadata (HostedServices) and have xDS emit a route per hosted name to the backend cluster, then redeploy both the service and the xDS/gateway so the route table regenerates." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/clients_must_not_permanently_bypass_gateway_for_cohosted_services> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fix missing hosted-service routing by teaching clients, MCP tools, or agents to permanently use direct backend ports instead of the gateway for a co-hosted gRPC service whose gateway route is absent." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/clients_must_not_permanently_bypass_gateway_for_cohosted_services> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/gateway.cohosted_grpc_services_must_be_declared> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/clients_must_not_permanently_bypass_gateway_for_cohosted_services> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster.teardown.do_not_treat_probe_failure_as_empty_ring> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster.teardown.do_not_treat_probe_failure_as_empty_ring> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "count_scylla_up_nodes returns an UNKNOWN sentinel on an unreachable probe; the caller fails closed (die with operator guidance) unless --last-node is explicitly passed; a confirmed count of exactly 1 (probe succeeded, one live member) is the only path that legitimately skips decommission. Corroborate with controller/etcd/peer signals when available." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster.teardown.do_not_treat_probe_failure_as_empty_ring> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Piping a failed/empty `nodetool status` (or any ring-membership probe) through `|| echo 0` / `|| true -> 0` and feeding it into a branch that SKIPS the safe teardown step (decommission) and proceeds to hard-stop Scylla. Also forbidden: letting --force (suppress interactive prompts) imply the single-node / last-node data-safety assertion. Unknown is not zero; interactivity is not data-safety." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster.teardown.do_not_treat_probe_failure_as_empty_ring> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster.teardown.membership_must_be_confirmed_before_destructive_stop> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster.teardown.do_not_treat_probe_failure_as_empty_ring> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster.teardown.do_not_treat_probe_failure_as_empty_ring> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Build a typed RemediationAction (SYSTEMCTL_*, FILE_DELETE, REINSTALL_PACKAGE, etc.) and dispatch it via the existing ActionExecutor. The action flows controller → workflow → node-agent; node-agent is the L3 writer. cluster-doctor records the action's outcome in its own audit ring (in-memory + ai-memory for history) — never in the L3 record itself.\nIn-memory caches of findings (lastFindings, lastEmittedFindings) and ai-memory writes of finding history are NOT etcd writes and are explicitly allowed." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cluster-doctor is observer-only on the four truth layers (invariant:cluster_doctor.observer_only_never_writes_etcd). Adding an etcd writer to cluster-doctor:\n  1. Makes L3 multi-writer (cluster-doctor + node-agent), reintroducing\n     the cross-layer drift class.\n  2. Bypasses the workflow service's audit chain — the mutation has no\n     correlation_id, no trigger_reason, no acknowledged_by, and no\n     rollback target.\n  3. Erodes the security boundary that keeps analytical services from\n     needing node-side privileges." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Add an etcd write (etcd.Put / kv.Put / installed_state.Write* / desired-state.Write*) anywhere under golang/cluster_doctor/. Includes \"convenience\" writes such as caching a Finding to etcd for inter-doctor sharing, or stamping a remediation outcome directly into an L3 InstalledPackage record." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster_doctor.observer_only_never_writes_etcd> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.layer_has_single_writing_actor> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Factor_service.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fcollector%2Fcollector.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fhandler_remediation.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fhealer_loop.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cluster_doctor_direct_write_to_etcd> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fserver.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/collapse_missing_expected_checksum_into_verified_success> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/collapse_source_absent_into_critical_missing_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/collapse_source_absent_into_critical_missing_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use the typed sourceroot.Resolve primitive. Distinguish four states\n— Found / Absent / Inaccessible / WrongContext — and only count\n\"Found + scanned + zero matches\" as critical-missing-evidence.\nAbsent / Inaccessible / WrongContext are info-severity telemetry\nsignals: surface them as \"telemetry unavailable, set\nawareness.repo_path or run on a host with source,\" never as\ncritical findings about the codebase." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/collapse_source_absent_into_critical_missing_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat \"no source tree available to scan\" — whether the cause is an\nempty repoRoot, a missing bundle, an EPERM on a runtime dir, or a\nnon-git cwd — as if it were a critical-severity missing-evidence\nfinding (e.g. REQUIRED_TEST_MISSING, \"0 Go files indexed critical\",\n\"N gaps have missing tests\"). It conflates \"we couldn't check\" with\n\"we checked and found nothing,\" and produces a wall of false alarms\nevery time awareness runs on a host without source — which is every\nproduction MCP host. Three separate incidents in 2026-05 (62 fake\nmissing tests, 39 fake missing fix_case tests, 0% coverage critical)\nall come from this shape." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/collapse_source_absent_into_critical_missing_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.source_scan_requires_verified_repo_root> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/collapse_source_absent_into_critical_missing_evidence> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_compiled_binary_as_source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_compiled_binary_as_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Build into an ignored output path; never git add a binary. git rm --cached any that slipped in and add a .gitignore rule. `make check-no-tracked-binaries` (libmagic content detection) fails the build if any tracked file is a compiled binary." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_compiled_binary_as_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "git add a compiled binary (ELF / Mach-O / Windows PE / object / archive) into the repo — e.g. a `go build` output like golang/node_agent_server_new. Binaries are platform-specific, bloat history, and are never source." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_compiled_binary_as_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/build.no_compiled_binaries_tracked_in_git> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_compiled_binary_as_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_generated_protobuf_outside_canonical_pb_dir> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_generated_protobuf_outside_canonical_pb_dir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Run generateCode.sh from its intended directory so protoc output lands in the canonical golang/<service>/<name>pb/ package. Diff any stray against the canonical copy (canonical is usually the superset) and delete strays. `make check-no-misplaced-pb` fails the build if any *.pb.go is outside a *pb/ dir." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_generated_protobuf_outside_canonical_pb_dir> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Generate or copy *.pb.go anywhere other than golang/<service>/<name>pb/ — e.g. running protoc / generateCode.sh from the repo root and leaving a root-level cluster_controller.pb.go. The strays declare the pb package but sit where no Go package exists, cannot compile, and shadow the authoritative copies." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_generated_protobuf_outside_canonical_pb_dir> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/build.generated_protobuf_only_in_canonical_pb_dir> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_generated_protobuf_outside_canonical_pb_dir> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.generated_artifacts_must_be_fresh_before_merge> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/commit_generated_protobuf_outside_canonical_pb_dir> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_cached_blob_against_installed_manifest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_cached_blob_against_installed_manifest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Content-address staging by digest/build_id and verify the staged blob against the DESIRED artifact's manifest." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_cached_blob_against_installed_manifest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The node-agent's cache-digest check compares the staged blob (the DESIRED artifact) against the INSTALLED artifact's manifest, producing a permanent false cache_digest_mismatch when desired != installed. Compounded by the identity-erasing latest.artifact filename." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_cached_blob_against_installed_manifest> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not verify a staged blob against the installed manifest" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_cached_blob_against_installed_manifest> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/staging.content_addressed> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_cached_blob_against_installed_manifest> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_version_string_for_convergence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_version_string_for_convergence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Compare build_id. Surface \"node ahead of desired (desired regressed)\" as a distinct finding from \"node behind desired (needs upgrade)\"." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_version_string_for_convergence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The version string is display identity. Comparing it for convergence cannot distinguish a desired-version regression from a legitimate pending upgrade, and turns a regressed desired into permanent unconvergeable drift." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compare_version_string_for_convergence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not decide convergence by comparing the version string" .
