<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/compute_hash_only_at_controller> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/concurrent_restart_on_start_limit_hit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Split the field. If the field today holds either kind A or kind B, rename it to FieldA and add FieldB as a separate field. Each is unambiguous. Every writer produces the kind matching the field name. Readers don't sniff; they read the field they need. Where a proto already declares the semantic (e.g. InstalledPackage.Checksum has the comment \"SHA256 of installed archive\"), the fix is to make every writer respect that semantic and remove the wrong-kind writes at the writer site, not at the reader." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The field's declared semantic is the contract. Different identities are different fields. Conditional interpretation is the bug, not a fix:\n  - it propagates: every new writer/reader needs to know the\n    conditional rules;\n  - it drifts: rules don't get updated in lock-step across services;\n  - it hides bugs: when the kind detection misclassifies a value,\n    the wrong code path runs silently.\nAll three observed today (5804f523 vs 2eb07b67, NodeReleaseStatus. InstalledHash, UpdatedUnix proof-anchor stomp) were the same shape." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Argue that a storage field can carry one of several semantics depending on which writer set it (\"for cluster-controller it's the release-identity; for backup-manager it's the binary SHA — readers branch on metadata to decide\"). Or: argue that a reader should sniff the value to guess its kind." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.field_semantic_is_single_writer_defined> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.has_single_canonical_source_and_is_immutable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/install_package.hash_schemas_must_not_alias> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/conditional_field_semantic_by_writer> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.identity_computation_must_be_invariant> .
