<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/confuse_k8s_etcd_with_globular_etcd> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/consume_generated_workspace_as_release_authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/continue_writing_after_lease_expiry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.kill_to_clear_lease_contention> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.kill_to_clear_lease_contention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wait for etcd to stabilize; the lease expires after its TTL without requiring process kills; only restart controllers after etcd is fully healthy." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.kill_to_clear_lease_contention> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Killing controller processes does not clear lease contention — the killed process\nheld the lease, and killing it without etcd being healthy means the lease expires\nand all remaining controllers immediately attempt re-election, adding more write\npressure. Only etcd stability resolves lease contention." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.kill_to_clear_lease_contention> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.kill_to_clear_lease_contention> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.restart_before_etcd_stable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.restart_before_etcd_stable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wait for all etcd members to return to quorum and a leader to be elected before restarting controller processes; premature restart amplifies write pressure." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.restart_before_etcd_stable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Restarting controller processes while etcd is in NOSPACE or leader-instability state\ncauses each restarted instance to immediately attempt to write a new leader lease to\netcd. These writes all fail (NOSPACE) or contend during re-election, amplifying the\nload on an already-stressed etcd cluster and delaying recovery." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.restart_before_etcd_stable> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.restart_before_etcd_stable> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.silence_drift_by_adding_profile_or_suppressing_rule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.silence_drift_by_adding_profile_or_suppressing_rule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Scope the DESIRED hash to the node's authorized subset in filterVersionsForNode via the existing placement law book (isOrphanedInstall / placementAllows) — catalog-unknown services kept. Unauthorized-but-installed packages surface via placement.installed_package_orphaned, never generic drift." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.silence_drift_by_adding_profile_or_suppressing_rule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "\"Fixing\" perpetual cluster.services.drift on a capability-restricted node by adding a media-server/ai profile to the node just to make the all-profile desired hash match (grants unintended placement authority and corrupts desired state), by suppressing the cluster.services.drift rule globally or special-casing node IDs, or by loosening the drift rule to ignore mismatches whenever applied is a subset of desired." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.silence_drift_by_adding_profile_or_suppressing_rule> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/controller.desired_services_hash_must_be_profile_scoped> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.silence_drift_by_adding_profile_or_suppressing_rule> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/doctor.layout_drift_must_reflect_real_risk> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.silence_drift_by_adding_profile_or_suppressing_rule> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.absence_scope_must_be_explicit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller.silence_drift_by_adding_profile_or_suppressing_rule> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/controller_inline_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/converge_on_inventory_alone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/converge_on_inventory_alone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The controller must obtain runtime proof (via GetServiceRuntimeProof\nor the verifier's etcd snapshot) for every required node before\nmoving to CONVERGED. Inventory is the convergence target; proof is\nthe convergence evidence." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/converge_on_inventory_alone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Permit the controller to advance the rollout state machine based on\nInstalledPackage records without independent runtime evidence." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/converge_on_inventory_alone> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/rollout.convergence_requires_runtime_proof> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/converge_on_inventory_alone> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/count_unverified_as_tests_not_found> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/count_unverified_as_tests_not_found> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Enumerate every status explicitly. `tests_found`, `tests_partial`,\nand `no_tests_required` are verified. `tests_not_found` is the\nonly real failure. `unverified` is its own info-severity signal.\n`invalid_metadata` is a playbook-quality issue, not a missing\ntest. The `default` branch should panic on an unknown status so\na future addition to the status enum forces a conscious choice." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/count_unverified_as_tests_not_found> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "In a switch over verification status, let the `default` branch\ncapture both genuinely-missing tests AND\n\"couldn't-check\"/\"unverified\"/\"no-tests-required\" entries, so all\nof them get reported under one bucket. The operator sees \"N gaps\nhave missing tests\" when the actual condition is \"we have no repo\nsource to scan.\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/count_unverified_as_tests_not_found> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.source_scan_requires_verified_repo_root> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/count_unverified_as_tests_not_found> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/create_new_runtime_dir_under_legacy_alias_name> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/create_parallel_release_records_for_same_id_under_different_kinds> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/create_parallel_release_records_for_same_id_under_different_kinds> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Route desired writes through routeInfrastructureDesired; prune cross-kind records (pruneCrossKindServiceReleases / deleteCrossKindServiceRelease) with the component catalog as oracle; block stale converged persistence (isStaleResolvedGhost). One id → one kind." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/create_parallel_release_records_for_same_id_under_different_kinds> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allow the same canonical package id to hold release/desired records under two kinds (e.g. a ServiceRelease and an InfrastructureRelease for xds), creating competing keyspaces and ghost desired state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/create_parallel_release_records_for_same_id_under_different_kinds> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/desired.keyed_by_kind_and_name> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/create_parallel_release_records_for_same_id_under_different_kinds> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.kind_is_registry_authored_downstream_is_projection> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/create_parallel_release_records_for_same_id_under_different_kinds> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_instance_coupling_via_single_workflow_run> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Call the owner's typed RPC. The owner is named in docs/awareness/etcd_path_ownership.yaml (Commit B). When a CLI or admin tool needs to mutate state, route the change through the same RPC the workflow service would call. When a service has an internal split between sub-actors (e.g. node-agent's heartbeat observer vs proof writer authority), the authority sub-actor is the only writer; the observer reads and reports." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Each truth layer has exactly one writing actor. Cross-layer writes produce the exact bug class observed 2026-06-04: release-identity hashes leaking into binary-SHA fields (5804f523 vs 2eb07b67), heartbeat stomping the proof writer's PID anchor, and MinIO mirror writes legitimizing themselves as a recovery source. These bugs all look different at the surface but share one shape — module M wrote to a path M doesn't own. The fix is structural, not local." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Write to an etcd path whose owner (per etcd_path_ownership and the actor_layer_mapping) is a different service. Typical shapes: cluster-controller writing into /globular/nodes/{id}/packages/ (L3, owned by per-node node-agent); a CLI tool calling etcd.Put directly against a controller-owned prefix instead of calling the controller's typed RPC; a heartbeat sub-actor stomping a field set by another sub-actor inside the same service." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/etcd.path_has_single_owner> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.actor_layer_mapping> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.layer_has_single_writing_actor> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/cross_layer_write_by_non_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
