<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_build_id_to_make_purge_succeed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_build_id_to_silence_install_storm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_build_id_to_silence_install_storm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Repair the repository: run `globular repository repair-index\n--from-all --dry-run` to identify reconstructable manifests; if\na manifest is genuinely lost, roll desired forward to a build_id\nthat exists (`globular services desired set <name> <new_version>`).\nDesired-state edits are valid as forward rolls — never as silent\ndeletions to hide repository corruption." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_build_id_to_silence_install_storm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When the controller install-storms against a build_id that the\nrepository can no longer resolve (\"build_id X not found for\nname=Y\"), the operator deletes the ServiceDesiredVersion /\nInfrastructureRelease row pinning build_id X to \"clear the error\".\nThe install loop stops, but desired state is now inconsistent\nwith the BOM and the orphaning continues silently — every later\ncluster operation reads desired state and sees the wrong version." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_build_id_to_silence_install_storm> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.desired_build_id_must_resolve> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_build_id_to_silence_install_storm> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.purge_must_not_delete_active_desired_builds> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_build_id_to_silence_install_storm> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_state_without_approval_marker> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_state_without_approval_marker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Create the delete-approval marker at the correct path before deletion; validate its generation and leader identity before committing the delete operation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_state_without_approval_marker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Delete a critical desired-state key from etcd without first creating the delete-approval marker at /globular/<domain>/delete_approval/<generation>." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_state_without_approval_marker> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_state.deletion_requires_audited_intent> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_desired_state_without_approval_marker> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
