<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_runtime_on_timeout> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "On etcd read timeout, retain current runtime state; set status=degraded; retry at the next tick after the configured timeout window." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_runtime_on_timeout> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Interpret an etcd read timeout as a stop or delete intent and halt the runtime service. Timeout must be treated as a temporary authority unavailability, not a destructive command." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/delete_runtime_on_timeout> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_state.absence_is_not_destructive_intent> .
