<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_reports_service_down_from_gateway_path_alone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_reports_service_down_from_gateway_path_alone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cross-check the direct backend before any down verdict. If the gateway answers a non-gRPC content-type (text/html) while the backend is healthy, report the gateway route/filter-chain as suspected and keep the service marked healthy; if the backend cannot be cross-checked, report indeterminate (CHECK_ERROR), not down. Fix the Envoy route/filter-chain; never make a direct-port bypass the permanent path." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_reports_service_down_from_gateway_path_alone> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Conclude that a service is down from a failed gateway-path probe alone, without cross-checking the direct backend port — or \"resolve\" a broken gateway route by permanently pointing clients at direct backend ports." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_reports_service_down_from_gateway_path_alone> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster_doctor.degraded_mode_must_not_depend_on_diagnosed_path> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_reports_service_down_from_gateway_path_alone> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_reports_service_down_from_gateway_path_alone> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_trusts_node_agent_apply_success> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_trusts_node_agent_apply_success> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "After dispatch, poll GetServiceRuntimeProof until running_exe_sha256\nmatches expected_sha256 (or a timeout). Apply success without proof\nis INSTALLED_CLAIMED, not RUNTIME_VERIFIED." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_trusts_node_agent_apply_success> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat a successful ApplyPackageRelease response as proof that the\nservice is running the new build. The success response is a CLAIM\nrecorded by the apply path, not independent runtime evidence." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/doctor_trusts_node_agent_apply_success> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/doctor.must_compare_claims_to_proofs> .
