<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/escalation_state_kept_in_memory_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Persist escalation state in etcd/ScyllaDB with TTL. Reload on startup. Workflow defer B3's durable counter is the pattern." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/escalation_state_kept_in_memory_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The contraction (escalate to approval) must survive what triggered it — including the restart that often follows a cascade." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/escalation_state_kept_in_memory_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Track escalation counter in process memory only" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/escalation_state_kept_in_memory_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/escalation_state_kept_in_memory_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/escalation_state_kept_in_memory_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.disarm_before_compact> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.disarm_before_compact> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always run in this safe order:\n  1. etcdctl compact <rev>          — compact revision history\n  2. etcdctl defrag --endpoints=<all> — defragment all members\n  3. Verify disk usage dropped below quota (df -h or du)\n  4. etcdctl alarm disarm           — only after disk is confirmed below quota" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.disarm_before_compact> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Run etcdctl alarm disarm before the etcd disk is actually below quota — specifically,\nbefore compact + defrag + verified disk size reduction have all completed." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.disarm_before_compact> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.disarm_before_compact> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.restart_nodes_without_nospace_fix> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.restart_nodes_without_nospace_fix> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Resolve disk pressure first (compact + defrag + verify quota below threshold); only restart etcd nodes after disk usage is confirmed below quota." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.restart_nodes_without_nospace_fix> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Restarting etcd nodes when NOSPACE is active does not help. The restarted node\nrejoins the cluster but immediately encounters the same alarm condition and cannot\ncommit writes. Leader election continues to fail. Resolve the disk pressure first." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.restart_nodes_without_nospace_fix> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd.restart_nodes_without_nospace_fix> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/etcd_nospace_by_deleting_random_keys> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/evidence_used_without_timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/evidence_used_without_writer_identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/exception_5_claimed_at_file_granularity_for_multi_step_function> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/execute_remediation_on_follower_instance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/execute_remediation_on_follower_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Followers return gRPC UNAVAILABLE (\"not leader\") for all remediation RPCs. Callers must redirect to the current leader. Leadership is re-checked on every call, never cached." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/execute_remediation_on_follower_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Followers serve stale/cached data and cannot safely authorize remediations. Allowing followers to execute creates split-brain remediation races where two instances attempt to heal the same component, amplifying the failure." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/execute_remediation_on_follower_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allow a cluster-doctor follower instance to execute or authorize remediation actions when the leader is unavailable or slow to respond." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/execute_remediation_on_follower_instance> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/execute_remediation_on_follower_instance> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fhandler_remediation.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/execute_remediation_on_follower_instance> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fleader_election.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/exit_0_on_missing_mandatory_tests> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/expected_sha256_by_binary_bridge_for_stale_workflow> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Before writing any code in a high-risk area, query the awareness graph for the relevant invariants/intents/forbidden_fixes. Specifically: awareness.briefing on the target file AND awareness.query with class=invariant search terms matching the operation being performed. If the briefing returns empty for a topic that clearly has an architectural rule, broaden the query, briefing on related files, or explicitly state that the rule is not in the graph rather than substituting code-inspection-derived assumptions." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The buggy code is not the contract. The contract is in the awareness graph (invariants, intents, forbidden fixes), in CLAUDE.md, and in the project's architectural documentation. When a fix is being designed, the contract — not the buggy implementation — is what dictates the shape of the fix. Extending the buggy pattern preserves the drift it encodes; in compound systems this drift accumulates faster than it can be repaid.\nLive regression class: v1.2.162's heal-from-mirror sweep was a direct application of this anti-pattern. The assistant read the existing publish path's MinIO mirror writes and concluded \"mirror is the source of truth for recovery\", instead of querying the awareness graph for where packages are supposed to live. The result was a fix that preserved the architectural violation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When fixing a bug in code that uses a pre-existing pattern (e.g. MinIO as mirror, a particular field-name semantic, a routing fallback), extend the pattern in the fix because \"that's how the code currently works\"." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/assistant.query_awareness_before_assuming_architecture> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/CLAUDE.md> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extend_existing_buggy_pattern_without_querying_architecture> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/docs%2Fawareness%2Finvariants.yaml> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/extract_tar_entries_with_absolute_paths_or_traversal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fail_on_corrupt_prior_contract_instead_of_overwriting> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/failure_counter_reset_on_process_restart> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/failure_policy_disappears_when_etcd_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_alternative_action_on_workflow_step_failure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_alternative_action_on_workflow_step_failure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "On transient failure, retry the same step until success or a bounded attempt count is reached. On terminal failure, reach workflow FAILED and surface the failure for human/escalation review. If a genuinely different action is appropriate, that's a different workflow with a different committed intent — not a branch inside the original." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_alternative_action_on_workflow_step_failure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Workflows derive their value from being the single source of truth for what happened. Once committed, the only sanctioned exits are retry-the-same-step or reach-terminal-FAILED. An alternative path breaks the equivalence between intent and effect." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_alternative_action_on_workflow_step_failure> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Branch a workflow step to an alternative action when the canonical action fails" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_alternative_action_on_workflow_step_failure> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_alternative_action_on_workflow_step_failure> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_alternative_action_on_workflow_step_failure> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_cwd_when_git_root_unknown> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_cwd_when_git_root_unknown> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Return `sourceroot.Result{State: Absent}` (or \"\" from the legacy\nhelper). Callers then take the correct branch — UNVERIFIED, not\nMISSING. If you genuinely need a writable working dir for some\nother purpose, use `os.Getwd()` directly at that call site with a\ndifferent verb; do not paint it as \"the repo root.\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_cwd_when_git_root_unknown> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` fails, fall back to\n`os.Getwd()` and return the cwd as if it were the repo root. On a\nproduction MCP host the cwd is the install dir (no source files),\nwhich makes every subsequent scan return zero matches and produce\ncritical-severity REQUIRED_TEST_MISSING / 0% coverage findings." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_cwd_when_git_root_unknown> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.source_scan_requires_verified_repo_root> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_cwd_when_git_root_unknown> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_cwd_when_git_root_unknown> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fall_back_to_profile_when_health_data_arrives_late> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fence_only_at_individual_write_sites_not_interceptor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/fetch_arbitrary_url_from_cluster_network> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/filter_out_vip_in_node_identity_ips> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/filter_out_vip_in_node_identity_ips> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "NodeIdentity.Ips is the canonical full IP list and must not be filtered.\nFix the consumers: replace Ips[0] / PrimaryIP() with StableIP(clusterVIP)\nor nodeAny<X>. The VIP is real and belongs in the identity; the\nselection rule belongs in the caller." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/filter_out_vip_in_node_identity_ips> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mutate node.Identity.Ips to remove the cluster VIP before publishing the\nidentity, so downstream code that reads Ips[0] never sees the VIP.\nDestroys the multi-IP truth (NodeIdentity.Ips is supposed to be the full\nlist) to paper over consumers that picked the wrong helper." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/filter_out_vip_in_node_identity_ips> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/finding_cleared_on_degraded_outcome> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/finding_cleared_on_dispatch_alone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/finding_cleared_on_failed_outcome> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/finding_cleared_on_pending_outcome> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.absorb_tls_error_into_timeout> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ai_text_invents_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ai_text_invents_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "AI-generated text must be bound to a concrete backend value. The text may\nrephrase or explain the value, but it may not add, remove, or invert the\nfact. If the backend returns a blocked reason, show the reason — not a\ngeneric or humorous substitute." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ai_text_invents_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use AI-generated or LLM-drafted text to describe a system state that the\nbackend did not confirm — including invented success, invented failures,\ninvented approvals, or speculation presented as observation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ai_text_invents_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ui.ai_text_must_not_invent_state> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ai_text_invents_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.cache_nil_handle_permanently> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.defer_in_for_loop_without_closure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.dispatch_as_success> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.dispatch_as_success> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Return ACCEPTED at dispatch time. Poll or stream workflow status until\na terminal state (SUCCEEDED / FAILED / BLOCKED) is observed. Report\nthat terminal state to the operator. For destructive or irreversible\noperations, require explicit confirmation before dispatch — not after." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.dispatch_as_success> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Report success to the user immediately after dispatching an async,\nirreversible, or destructive action — before the workflow or backend\nhas confirmed terminal success." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.dispatch_as_success> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/workflow.dispatch_is_not_completion> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.dispatch_as_success> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/workflow.success_requires_backend_confirmation> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.dispatch_as_success> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.fire_and_forget_goroutine_on_error_path> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.fix.delete_legacy_runtime_dirs_without_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.fix.hide_permission_error_with_allowlist> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.fix.layout_drift_by_expanding_allowlist_only> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.fmt_errorf_v_verb_for_wrapped_err> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.localhost_dns_bypass> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.localhost_dns_bypass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fix the root cause: update the certificate SAN, correct the DNS record,\nor resolve the routing misconfiguration. Switching to loopback hides\nthe problem, breaks multi-node correctness, and bypasses mTLS identity.\nListener bind addresses must use 0.0.0.0, not 127.0.0.1." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.localhost_dns_bypass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Replace a cluster DNS name, node IP, or VIP with localhost or 127.0.0.1\nto work around a TLS, DNS, SAN, or routing failure." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.localhost_dns_bypass> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/network.no_loopback_escape_for_cluster_identity> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.localhost_dns_bypass> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.missing_inventory_as_down> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.missing_inventory_as_down> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Absent records mean UNKNOWN, not KNOWN_BAD. Use the three-bucket model:\nPRESENT / UNKNOWN / KNOWN_BAD. Only KNOWN_BAD contributes to severity\nescalation. When DataIncomplete=true and KNOWN_BAD count is 0, suppress\nCRITICAL and emit a caveat about the partial snapshot instead." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.missing_inventory_as_down> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat missing inventory, absent collector data, or an absent NodeRecord\nin a snapshot as evidence that a node, service, or member is known-down." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.missing_inventory_as_down> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/evidence.missing_is_not_known_bad> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.missing_inventory_as_down> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/objectstore.partial_snapshot_unknown_not_down> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.missing_inventory_as_down> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/state.unknown_must_not_default_to_healthy> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.missing_inventory_as_down> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.optimistic_destructive_success> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.optimistic_destructive_success> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Return an accepted receipt at dispatch time. Stream or poll workflow status\nuntil a terminal state is reached. Report that terminal state to the user.\nDestructive operations must additionally require operator confirmation\nbefore dispatch." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.optimistic_destructive_success> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Report success to the user for a destructive or irreversible operation\nbefore backend or workflow confirmation is received." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.optimistic_destructive_success> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/workflow.success_requires_backend_confirmation> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.optimistic_destructive_success> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.partial_snapshot_false_quorum_loss> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.partial_snapshot_false_quorum_loss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Classify absent NodeRecord entries as UNKNOWN. Emit a DataIncomplete caveat\non the finding. Only classify a node as KNOWN_DOWN when its NodeRecord is\npresent in the snapshot and explicitly reports unhealthy or unreachable." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.partial_snapshot_false_quorum_loss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fire a quorum-loss finding or emit a KNOWN_DOWN classification for a node\nthat is absent from an incomplete objectstore snapshot, treating absence\nas evidence of failure rather than a collector gap." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.partial_snapshot_false_quorum_loss> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.partial_snapshot_false_quorum_loss> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/objectstore.partial_snapshot_unknown_not_down> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.partial_snapshot_false_quorum_loss> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.permission_denied_as_network_error> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.permission_denied_as_network_error> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Map PERMISSION_DENIED distinctly from transient errors. Show a clear\n\"not authorized\" message. Do not show a retry button for PERMISSION_DENIED.\nDisable the action before submit when the RBAC result is known ahead of time." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.permission_denied_as_network_error> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Display a gRPC PERMISSION_DENIED error as a generic network error,\nconnection failure, or unknown error, causing the user to diagnose\nconnectivity instead of authorization." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.permission_denied_as_network_error> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ui.action_requires_permission_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.permission_denied_as_network_error> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.runtime_from_desired> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.runtime_from_desired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Read runtime health from the runtime authority: systemd unit state,\ngRPC health RPC, or a live socket probe. Desired state expresses intent;\nit must never answer the question \"is it running right now?\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.runtime_from_desired> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Infer runtime health or liveness from desired state, desired-release records,\nor install-workflow completions instead of a live runtime probe." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.runtime_from_desired> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/runtime.desired_enabled_not_alive> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.runtime_from_desired> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/state.runtime_not_desired> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.runtime_from_desired> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ui.visible_state_requires_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.runtime_from_desired> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.silent_default_in_state_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ui_action_enabled_without_permission> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ui_action_enabled_without_permission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Call the RBAC permission check before rendering the action component.\nDisable the button and display a \"requires <permission>\" tooltip when\nthe check returns denied. Pre-disabling is better than post-submit denial." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ui_action_enabled_without_permission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Enable a destructive or state-mutating UI action button without first\nchecking the user's RBAC permission for that action." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ui_action_enabled_without_permission> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ui.action_requires_permission_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.ui_action_enabled_without_permission> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unbounded_retry_on_transient_failure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unknown_as_healthy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unknown_as_healthy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Treat UNKNOWN as a distinct state — not as HEALTHY. Status aggregations\nmust propagate UNKNOWN upward to the summary level. Show \"unknown as of T\"\nrather than defaulting to a passing status." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unknown_as_healthy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Render an unknown or unobserved state as healthy/green in status rollups,\nbadges, or CLI output." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unknown_as_healthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/state.runtime_not_desired> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unknown_as_healthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ui.status_freshness_must_be_surfaced> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unknown_as_healthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ui.visible_state_requires_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.unknown_as_healthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_as_node_identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_as_node_identity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use StableIP(clusterVIP) — which filters the known cluster VIP from the\nnode's IP list — for all identity-bearing operations: etcd peer URLs,\nScyllaDB seed nodes, MinIO pool IPs, leader election self-match.\nNever use PrimaryIP() or Ips[0] in identity contexts without first\nexcluding the floating VIP." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_as_node_identity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use a floating Virtual IP, load balancer address, keepalived VIP, or\nfailover endpoint as the stable identity of a node in etcd, ScyllaDB,\nMinIO, or any other membership/leadership system." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_as_node_identity> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.stable_node_identity_not_floating_vip> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_as_node_identity> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ops.vip_requires_observed_owner> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_as_node_identity> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_without_runtime_proof> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_without_runtime_proof> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Identify the VIP holder by reading /globular/ingress/v1/status/{node_id}\nand looking for VRRP MASTER state. A gateway profile or a keepalived\ninstallation record is necessary but not sufficient — only live VRRP state\nproves current VIP ownership." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_without_runtime_proof> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assume a node holds the cluster VIP because it has the 'gateway' profile,\nbecause keepalived is installed, or because desired topology includes it\nas a gateway node — without reading the live VRRP state from etcd." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_without_runtime_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ops.vip_requires_observed_owner> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden.vip_without_runtime_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.add_workflow_dispatch_to_globular_node_executor_to_fix_the_c> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.add_workflow_dispatch_to_globular_node_executor_to_fix_the_c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "least privilege: globular-node-executor is bound to every joining worker node; dispatch rights belong to globular-controller-sa alone" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.add_workflow_dispatch_to_globular_node_executor_to_fix_the_c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Add workflow.dispatch to globular-node-executor to fix the controller's PermissionDenied" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.add_workflow_dispatch_to_globular_node_executor_to_fix_the_c> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.close_the_client_returned_by_config_getetcdclient> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.close_the_client_returned_by_config_getetcdclient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "GetEtcdClient returns the process-wide SHARED etcd singleton; NewEtcdClient returns a caller-owned client. Writing the idiomatic 'cli, err := config.GetEtcdClient(); defer cli.Close()' therefore destroys etcd access for every other caller in the process. Observed 2026-08-11 on 1.2.310: a per-minute invariant path did exactly this, and the controller spun continuously on 'grpc: the client connection is closing' while every cluster RPC failed DeadlineExceeded and the cluster never reached ready. The defer looks correct in isolation and is the habit every Go reviewer has; the hazard is invisible at the call site because the function name does not say 'shared'. Either take the shared client and do not close it, or call NewEtcdClient and own the lifecycle. A short-lived CLI closing it at exit is harmless; a long-running service doing so is an outage." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.close_the_client_returned_by_config_getetcdclient> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Close the client returned by config.GetEtcdClient" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.close_the_client_returned_by_config_getetcdclient> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/infrastructure.etcd.quorum_backed_config_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.close_the_client_returned_by_config_getetcdclient> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.derive_etcd_initial_cluster_from_desired_placement_instead_o> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.derive_etcd_initial_cluster_from_desired_placement_instead_o> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Building initial-cluster from the node registry (which nodes SHOULD run etcd), or from any snapshot taken before the node's etcd first starts. etcd validates initial-cluster by count against its own member list, and the two sets disagree for the whole join window. For a member that has never initialized the mismatch is permanent — it has no WAL to fall back on, so it re-reads the same wrong file and restart-loops forever. Also forbidden: dropping an unstarted (unnamed) member from the render, which breaks the count the same way." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.derive_etcd_initial_cluster_from_desired_placement_instead_o> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Derive etcd initial-cluster from desired placement instead of the live member list" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.derive_etcd_initial_cluster_from_desired_placement_instead_o> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.derive_etcd_initial_cluster_from_desired_placement_instead_o> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.gate_the_etcd_endpoint_list_on_node_convergence_status> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.gate_the_etcd_endpoint_list_on_node_convergence_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "invariant:etcd.endpoint_reachability — the endpoint list must name reachable etcd members, and membership is etcd's to declare" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.gate_the_etcd_endpoint_list_on_node_convergence_status> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Gate the etcd endpoint list on node convergence status" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.gate_the_etcd_endpoint_list_on_node_convergence_status> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.let_an_already_established_member_back_through_join_prefligh> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.let_an_already_established_member_back_through_join_prefligh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Exempting a node from the join preflight identity-conflict scan whenever it matches an existing record, without checking that the existing record is still bootstrapping. approveJoinRecordLocked overwrites state.Nodes with a fresh converging/BootstrapAdmitted nodeState, so admitting an already-active member discards its placement generation, bootstrap phase and runtime progress — turning a cheap refusal into a reset of a healthy node. The exemption exists only so a node mid-join can retry past the record its own previous attempt created." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.let_an_already_established_member_back_through_join_prefligh> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Let an already-established member back through join preflight" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.let_an_already_established_member_back_through_join_prefligh> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.half_done_must_not_look_done> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.let_an_already_established_member_back_through_join_prefligh> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.move_scylladb_api_address_to_loopback_to_make_nodetool_work> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.move_scylladb_api_address_to_loopback_to_make_nodetool_work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Setting scylla.yaml api_address to 127.0.0.1 because nodetool defaults to loopback and was failing with 'exit status 2 / Connection refused'. It does fix nodetool, and it looks like a security improvement because the admin API is unauthenticated — but the admin API has REMOTE consumers and moving it silently breaks them: cluster_controller calls /storage_service/host_id and /storage_service/remove_node on OTHER nodes during ring removal, and backup_manager sweeps the LAN IPs to discover the address it registers with scylla-manager. Applied 2026-08-11, it left every node stuck at 'scylla auto-registration: local ScyllaDB not yet reachable on its LAN REST API' with cluster_count=0, so backup, repair and restore were unavailable while every node was NORMAL and visibly healthy; the doctor surfaced it as scylla_manager.cluster_registered ERROR. The real nodetool defect was that the probe chose -h by ranging over a Go MAP of local IPs, so the address varied run to run — fix the determinism and pass -h explicitly, and leave api_address on the routable IP. Locking the API down is legitimate but requires routing the controller's ring-removal calls through node_agent first." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.move_scylladb_api_address_to_loopback_to_make_nodetool_work> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Move ScyllaDB api_address to loopback to make nodetool work" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.move_scylladb_api_address_to_loopback_to_make_nodetool_work> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.has_single_canonical_source_and_is_immutable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.move_scylladb_api_address_to_loopback_to_make_nodetool_work> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A standalone publisher.type {service,org,user} duplicates RBAC subject identity. Publisher kind must be derived from the owning RBAC subject (Organization / Account / service account), not modeled twice." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Resolve the publisher namespace's owning RBAC subject and derive kind from the subject's type." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not add a parallel publisher identity/type enum" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.publisher_kind_derived_from_rbac_subject> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.publisher_namespace_is_rbac_resource> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.release_authority_is_rbac_native> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.add_parallel_publisher_type_enum> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_git_tag_to_allocate_release_without_repository> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_git_tag_to_allocate_release_without_repository> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A git tag is release intent, not authority. Allocating a release version directly from a tag bypasses the repository (the single version authority) and its RBAC permission check." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_git_tag_to_allocate_release_without_repository> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The tag is intent; the resolved subject must pass the RBAC permission check and the repository allocates the release identity." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_git_tag_to_allocate_release_without_repository> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not let a git tag allocate a release version without the repository" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_git_tag_to_allocate_release_without_repository> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.ci_is_not_release_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_git_tag_to_allocate_release_without_repository> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/release.version_single_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_git_tag_to_allocate_release_without_repository> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_stable_without_rbac_permission> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_stable_without_rbac_permission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Require repository.release.allocate on the namespace for any STABLE target; force everything else to DEV." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_stable_without_rbac_permission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "STABLE is the cluster's convergence stream. Writing to it without proving the subject holds repository.release.allocate lets a DEV-only or unauthenticated caller pollute releases." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_stable_without_rbac_permission> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not allow a STABLE-channel write without an RBAC permission check" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_stable_without_rbac_permission> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.release_allocation_requires_rbac_permission> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_stable_without_rbac_permission> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.stable_channel_requires_release_permission> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.allow_stable_without_rbac_permission> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.authorize_release_from_forge_identity_directly> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.authorize_release_from_forge_identity_directly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A GitHub org/user/repo, forge token, or CI environment proves identity, not authority. Authorizing \"GitHub org == globulario therefore allow STABLE\" makes the forge the authority and bypasses RBAC." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.authorize_release_from_forge_identity_directly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Resolve the forge identity to an RBAC subject via trusted_publisher, then perform a separate RBAC permission check on that subject." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.authorize_release_from_forge_identity_directly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not authorize a release from a forge identity directly" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.authorize_release_from_forge_identity_directly> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.forge_binding_is_not_authorization> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.authorize_release_from_forge_identity_directly> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.release_authority_is_rbac_native> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.authorize_release_from_forge_identity_directly> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.hardcode_ci_release_privilege> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.hardcode_ci_release_privilege> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CI authenticates, resolves to an RBAC subject, and passes normal RBAC authorization for repository.release.allocate." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.hardcode_ci_release_privilege> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CI is a forge adapter with no implicit privilege. Hardcoding a CI release privilege re-couples release authority to a build environment." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.hardcode_ci_release_privilege> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not hardcode CI as a privileged release actor" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.hardcode_ci_release_privilege> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.ci_is_not_release_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.package.hardcode_ci_release_privilege> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.raise_maxuses_or_recreate_the_token_to_get_a_stranded_node_t> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.raise_maxuses_or_recreate_the_token_to_get_a_stranded_node_t> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bumping a join token's MaxUses, minting a replacement token, or decrementing Uses on failure to work around a node that cannot rejoin. These treat the budget as the problem when the defect is that the budget counts ATTEMPTS instead of NODE ADMISSIONS — the workaround scales with how flaky the network is and silently widens how many distinct nodes the token admits. Also forbidden: dropping the preflight hostname/IP conflict check to let a retry through; the check is correct, it just has to exempt the node from colliding with its own record (same hostname AND a shared routable IP)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.raise_maxuses_or_recreate_the_token_to_get_a_stranded_node_t> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Raise MaxUses or recreate the token to get a stranded node to rejoin" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.raise_maxuses_or_recreate_the_token_to_get_a_stranded_node_t> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.half_done_must_not_look_done> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.raise_maxuses_or_recreate_the_token_to_get_a_stranded_node_t> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.resolve_a_workflow_key_mismatch_by_trying_both_key_shapes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.resolve_a_workflow_key_mismatch_by_trying_both_key_shapes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An etcd workflow key is the bare workflow name, defined by its writer; the .yaml extension belongs to the local filename only." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.resolve_a_workflow_key_mismatch_by_trying_both_key_shapes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Resolve a workflow key mismatch by trying both key shapes" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.resolve_a_workflow_key_mismatch_by_trying_both_key_shapes> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.field_semantic_is_single_writer_defined> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.resolve_a_workflow_key_mismatch_by_trying_both_key_shapes> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.satisfy_a_nil_gated_subsystem_by_setting_the_field_in_the_te> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.satisfy_a_nil_gated_subsystem_by_setting_the_field_in_the_te> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When a subsystem is gated on a field (srv.lastSpec, a cached config, an injected client) and the tests construct that field directly in a struct literal, the tests prove the code below the gate works while saying nothing about whether the gate ever opens. If no production path assigns the field, the feature is inert and every test still passes. Do not add or extend such a test as evidence the path works. Assert the WIRING: that the field gets populated by the running system, or that its absence is derived/reported rather than silently skipped. A green suite over a permanently-closed gate is how the entire certificate renewal subsystem ran for zero seconds in production." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.satisfy_a_nil_gated_subsystem_by_setting_the_field_in_the_te> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Satisfy a nil-gated subsystem by setting the field in the test instead of wiring production" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.satisfy_a_nil_gated_subsystem_by_setting_the_field_in_the_te> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/diagnostics.must_measure_reality> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.satisfy_a_nil_gated_subsystem_by_setting_the_field_in_the_te> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.skip_an_unsafe_archive_entry_and_continue_installing_the_res> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.skip_an_unsafe_archive_entry_and_continue_installing_the_res> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Do not add a skip-and-log or compatibility mode to package archive extraction, and do not validate entries one at a time while streaming. Both leave a package partially installed while the version marker advances and the service restarts, so the installed payload no longer matches the published artifact — package identity becomes unprovable and rollback evidence ambiguous. A package is admitted in full or rejected in full. Equally forbidden: normalizing entry names with strings.TrimLeft(name, \"./\"), whose cutset consumes the dots of a leading ../ and launders a traversal into an innocent relative path." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.skip_an_unsafe_archive_entry_and_continue_installing_the_res> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Skip an unsafe archive entry and continue installing the rest of the package" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.skip_an_unsafe_archive_entry_and_continue_installing_the_res> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/invariant.package_archive_extraction_must_stay_within_node_owned_desti> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/forbidden_fix.skip_an_unsafe_archive_entry_and_continue_installing_the_res> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
