<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generate_code_when_alignment_verdict_is_conflicting> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generate_code_when_alignment_verdict_is_unknown_impact> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A generic read tool authorises around every owner's RPC contract. Even allowlist-blocked tools represent a structural vector: a single policy change or allowlist edit exposes the entire cluster state to callers that have no contract with the owners. The principle is the same as the write-side generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers: the safe state is not \"blocked at the policy\", it is \"the tool does not exist\"." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Replace generic read tools with owner-specific typed RPCs. If a diagnostic surface is needed, expose ListFindings (via cluster-doctor) and the owner's typed Get/List RPCs — never a \"give me any prefix\" tool. Bootstrap-only paths (config seeds, leader election) that need a generic primitive must be scoped to a fixed prefix allowlist HARD-CODED in the tool, not configured externally." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Expose a generic etcd_get / etcd_list / storage_read tool to MCP / admin / external callers, even when an allowlist currently blocks remote use. Examples: mcp/tools_etcd.go's etcd_get, an admin CLI's \"raw etcd get\" command, a debugging endpoint that returns arbitrary /globular/* paths." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.truth_read_via_owner_rpc_not_direct_storage> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/mcp.etcd.tools_must_not_join_remote_allowlist> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fmcp%2Faggregator_policy.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_or_storage_read_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fmcp%2Ftools_etcd.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A generic write tool authorises around every layer-owner's contract. The \"/globular/\" prefix guard does not narrow the blast radius — it still permits writes to L1/L2/L3 paths owned by the repository, cluster_controller, and per-node node_agent. The read_only flag is operator-configurable and represents a single switch between safe and catastrophic. forbidden_fix:cross_layer_write_by_non_owner is violated by any caller of such a tool that writes a path it does not own — and the tool itself does not constrain who its callers are.\nThe remote-allowlist is also not protection: invariant mcp.etcd.tools_must_not_join_remote_allowlist (anchored) names the rule, and failure_mode:mcp.etcd_remote_allowlist_expansion names the regression class where a tool was once safely local and then quietly added to remote_call. The safe state is \"the tool does not exist\", not \"the tool exists but is blocked at the door\".\nRemoved v1.2.167: tools_etcd.go's registerEtcdTools no longer registers etcd_get / etcd_put / etcd_delete. The architectural pin test in mcp_etcd_authority_pin_test.go fails the build if any of them is re-introduced." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use the owner's typed RPC. Mutations to L1 go through repository (UploadArtifact, UpdateArtifactBinary). Mutations to L2 go through cluster_controller (ApplyServiceRelease, UpsertDesiredService). Mutations to L3 go through the per-node node_agent's typed handlers (ApplyPackageRelease, etc.). For operator workflows that span multiple owners, dispatch through the workflow service.\nIf a bootstrap-only generic write primitive is genuinely needed (e.g., Day-0 day0_seed paths), scope it to a fixed prefix allowlist HARD-CODED in the tool, narrowly named (day0_seed_set, never etcd_put), and gate it on a Day-0 boot phase that auto-disables after first apply." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Expose a generic etcd_put / etcd_delete / storage_write tool to MCP / admin / external callers, even when an allowlist currently blocks remote use AND even when the tool guards itself with a \"/globular/\" prefix check or a read_only flag. Examples: mcp/tools_etcd.go's etcd_put + etcd_delete (removed v1.2.167), an admin command that accepts an arbitrary key+value to Put, a debugging endpoint with a \"set\" verb." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/etcd.path_has_single_owner> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.layer_has_single_writing_actor> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/mcp.etcd.tools_must_not_join_remote_allowlist> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fmcp%2Faggregator_policy.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fmcp%2Fserver.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/generic_etcd_write_tool_exposed_to_callers> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fmcp%2Ftools_etcd.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/grant_admission_on_etcd_lookup_failure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/grant_node_executor_desired_state_write> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/grant_node_executor_rbac_admin> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/grow_allowlist_to_avoid_token_plumbing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inject cluster_id at the connection (interceptor) level using security.GetLocalClusterID() as the canonical source, with metadata.AppendToOutgoingContext so any upstream metadata is preserved. Keep optional propagation of the cluster_id field for cases where the caller has a more authoritative source — but never make it the sole mechanism." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "cluster_id is a connection-level invariant, not a call-site concern. Tying it to a field that may or may not be populated (cluster_doctor's c.clusterID was only set via WithWorkflowClient — if the workflow dial failed or wfEndpoint was empty, all later repository/ai-memory/awareness-graph calls silently skipped injection). The failure mode is invisible at the call site and surfaces only as Unauthenticated errors on the wire." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Make cluster_id metadata injection conditional on a struct field (e.g. collector.clusterID) that is populated through an optional setup path, so when that path doesn't run the guard silently skips and every RPC fails Unauthenticated." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/grpc.backbone.contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fcollector%2Fcollector.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/guard_cluster_id_injection_on_optionally_propagated_field> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fserver.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/halting_all_reconciliation_when_workflow_is_degraded> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_packagecatalog_specs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_packagecatalog_specs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Edit packages/registry.yaml (the real source of truth) and regenerate the mirror with ../globular-installer/Makefile sync-specs; validate with check-specs." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_packagecatalog_specs> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Directly hand-edit globular-installer/internal/packagecatalog/* instead of regenerating it from packages/registry.yaml via the Makefile sync-specs target. The embedded catalog is a generated mirror bound to the registry by manifest digest; a hand edit drifts from its source of truth without changing the digest that is supposed to prove they match." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_packagecatalog_specs> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repo.installer_embedded_assets_are_generated_mirrors_only> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_packagecatalog_specs> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_webroot_as_source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_webroot_as_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Edit services/webroot (the real source) and regenerate the mirror with ../globular-installer/Makefile sync-webroot; validate with check-webroot." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_webroot_as_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Directly hand-edit globular-installer/internal/assets/webroot as if it were authored platform content, instead of treating it as a generated fallback mirror of services/webroot." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_webroot_as_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repo.installer_embedded_assets_are_generated_mirrors_only> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hand_edit_installer_webroot_as_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
