<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hardcoding_a_literal_version_in_service_main> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "For missing local POSIX blobs, use the upstream-import path: `globular repository sync --tag vX.Y.Z` triggers materializeLocalPackageArchive, which writes verified bytes from the upstream release into /var/lib/globular/packages/ on every node. For repository-side missing artifacts, the operator republishes via `globular pkg publish` against the artifact downloaded from the upstream GitHub release. Either way the bytes flow from the upstream source, not from MinIO. The publish-reconciler's only legitimate role is to retry stuck VERIFIED→PUBLISHED promotions; it must not heal MISSING_BLOB." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "MinIO is for secondary user data only. Package artifacts live in /var/lib/globular/packages/ (the per-node install-time CAS) and in the repository service's own /var/lib/globular/repository/artifacts/ backend — never in MinIO. The fact that the running v1.2.159 repository writes a \"mirror\" copy to MinIO via ResilientStorage is legacy architectural drift, not a contract; bytes appearing in MinIO are a symptom of the drift, not a recovery source. Reading from the mirror — even under cryptographic verification — legitimizes the violation: it makes MinIO authoritative in the recovery path, locks future code to assume mirror presence, and silently entrenches the rule violation rather than removing it.\nLive regression class: v1.2.162's first cut added exactly this sweep (`healPublishedMissingBlobsOnce`) and was reverted before merge." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Add a publish-reconciler sweep (or any recovery path) that reads package binary bytes from MinIO mirror and writes them into the repository's local POSIX CAS, on the theory that the mirror is \"informational only\" and the checksum-verify gate makes it safe." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.minio_is_not_valid_package_source> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Frepository%2Frepository_server%2Fartifact_handlers.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Frepository%2Frepository_server%2Fpublish_reconciler.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_inventory_omits_partial_marker> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_inventory_omits_partial_marker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Add `InstalledPackagesObservability` to the heartbeat proto: per-kind enumeration status, source timestamp, error if any. The controller branches on observability before treating the per-kind list as authoritative." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_inventory_omits_partial_marker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Layer-3 heartbeat reports `InstalledPackages` but lacks a per-source completeness marker. Controller cannot distinguish \"service absent from this node\" from \"this node's source for that service kind was unavailable this tick\"." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_inventory_omits_partial_marker> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/infra.heartbeat_observer_only_not_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_inventory_omits_partial_marker> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_inventory_omits_partial_marker> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_sets_desired_hash> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/heartbeat_sets_desired_version> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hiding_required_runtime_dependency_from_package_manifest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hold_mode_allows_dispatch_with_stale_inputs> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hot_deploy_local_binary_as_break_glass> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hot_deploy_local_binary_as_break_glass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use the typed escape that already exists for the broken layer: controller — `controller.bootstrap_handoff_required` event + operator restart of leader; node-agent install — Day-1 join fetches from GitHub release, not the cluster repository; etcd rejoin — call `cluster_controller.RejoinNode` RPC which enforces 4 preconditions; repository corruption — `globular pkg publish --force` + repair-unseal flow with audit logging. If a needed escape does not exist, file an invariant for it; do not invent an ad-hoc `cp`." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hot_deploy_local_binary_as_break_glass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recover from a broken control-plane service by `scp` / `cp` of a locally-built binary onto a node and `systemctl restart` — bypassing the repository, the manifest's entrypoint_checksum, the controller's typed ApplyPackageRelease dispatch, and the audit trail." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hot_deploy_local_binary_as_break_glass> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.has_single_canonical_source_and_is_immutable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hot_deploy_local_binary_as_break_glass> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.circular_dependency_must_have_break_glass> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/hot_deploy_local_binary_as_break_glass> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_doctor_index> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_doctor_index> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Add artifact_state as a string field to ArtifactManifest proto. Populate it in\nListArtifacts from the Scylla artifact_state column. Update buildIDIndexFromManifests\nto mirror isRowInstallable's two-column check. This makes the doctor's index agree\nexactly with the resolver's installability decision for every row." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_doctor_index> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use IsInstallableByPin (publish_state only) as the sole filter in\nbuildIDIndexFromManifests, allowing split-state build_ids to appear as\n\"resolvable\" in RepositoryBuildIDIndex even though the resolver would reject them.\nThe doctor then stays silent on a desired pin that will generate an endless\nDesiredBuildIdOrphaned error for every node that tries to install it." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_doctor_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_doctor_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.artifact.installable_compound_predicate> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_doctor_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_orphan_checks> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_orphan_checks> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "1. Fix the write path: promoteToPublished MUST call transitionArtifactState(PipelinePublished)\n   so both columns are set atomically. If the artifact_state write failed, the artifact\n   stays in VERIFIED (not discoverable) until publish is retried.\n2. Run backfillArtifactStates to repair any existing stuck BLOB_VERIFIED rows: it verifies\n   the blob is present, then drives the state machine forward to PipelinePublished.\n3. Never remove the artifact_state check from isRowInstallable. The check costs nothing\n   and catches a class of broken rows that publish_state alone cannot distinguish." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_orphan_checks> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Remove or bypass the artifact_state check in resolveByBuildID / isRowInstallable\nso that a row with publish_state=PUBLISHED is always treated as installable regardless\nof artifact_state. This \"fixes\" the DesiredBuildIdOrphaned symptom by hiding the\nsplit-state signal rather than repairing the underlying data inconsistency." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_orphan_checks> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_orphan_checks> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.artifact.installable_compound_predicate> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_orphan_checks> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.desired_build_id_must_resolve> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_artifact_state_in_orphan_checks> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_backend_health_on_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_backend_health_on_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Check Scylla health and quorum state before dispatching; if health check fails, return a retriable error to the caller without creating a workflow record." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_backend_health_on_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Skip the backend health preflight check when dispatching workflows, relying on Scylla to surface errors during the write rather than failing fast before creating the record." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_backend_health_on_dispatch> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_backend_health_on_dispatch> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/workflow.backend_health_gate> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_backend_health_on_dispatch> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_certificate_san_mismatch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_context_timeout_in_critical_query> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_context_timeout_in_critical_query> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always check ctx.Err() after a bounded query; return the timeout error to the caller; do not proceed as if the query succeeded." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_context_timeout_in_critical_query> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ignore or suppress the ctx.Err() result from a bounded query in a critical path, allowing the caller to proceed as if the query succeeded." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_context_timeout_in_critical_query> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_queries.must_be_bounded> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_context_timeout_in_critical_query> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_context_timeout_in_critical_query> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_forbidden_fix_edges_in_scoring> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_forbidden_fix_edges_in_scoring> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In ScoreImpactPath, apply the decision domain bonus (+25) to steps that touch\nforbidden_fix or invariant nodes via EdgeForbids. Rank these paths first." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_forbidden_fix_edges_in_scoring> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Score impact paths without giving extra weight to edges that lead to\nforbidden_fix nodes. Paths that terminate at forbidden_fix nodes are PRE-EDIT\ndecision paths — the most actionable signals in the graph. Scoring them the\nsame as information paths causes them to be buried under less relevant results." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_forbidden_fix_edges_in_scoring> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.graph.domain_classification_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_forbidden_fix_edges_in_scoring> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_forbidden_fix_edges_in_scoring> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_lkg_when_authority_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_lkg_when_authority_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always fall back to the LKG file when authority is unreachable; treat a missing LKG as first-boot only; never serve empty config on authority timeout." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_lkg_when_authority_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fail or use empty config when the authority source is unreachable instead of falling back to the validated LKG file." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_lkg_when_authority_unavailable> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_lkg_when_authority_unavailable> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/runtime.last_known_good_required_for_critical_consumers> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_lkg_when_authority_unavailable> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_missing_workflow_checksum_field> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_package_kind_in_runtime_proof> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_package_kind_in_runtime_proof> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use the catalog-defined kind as the sole gate for systemd unit requirement; package name heuristics must not override catalog kind." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_package_kind_in_runtime_proof> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use only the package name (not the catalog-defined kind) to decide whether a systemd unit is required. This causes false positives for new command packages." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_package_kind_in_runtime_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.identity_computation_must_be_invariant> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_package_kind_in_runtime_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/runtime.installed_state_must_match_package_kind> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_package_kind_in_runtime_proof> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_publisher_field_during_cross_cluster_sync> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_rf_violation_in_multi_node> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_rf_violation_in_multi_node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Doctor must emit CRITICAL for any critical keyspace below required RF on a cluster with >=2 nodes; include an ALTER KEYSPACE command in the remediation step." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_rf_violation_in_multi_node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allow a critical keyspace to remain below required RF on a multi-node cluster without emitting a doctor finding or repair action." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_rf_violation_in_multi_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_rf_violation_in_multi_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/scylla.critical_keyspace_replication_policy> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_rf_violation_in_multi_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_status.resolved_build_id_when_collecting_desired_roots> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_status_resolved_build_id_when_collecting_desired_roots> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_status_resolved_build_id_when_collecting_desired_roots> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Collect BOTH Spec.BuildID and Status.ResolvedBuildID across all\nfour desired-state etcd prefixes. The reachability guard must\ntreat any pinned build_id — wherever pinned — as a hard root." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_status_resolved_build_id_when_collecting_desired_roots> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "collectDesiredBuildIDs scans only Spec.BuildID and forgets that\nStatus.ResolvedBuildID is also a live pin (the controller writes\nit when resolving a version policy at dispatch time). The guard\nblocks deletion of the SPEC build_id but happily archives the\nRESOLVED one, breaking installs mid-rollout." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_status_resolved_build_id_when_collecting_desired_roots> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_status_resolved_build_id_when_collecting_desired_roots> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.purge_must_not_delete_active_desired_builds> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignore_status_resolved_build_id_when_collecting_desired_roots> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignoring_orphan_processes_assuming_systemd_handles_them> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignoring_orphan_processes_assuming_systemd_handles_them> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Add ExecStartPre=+/bin/sh -c 'pkill -9 -x <binary> || true' to every service unit that binds a port; this kills any orphaned process from a prior cgroup escape before the new process tries to bind. MUST use -x (process-name match), never -f — `pkill -f` matches the FULL command line including the parent shell's argv (which contains the binary name as the pkill argument), so the parent shell self-SIGKILLs and ExecStartPre fails. For binary names >15 chars use the bracket trick: pkill -9 -f '[<first_char>]<rest>'." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignoring_orphan_processes_assuming_systemd_handles_them> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assume systemd's Restart= directive cleanly terminates all child processes from a prior cgroup escape when the service restarts, without adding an ExecStartPre kill step." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignoring_orphan_processes_assuming_systemd_handles_them> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignoring_orphan_processes_assuming_systemd_handles_them> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.endpoint.cgroup_escape_guard> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ignoring_orphan_processes_assuming_systemd_handles_them> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
