<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/import_bundle_via_separate_non_sync_code_path> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/increase_drift_threshold_to_hide_low_severity_drift> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/increase_drift_threshold_to_hide_low_severity_drift> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Any drift on a seed-tagged entry is a fact about the immutability layer,\nnot a noise level to tune. Re-run the seeder, audit how the drift arose,\nand fix the originating CLI / RBAC bypass." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/increase_drift_threshold_to_hide_low_severity_drift> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Widen the drift-detection tolerance so \"small\" content differences between\nthe bundle and ai-memory no longer trigger the finding. Reduces noise by\nlosing signal that the immutability layer might be broken." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/increase_drift_threshold_to_hide_low_severity_drift> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/increase_drift_threshold_to_hide_low_severity_drift> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ops_knowledge.seed_integrity> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/increase_drift_threshold_to_hide_low_severity_drift> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
