<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Awareness anchors exist precisely to remind future contributors that the implementation may have drifted from the intended architecture. If the graph has an anchor and the code disagrees with the anchor, the anchor wins by definition — the code is the bug. Inferring \"the architecture is whatever the code currently does\" silently downgrades the anchor from a contract into a comment." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When the awareness graph has an anchor on a topic, design the fix against the anchor's contract. If the existing code violates the anchor, the fix should remove the violation rather than extend it. If the anchor and the implementation appear to be in genuine conflict and the right resolution isn't obvious, stop and surface the conflict to the operator — do not silently resolve it by deferring to the code." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat the running implementation as the architectural contract when an awareness anchor (invariant / forbidden_fix / intent) on the same topic already exists." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/assistant.query_awareness_before_assuming_architecture> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.minio_is_not_valid_package_source> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/CLAUDE.md> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_architecture_from_code_when_awareness_anchor_exists> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/docs%2Fawareness%2Finvariants.yaml> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_desired_from_runtime_observation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_kind_from_service_name> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_kind_from_service_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kind must always be read from package.json metadata. Service name is not a\nreliable proxy for kind — names change, packages are renamed, and inference\ncreates silent mismatches that only surface at convergence time." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_kind_from_service_name> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Infer package kind (infrastructure vs service) from the service name string (e.g.\n\"xds\" implies infrastructure) rather than reading from the canonical package\nmetadata registry." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_kind_from_service_name> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_kind_from_service_name> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
