<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_scylla_cluster_membership_from_local_process_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Local process state is observer-only and can be stale. A node may still have scylla-server running from a previous join attempt after being removed from the desired topology. Inference creates split-brain membership views and can allow a decommissioned node to participate in the cluster." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_scylla_cluster_membership_from_local_process_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Read ScyllaDB cluster membership from etcd (/globular/objectstore/scylla/members or equivalent cluster-controller-owned key). Never infer from local systemd state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_scylla_cluster_membership_from_local_process_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Determine which nodes are ScyllaDB members by checking if scylla-server is running or installed locally, rather than querying cluster topology from etcd." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_scylla_cluster_membership_from_local_process_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/objectstore.membership_requires_explicit_desired_state> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/infer_scylla_cluster_membership_from_local_process_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
