<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/iterate_all_artifact_versions_for_kind_resolution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/iterate_all_artifact_versions_for_kind_resolution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "After ListArtifacts(), build a map keyed by (name, platform) and retain only the highest-version manifest (versionutil.Compare; tie-break by build_number). Only the winner per key participates in kind resolution and staleService deletion logic." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/iterate_all_artifact_versions_for_kind_resolution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ListArtifacts() returns all published versions, including old ones. A version published before an artifact's kind was changed (e.g., INFRASTRUCTURE → SERVICE) carries the old kind. If the heartbeat processes that old manifest, it deletes the correctly-classified record written by the install pipeline and recreates it with the wrong kind and a fresh updatedUnix timestamp. This produces a permanent service.old_pid_after_upgrade finding and blocks install convergence. INC-2026-0019 (mcp 1.2.131/1.2.132 INFRA deleted SERVICE/mcp@1.2.133 on every heartbeat cycle). Fixed in 72cc72b2." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/iterate_all_artifact_versions_for_kind_resolution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Iterate every version returned by ListArtifacts() when resolving artifact kind in syncRepoArtifactsToEtcd, without deduplicating to the latest version per (name, platform)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/iterate_all_artifact_versions_for_kind_resolution> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/iterate_all_artifact_versions_for_kind_resolution> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fnode_agent%2Fnode_agent_server%2Fheartbeat.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/join_archive_entry_without_clean_boundary_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_drift_warning_forever_without_escalation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_drift_warning_forever_without_escalation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Apply driftSeverity() escalation: WARN for age <=5 min, ERROR for >5 min, CRITICAL for >5 min on a service defined as critical." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_drift_warning_forever_without_escalation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Keep service drift finding at WARN severity indefinitely regardless of age or affected services. Drift older than 5 minutes is ERROR; drift on critical services is CRITICAL." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_drift_warning_forever_without_escalation> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_drift_warning_forever_without_escalation> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/services.drift_must_age_and_escalate> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_drift_warning_forever_without_escalation> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_env_var_as_fallback_for_dev_only> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_env_var_as_fallback_for_dev_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Local dev seeds an etcd instance via the same code path as production.\nNo os.Getenv() for cluster addresses anywhere; if etcd is unreachable\nthe service ERRORS instead of falling back." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_env_var_as_fallback_for_dev_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Add `if os.Getenv(\"XYZ_ENDPOINT\") != \"\" { return env }` \"for dev only\" so\nlocal builds don't need etcd at startup. Ships per-node mutable\nconfiguration into the same binary as production code paths and breaks\nthe etcd-is-sole-source-of-truth rule." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_env_var_as_fallback_for_dev_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/etcd.endpoint_reachability> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_env_var_as_fallback_for_dev_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_env_var_as_fallback_for_dev_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.endpoint.etcd_address_reachability> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_env_var_as_fallback_for_dev_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/keep_undeclared_binary_aliases_in_packages_bin> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/leave_local_install_dir_empty_after_repository_import> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/leave_partial_contract_on_write_error> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/let_component_catalog_or_config_override_registry_kind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/let_component_catalog_or_config_override_registry_kind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "These are projections: derive kind from packagekind/registry (kindFromRegistry, registryArtifactKind, the inferPackageKind wrapper). Trust the registry-stamped manifest; do not re-correct it from a local list." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/let_component_catalog_or_config_override_registry_kind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Let component_catalog.go, config.json, an artifact manifest, or node-agent inference DECLARE or OVERRIDE a package's kind independently of registry.yaml (e.g. re-introduce inferCorrectKind overriding the published manifest, or hand-author Component.Kind)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/let_component_catalog_or_config_override_registry_kind> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.identity_computation_must_be_invariant> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/let_component_catalog_or_config_override_registry_kind> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.kind_is_registry_authored_downstream_is_projection> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/let_component_catalog_or_config_override_registry_kind> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/let_each_service_invent_its_own_runtime_dir_normalization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/local_deploy_allocates_release_version> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/local_deploy_allocates_release_version> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Local/agent builds use the dev channel and bump build_number only. Release versions are allocated by CI through the repository with the release-authority capability; the git tag is the intent input, the repository is the truth." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/local_deploy_allocates_release_version> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The release version has one authority — the repository on the release channel, gated by a release capability. A local `deploy --bump` or agent build that allocates a release version creates a second author, lands below the CI release high-water mark, and becomes unconvergeable desired-state. This is the observed root cause (local 1.2.234 below CI 1.2.235)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/local_deploy_allocates_release_version> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do not let a local or agent build allocate or advance a release version" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/local_deploy_allocates_release_version> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.release_vs_dev_channel_boundary> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/local_deploy_allocates_release_version> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/release.version_single_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/local_deploy_allocates_release_version> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes/package_identity_forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_and_continue_on_verification_failure> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_full_asset_url_for_debugging> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_only_fallback_without_finding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_only_fallback_without_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every fallback site calls emitDegradedFinding(...) at the moment of\nswitchover. Logging is supplementary, never primary." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_only_fallback_without_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Log \"falling back to X\" via stdout/journal but do not emit a\nstructured finding. Logs are not consumed by health/doctor; the\noperator sees green while the system is degraded." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_only_fallback_without_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/fallback.must_emit_degraded_finding> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_only_fallback_without_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_only_fallback_without_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_outage_message_on_every_tick> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/log_per_retry_without_dedup> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_dns_ttl_so_bad_resolutions_expire_faster> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_dns_ttl_so_bad_resolutions_expire_faster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Gate publication on Installed + Runtime-healthy. Records for\nunhealthy nodes never appear in the first place, so TTL becomes\na normal performance knob instead of a band-aid." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_dns_ttl_so_bad_resolutions_expire_faster> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A node's records keep pointing at a half-dead service, so the\noperator lowers the TTL from 60s to 5s to \"shorten the bad\nwindow.\" Caching layers (resolver, OS, gRPC client connection\npool) still cache the bad answer for longer than the TTL; the\nreal bug — publishing the record at all — is unfixed; cluster-\nwide query load multiplies." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_dns_ttl_so_bad_resolutions_expire_faster> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/dns.records_must_be_installed_and_runtime_healthy> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_dns_ttl_so_bad_resolutions_expire_faster> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_penalty_for_invalid_trust_paths> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_penalty_for_invalid_trust_paths> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Invalid paths must score below any declared path. If invalid paths are surfacing\nin practice, fix the graph data (reindex, validate) rather than inflating invalid\npath scores to paper over the gap." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_penalty_for_invalid_trust_paths> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reduce the score penalty for paths with TrustInvalid edges (currently -100)\nto make them \"less invisible\" in the output. Invalid paths represent broken\nor stale graph edges — making them visible in decision output is more\ndangerous than filtering them." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_penalty_for_invalid_trust_paths> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.weight_learning.human_approval_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_penalty_for_invalid_trust_paths> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/lower_penalty_for_invalid_trust_paths> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/make_allowedremotetools_configurable_at_runtime> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/make_services_repo_owner_of_installer_execution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/make_services_repo_owner_of_installer_execution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Keep install execution authority in globular-installer/scripts/install-day0.sh; services only publishes releases and authors package/registry data, per docs/design/artifact-authority-matrix.md and docs/design/package-authority-layout.md." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/make_services_repo_owner_of_installer_execution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have the services repo take on ownership of installer EXECUTION (running the actual install workflow) rather than remaining the release-publication and package-authority source, violating the documented cross-repo authority split." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/make_services_repo_owner_of_installer_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repo.release_wrapper_is_not_install_execution_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/make_services_repo_owner_of_installer_execution> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/making_background_dependency_startup_required_without_reason> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/making_reconciler_responsible_for_starting_join_installed_units> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manual_repair_path_diverges_from_committed_workflow_intent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manual_repair_path_diverges_from_committed_workflow_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Either (a) fix the canonical path and retry the workflow, or (b) explicitly mark the workflow ABANDONED with a documented reason and dispatch a NEW workflow for the corrective action. The quarantined scripts/forbidden-historical/ directory is the documented bad-example reference." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manual_repair_path_diverges_from_committed_workflow_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The discipline applies to humans too. A workflow stuck at FAILED is a signal that the canonical path needs investigation, not an invitation to take an alternative path outside the audit trail." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manual_repair_path_diverges_from_committed_workflow_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Operator (or AI agent) executes a manual repair that diverges from the workflow's committed intent" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manual_repair_path_diverges_from_committed_workflow_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manual_repair_path_diverges_from_committed_workflow_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manual_repair_path_diverges_from_committed_workflow_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_copy_package_blobs_without_index_repair> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_copy_package_blobs_without_index_repair> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use repository repair/import workflows that update metadata and blob provenance atomically." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_copy_package_blobs_without_index_repair> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Copying package blobs into object storage manually without repairing Scylla metadata/index rows and provenance links." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_copy_package_blobs_without_index_repair> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.metadata_first> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_copy_package_blobs_without_index_repair> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_delete_dep_block_keys_via_etcdctl_as_recovery_mechanism> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_patching_release_phase_to_available> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_patching_release_phase_to_available> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Retry the workflow's commit RPC with idempotent semantics; the workflow system handles the case where a wave succeeds but the terminal commit fails. Never write phase directly to etcd." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_patching_release_phase_to_available> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manually set ServiceRelease.Phase to AVAILABLE in etcd after a wave succeeds but the commit RPC fails, bypassing the workflow's terminal-state commit." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_patching_release_phase_to_available> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/install.result.atomic_commit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_patching_release_phase_to_available> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_patching_release_phase_to_available> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_running_services_desired_set_per_service> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_running_services_desired_set_per_service> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fix the BOM to include the missing service; re-run platform-upgrade to trigger the full desired-state pipeline. One-off RPC calls bypass provenance tracking and promotion validation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_running_services_desired_set_per_service> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Call the ServicesDesiredSet RPC individually for each service to work around a missing or incomplete BOM, creating desired-state records outside the platform-upgrade pipeline." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_running_services_desired_set_per_service> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_running_services_desired_set_per_service> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.desired_state.bom_completeness> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_running_services_desired_set_per_service> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_seeding_desired_state_per_node> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_seeding_desired_state_per_node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "All desired state must flow through the BOM release pipeline (platform-upgrade -> ServicesDesiredSet -> promotion reconciler). Manual seeding bypasses provenance tracking." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_seeding_desired_state_per_node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manually write DesiredService or DesiredRelease records per-node via direct etcd writes or gRPC calls outside the BOM pipeline, creating records that the promotion reconciler did not validate." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_seeding_desired_state_per_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_seeding_desired_state_per_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.desired_state.bom_completeness> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_seeding_desired_state_per_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_start_mcp_without_fixing_spec> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_start_mcp_without_fixing_spec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Add a start_services step to mcp_service.yaml for the Day-1 install; the spec is the source of truth for what runs after install. Manual systemctl calls are not durable across reinstalls." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_start_mcp_without_fixing_spec> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Manually run systemctl start globular-mcp.service after a Day-1 install to work around a missing start_services step in the spec, without updating the spec." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_start_mcp_without_fixing_spec> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/convergence.no_infinite_retry> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_start_mcp_without_fixing_spec> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/manually_start_mcp_without_fixing_spec> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
