<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_custom_grpc_client> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_custom_grpc_client> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use s.clients.get(ctx, gatewayEndpoint()) to get a pooled connection, then wrap it with the generated proto stub: stub := mypb.NewMyServiceClient(conn). Envoy routes the call by gRPC path prefix — no per-tool service discovery needed." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_custom_grpc_client> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Creating a standalone gRPC client (custom *grpc.ClientConn, custom TLS config, or a dedicated *_client package) inside a new MCP tool handler instead of using the shared gateway client pool. This was the exact mistake in tools_awareness.go: a bespoke awareness_graph_client.Client did its own etcd service lookup, failed silently when etcd was unreachable from the MCP process, and returned a misleading \"service not registered in etcd\" error even though the service was running and Envoy had a valid route." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_custom_grpc_client> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/mcp.tools.use_gateway_client_pool> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_custom_grpc_client> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_direct_service_discovery> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_direct_service_discovery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Call gatewayEndpoint() (defined in golang/mcp/clients.go) and obtain the connection through s.clients.get(ctx, endpoint). The gatewayEndpoint function already performs the correct mesh address resolution once; the pool reuses connections across all tool calls." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_direct_service_discovery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Calling config.ResolveServiceAddr, config.GetMeshAddress, or config.GetServicesConfigurationsByName directly inside an MCP tool handler to find a service endpoint. These functions require the MCP process to reach etcd with valid TLS, which may not be available, and they bypass the shared connection pool and Envoy mesh routing." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_direct_service_discovery> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/mcp.tools.use_gateway_client_pool> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_direct_service_discovery> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_executes_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_executes_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every mutating MCP tool dispatches a workflow via the governor. Read-only tools may call services directly; write tools never do." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_executes_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "MCP tools that mutate state are operator-facing actions, not queries. They must commit intent before action." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_executes_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MCP tool executes a state-changing RPC directly without going through plan→validate→approve→execute" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_executes_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_executes_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mcp_tool_executes_mutation_without_workflow_dispatch> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
