<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mutate_desired_build_id_after_resolver_pins_it> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mutate_desired_build_id_after_resolver_pins_it> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Once desired state is fully resolved (version + build_number both set), use persisted values directly. Only re-resolve on explicit desired-state update RPCs." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mutate_desired_build_id_after_resolver_pins_it> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Resolution during reconciliation is non-deterministic when multiple builds exist for a version. Re-resolving can silently switch the convergence target without operator approval, breaking the immutability contract and causing nodes to converge to a different artifact than what was approved." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mutate_desired_build_id_after_resolver_pins_it> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Re-resolve the desired-state version during reconciliation when both version and build_number are already set (pinned), silently switching convergence targets." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mutate_desired_build_id_after_resolver_pins_it> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.build_id_server_generated_not_client_driven> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/mutate_desired_build_id_after_resolver_pins_it> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
