<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/nest_a_data_key_under_an_etcd_mutex_prefix> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/nest_a_data_key_under_an_etcd_mutex_prefix> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Make the mutex key a leaf sibling of any related data key (mutex \".../foo/lock\", state \".../foo/state\") so the Mutex prefix scan never sees a non-lock key. Deleting a poisoning data key is a one-time RECOVERY only; the durable fix is the disjoint key layout plus a regression test asserting the mutex key is not a prefix of the data key." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/nest_a_data_key_under_an_etcd_mutex_prefix> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Store a state/config/data key under an etcd concurrency.Mutex key prefix (e.g. mutex \".../foo\" with state \".../foo/state\"), or \"fix\" the resulting Mutex.Lock deadlock by lengthening the timeout or by deleting the data key as a permanent workaround." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/nest_a_data_key_under_an_etcd_mutex_prefix> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/etcd.mutex_key_must_not_prefix_non_lock_keys> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/nest_a_data_key_under_an_etcd_mutex_prefix> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
