<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/parallel_apply_dispatch_path_without_manifest_identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/partial_override_silently_disables_defaults> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/partial_rollout_converged> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/partial_rollout_converged> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use the explicit state machine PENDING → APPLYING → INSTALLED_CLAIMED\n→ INSTALLED_VERIFIED → RUNTIME_VERIFIED → CONVERGED. Only emit\nCONVERGED after every required node has reached RUNTIME_VERIFIED\nvia GetServiceRuntimeProof. Anything else is PARTIAL." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/partial_rollout_converged> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mark a rollout CONVERGED when only inventory state on each node says\ninstalled=true, even though one or more nodes have not yet been\nruntime-verified (running binary hash, runtime version, effective\nsystemd unit)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/partial_rollout_converged> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/rollout.convergence_requires_runtime_proof> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/partial_rollout_converged> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
