<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/partial_write_to_final_local_path_without_atomic_rename> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pass_auth_token_as_git_command_argument_to_avoid_askpass_complexity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pass_empty_expected_sha256_to_download_without_prefetch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pass_package_tarball_sha256_as_expected_sha256> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/patch_apply_desired_to_force_an_install_dispatch_regardless_of_skip_result> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/patch_xds_or_torrent_kind_by_name_only> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/patch_xds_or_torrent_kind_by_name_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fix the kind at the source (registry.yaml) and let the projection/gate flow it everywhere. If a name-based branch seems necessary, the real bug is a missing registry-derived lookup at that site. (Closely related forbidden_fix: hardcode_package_kind_classification_outside_canonical_registry.)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/patch_xds_or_torrent_kind_by_name_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fix a kind/keyspace symptom by special-casing a package name (e.g. `if name == \"xds\"` or `== \"torrent\"`) in a downstream consumer. Patches one copy while the classification keeps being re-asserted from another — the exact multi-PR loop the registry-authority work exists to end." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/patch_xds_or_torrent_kind_by_name_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.kind_is_registry_authored_downstream_is_projection> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/patch_xds_or_torrent_kind_by_name_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/per_package_failure_threshold_constants> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/perform_destructive_action_from_inferred_intent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/perform_destructive_action_from_inferred_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every destructive action requires an explicit typed approval record; do not infer intent from missing keys, etcd timeouts, or local disk state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/perform_destructive_action_from_inferred_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Infer that a destructive action is desired from indirect signals (missing key, timeout, local disk state) rather than requiring explicit audited intent." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/perform_destructive_action_from_inferred_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_state.absence_is_not_destructive_intent> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/perform_destructive_action_from_inferred_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/destructive_actions.require_explicit_guard> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/perform_destructive_action_from_inferred_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/perform_destructive_action_from_inferred_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pkill_with_f_flag_to_stop_service> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pkill_with_f_flag_to_stop_service> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "pkill -f matches the full argv string including the parent shell's command line. In systemd ExecStartPre, the parent shell running the script matches the pattern and kills itself, aborting the install mid-flight. This was observed across 9 service spec files. Use pkill -x <binary-name> instead." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pkill_with_f_flag_to_stop_service> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "pkill -x <exact-binary-name> — matches only process name, not argv. Never pkill -f." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pkill_with_f_flag_to_stop_service> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use pkill -f <binary-name> to stop a service in ExecStartPre or install scripts." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pkill_with_f_flag_to_stop_service> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/pkill_with_f_flag_to_stop_service> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fnode_agent%2Fnode_agent_server%2Finternal%2Fsupervisor%2Fsupervisor.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/placement.remove_orphan_via_cluster_wide_desired_or_manual_rm> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/placement.remove_orphan_via_cluster_wide_desired_or_manual_rm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use a node-scoped operator entry (MCP nodeagent_uninstall_package / CLI `globular node uninstall-package --package <name> --node <ep>`) that invokes the node-agent's supervisor-mediated \"uninstall-package\" workflow on that ONE node — clears installed-state, never touches cluster desired-state. Removing an authorized package this way is self-healing (reconcile reinstalls); removing an orphan retires it." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/placement.remove_orphan_via_cluster_wide_desired_or_manual_rm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Removing a placement orphan from ONE node by (a) `globular services desired remove <name>` — cluster-wide, which retires the service on every node including those that legitimately host it — or (b) manual `systemctl stop/disable` + `rm` of the binary/unit, which bypasses the supervisor and leaves installed-state stamped, or (c) auto-removing orphans in the controller convergence loop (orphan removal is deliberately operator-gated for data safety)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/placement.remove_orphan_via_cluster_wide_desired_or_manual_rm> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.layer_has_single_writing_actor> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/placement.remove_orphan_via_cluster_wide_desired_or_manual_rm> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/placement.orphan_removal_needs_a_lawful_node_scoped_path> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/placement.remove_orphan_via_cluster_wide_desired_or_manual_rm> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/process_trusted_by_port_listening_alone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/process_trusted_by_systemd_active_alone> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/promote_weights_without_graph_rebuild> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/promote_weights_without_graph_rebuild> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "After promoting weight changes to path_weights.yaml, always rebuild and reload\nthe awareness graph to incorporate the new weights.\nVerify the ranking changes using awareness.decision_context on a known scenario." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/promote_weights_without_graph_rebuild> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Promote a weight change from a proposal into path_weights.yaml and then\nimmediately rely on the new rankings without rebuilding the graph. The graph\nreads weights at build time; live scoring uses the compiled graph, not the\nYAML directly." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/promote_weights_without_graph_rebuild> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.weight_learning.human_approval_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/promote_weights_without_graph_rebuild> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.half_done_must_not_look_done> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/promote_weights_without_graph_rebuild> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/propagate_day0_parse_error_to_caller> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/publish_dns_from_desired_or_profile_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/publish_dns_from_desired_or_profile_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Gate every service-bearing record by NodeInfo.ServiceReady which\nconsults InstalledServices (Layer 3) AND RuntimeHealthy (Layer 4)\nbefore publication. Use ComputeDesiredStateWithFunnels and emit\nWITHDREW log lines so the candidate funnel is visible." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/publish_dns_from_desired_or_profile_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compute DNS records from Profile membership only — every node\nwith profile=gateway gets an entry in gateway.<domain> regardless\nof whether the package is installed or the unit is running.\nClients hit dead endpoints on every TTL flip; new nodes appear in\nDNS before they can serve traffic; nodes whose service crashed\nsilently stay in records until the next reconcile." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/publish_dns_from_desired_or_profile_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/dns.records_must_be_installed_and_runtime_healthy> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/publish_dns_from_desired_or_profile_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/publish_local_build_as_official_stable_to_fix_mismatch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/publish_success_inferred_from_log_text> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
