<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/re_enqueueing_via_drift_reconciler_instead_of_explicit_retry_counter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_advertise_ip_without_falling_through_to_ips_list> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_advertise_ip_without_falling_through_to_ips_list> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Prefer AdvertiseIp when non-empty, otherwise fall through to the\nnodeAny<X> helpers that match against any of node.Identity.Ips with the\nVIP excluded. Until the controller populates AdvertiseIp consistently,\nAdvertiseIp-only reads produce wrong answers in real clusters." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_advertise_ip_without_falling_through_to_ips_list> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use only n.GetIdentity().GetAdvertiseIp() and treat empty as \"node has\nno usable IP\". Verified live 2026-05-10: the controller does not populate\nAdvertiseIp on any node, so this path is always-empty and produces\nfalse-positives (node not in pool → write_quorum_lost) or false-negatives\n(skip check → real violations missed)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_advertise_ip_without_falling_through_to_ips_list> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
