<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_only_mode_serves_cached_writes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Call the owner's typed RPC. For L1: repository.{ListArtifacts, GetArtifactManifest, ...}. For L2: cluster_controller.{GetDesiredState, GetServiceRelease, GetInfrastructureRelease, ...}. For L3: node_agent.{ListInstalledPackages, GetInstalledPackage, GetServiceRuntimeProof, ...}. If the typed RPC does not yet exist for the exact shape needed, ADD it on the owner (proto + handler + awareness anchor) — then call it. Do not \"temporarily\" scan etcd.\nWhen the data is needed for batch consumption (rules sweep, convergence scan), the collector pattern in cluster_doctor is the canonical shape: collector calls the typed RPCs once per sweep and populates a Snapshot; rules read the Snapshot. Adding a new Snapshot.<X> field is cheaper than adding a one-off etcd reader." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The owner's typed RPC is the canonical reader. Direct etcd reads bypass:\n  - the owner's canonicalization (e.g. controller resolves version → build_id once)\n  - the owner's in-memory state (writes not yet flushed)\n  - version contracts (gates against pre-Day-1 reads)\n  - audit attribution\nEven when the typed RPC happens to be missing for a particular shape, the answer is to add a typed RPC to the owner, not to scan etcd. Live regressions: cluster_doctor/rules/repository_dns_invariants.go and rules/package_version_authority.go both fire on every invariant evaluation and read four L2 etcd prefixes directly even though the collector has a controllerClient already dialled." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Read an etcd prefix or storage backend directly (e.g. `cli.Get(ctx, \"/globular/resources/ServiceDesiredVersion/\", ...)`) when the prefix is owned by another service. Includes scanning multiple L1/L2/L3 prefixes via the etcd client even when \"we just need the data for a moment\" or \"the owner doesn't expose a typed RPC for exactly this shape yet\"." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/etcd.path_has_single_owner> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/four_layer.truth_read_via_owner_rpc_not_direct_storage> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_controller%2Fcluster_controller_server%2Fhandlers_node.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/read_owned_etcd_prefix_directly_instead_of_calling_owner_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fcollector%2Fcollector.go> .
