<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A missing canonical value is a finding, not a recovery surface. Emit the appropriate doctor finding (MISSING_BLOB, BROKEN_MANIFEST_MISSING, DesiredBuildIdOrphaned, etc.) and stop. The operator's recovery path is to re-import from the canonical source (the original publisher, the upstream registry, the CI pipeline). Local recovery from a secondary observation is forbidden because it creates a value with no canonical attribution." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The canonical source is the only thing that defines the identity. Substituting a secondary observation creates a \"truth\" that has no audit trail, no version contract, and no way to verify. The PUBLISHED_MISSING_BLOB recovery attempt that pulled bytes from MinIO mirror and re-named them as the canonical L1 blob was exactly this shape — bytes that the publisher never signed becoming \"the same artifact\". The fix in v1.2.163 was to refuse this and require re-import from the upstream canonical source (`globular repository sync --tag vX.Y.Z`)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Argue that a missing or stale canonical identity value can be \"recovered\" from a secondary observation: if the manifest checksum is empty, hash the disk binary and treat that as the manifest checksum; if the build_id is unknown, derive one from the version string; if the manifest is missing, accept the bytes that happen to be on disk." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/identity.has_single_canonical_source_and_is_immutable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.minio_is_not_valid_package_source> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fnode_agent%2Fnode_agent_server%2Finstaller_api.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Frepository%2Frepository_server%2Fartifact_handlers.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/recompute_identity_from_secondary_source> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Frepository%2Frepository_server%2Fpublish_reconciler.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile.clear_drift_on_dispatch_ack_without_observation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile.clear_drift_on_dispatch_ack_without_observation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "After the child returns, re-read installed_state for (node_id, package_name). Clear the observation and mark SUCCEEDED only on a match; on repeated no-progress success, escalate to FAILED with reason=remediation_no_progress — never a silent SUCCEEDED loop. Distinguish converged-skip from ineligible-skip so 0 targets on a genuinely-absent package is DEFERRED/BLOCKED, not AVAILABLE." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile.clear_drift_on_dispatch_ack_without_observation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Clearing a reconcile drift observation / marking a missing_package or version_drift remediation terminal-SUCCEEDED based on the child workflow's reported status (dispatch acknowledgement or a 0-target noop finalize) rather than a fresh read of installed_state proving the package's build identity now matches desired on that node. Also forbidden: treating len(selected_targets)==0 as unconditional convergence, and silencing the re-detection loop by suppressing the missing_package emission instead of installing or escalating." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile.clear_drift_on_dispatch_ack_without_observation> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/convergence.no_infinite_retry> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile.clear_drift_on_dispatch_ack_without_observation> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile.clear_drift_on_dispatch_ack_without_observation> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/reconcile.terminal_success_requires_observed_convergence> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile.clear_drift_on_dispatch_ack_without_observation> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile_from_in_memory_snapshot_after_failover> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile_from_in_memory_snapshot_after_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "After every leader election, the reconciler must reload desired state exclusively\nfrom etcd before running any convergence tick. In-memory state from a prior\nleader session is stale by definition and must be discarded entirely." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile_from_in_memory_snapshot_after_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "After acquiring cluster leadership, load desired state from an in-memory snapshot\ncarried over from a prior leader session rather than reading fresh from etcd." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile_from_in_memory_snapshot_after_failover> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reconcile_from_in_memory_snapshot_after_failover> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
