<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reintroduce_install_package_hash_alias_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relax_require_checksum_when_mirror_lookup_lacks_sha256> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relax_require_checksum_when_mirror_lookup_lacks_sha256> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Leave require_checksum=true. If the upstream mirror genuinely\ncannot provide sha256 in its responses, treat the mirror as\nuntrusted and configure trust policy to require local-only.\nRepair the missing manifest with `repair-index` or roll the\ndesired build_id forward." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relax_require_checksum_when_mirror_lookup_lacks_sha256> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When upstream mirror lookups fail with \"require_checksum=true but\nrequest has no sha256,\" the operator flips require_checksum off\nin repository config to \"make installs proceed.\" The cluster now\ninstalls whatever bytes the mirror returns without verifying they\nmatch the desired identity. This is the canonical wrong fix for\nthe build_id orphaning cascade — the missing manifest, not the\nenforced checksum, is the actual bug." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relax_require_checksum_when_mirror_lookup_lacks_sha256> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.fallback_requires_manifest_and_checksum> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relax_require_checksum_when_mirror_lookup_lacks_sha256> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_dns_to_recover_dns> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_dns_to_recover_dns> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fix DNS at the source: reconciler gates dns.<domain> on the dns\nservice being installed AND healthy on each candidate. Bad nodes\ndrop out automatically. Do not edit records via the DNS RPC API\nas a workaround for reconciler bugs — the reconciler is the\nsource of truth and will overwrite manual changes." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_dns_to_recover_dns> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The DNS service itself is unhealthy on some nodes, so the operator\n\"fixes\" it by editing dns.<domain> records to remove the bad\nnodes. Now the DNS reconciler writes its own remediation back on\nthe next cycle because the records are computed from cluster\nstate, not from operator overrides. The records flap; clients see\nboth states in the same TTL window." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_dns_to_recover_dns> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/dns.records_must_be_installed_and_runtime_healthy> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_dns_to_recover_dns> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_entrypoint_checksum_to_catch_a_wrong_but_self_consistent_payload> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_format_json_presence_as_wipe_completion_signal> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_rpc_audit_as_substitute_for_workflow_run> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_stale_graph_after_knowledge_edit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_stale_graph_after_knowledge_edit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Check graph freshness before using decision_context.\nIf the graph is stale, rebuild and reload. Never treat stale-graph output as current guidance." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_stale_graph_after_knowledge_edit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use the awareness graph's decision paths, coverage, or blind_spots as authoritative\nguidance immediately after a knowledge YAML edit, without rebuilding the graph.\nA stale graph silently omits the newly added forbidden_fixes and invariants." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_stale_graph_after_knowledge_edit> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.knowledge.graph_rebuild_after_yaml_edit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_stale_graph_after_knowledge_edit> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rely_on_stale_graph_after_knowledge_edit> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_service_restart_without_pkill_guard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_service_restart_without_pkill_guard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Gate every service restart with an ExecStartPre kill step; the guard must run even if systemd believes the service is stopped, because cgroup-escaped orphans do not appear in systemd state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_service_restart_without_pkill_guard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Restart a service unit via systemctl or Restart=on-failure without first killing any orphaned process that escaped its cgroup and may still be holding the port." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_service_restart_without_pkill_guard> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_service_restart_without_pkill_guard> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.endpoint.cgroup_escape_guard> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_service_restart_without_pkill_guard> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.endpoint.etcd_address_reachability> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_service_restart_without_pkill_guard> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/relying_on_systemd_to_kill_processes_outside_the_cgroup> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remediation_proceeds_on_stale_evidence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_decision_edges_from_impact_kinds> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_decision_edges_from_impact_kinds> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "If an edge kind proves too noisy, add a scoring penalty instead of removing it\nfrom impactEdgeKinds. The traversal must stay complete; filtering happens in scoring." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_decision_edges_from_impact_kinds> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Remove EdgeForbids, EdgeTestedBy, EdgeRequiresTest, or EdgeEnforces from the\nimpactEdgeKinds set in impact_path.go. These are the ONLY edges that create\ndecision-domain traversal paths. Removing them causes decision_context to return\nonly information paths for all queries." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_decision_edges_from_impact_kinds> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.graph.domain_classification_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_decision_edges_from_impact_kinds> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.preflight.required_before_edit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_decision_edges_from_impact_kinds> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_ghost_voter_without_verifying_quorum_remains> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_member_on_single_timeout> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_platform_filter_entirely> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_profile_from_node_to_hide_record> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_profile_from_node_to_hide_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Preserve intended profiles and correct DNS desired/runtime reconciliation logic." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_profile_from_node_to_hide_record> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Removing node profiles to hide incorrect DNS publication instead of fixing desired DNS state and health filters." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_profile_from_node_to_hide_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/dns.records_must_be_installed_and_runtime_healthy> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/remove_profile_from_node_to_hide_record> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
