<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/rename_local_artifact_to_official_without_rebuild> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repeated_auto_restart_until_start_limit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replace_compiled_seed_match_with_live_behavioral_rpc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replace_compiled_seed_match_with_live_behavioral_rpc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Keep the compiled-seed alias match as the authority that refuses a known forbidden move — deterministic, locally available, no runtime dependency on ai-memory. A live behavioral RPC may be added later only as ADVISORY enrichment layered on top of, never replacing, the local deterministic gate." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replace_compiled_seed_match_with_live_behavioral_rpc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Replace govops's deterministic, in-process forbidden-move match (the alias set loaded from the COMPILED cluster_operator behavioral seed pack) with a live ai-memory behavioral CheckAction RPC — making refusal of a known forbidden move depend on behavioral-memory being reachable. This reopens the exact tension the Governed Operation Gateway closes: ai-memory down => the gate either fails open (loses governance) or fails closed (a supplementary service blocks deterministic control-plane operations). The forbidden spell must be carved into the gate, not a phone call to the oracle." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replace_compiled_seed_match_with_live_behavioral_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/govops_behavioral_refusal_uses_compiled_seed_not_live_rpc> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replace_compiled_seed_match_with_live_behavioral_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fail_safe_defaults_when_authority_is_uncertain> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replace_compiled_seed_match_with_live_behavioral_rpc> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replace_safejoin_with_filepath_join_plus_hasprefix> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replay_store_falls_back_to_process_local_on_etcd_error> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replay_store_silently_accepts_when_etcd_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/replayed_attestation_treated_as_live> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/report_systemd_active_as_version_ok> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/report_systemd_active_as_version_ok> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Combine systemd state with /proc/<pid>/exe hash + runtime version\nprobe before declaring version OK. Treat /proc/exe unavailable as\nUNKNOWN, not OK." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/report_systemd_active_as_version_ok> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Map systemctl is-active to a positive version health result. The\nprocess can be active and still be the wrong version (old binary\non disk; new binary on disk + old PID; binary replaced out-of-band)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/report_systemd_active_as_version_ok> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/health.must_not_use_inventory_as_runtime_truth> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/report_systemd_active_as_version_ok> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Run the owner RepairIndex operation (dry-run by default; explicit --commit to apply). It reconstitutes the index row from the existing repository-owned evidence (blob digest + sidecar manifest), verifies checksum before PUBLISHED, refuses on missing/contradictory identity, and never touches desired state. Identity and checksum come from the blob/manifest, never minted; the split is repaired at the index layer, from the blob, or not at all." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Resolving a CAS-present / index-UNKNOWN divergence by rolling desired state forward to a different build, by manually UPSERTing publish_state, or by minting a build_id / publisher / checksum — instead of repairing the index row from the on-disk blob + sidecar manifest through the repository owner. Also forbidden: promoting a blob to PUBLISHED without verifying its sidecar manifest and checksum, or auto-elevating REVOKED / QUARANTINED rows." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.cas_present_index_unknown_is_owner_repairable> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.published_requires_verified_manifest> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.repair_selects_existing_build> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/repository.roll_desired_forward_instead_of_repairing_index> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_agents_to_run_sudo_chown_through_mcp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_derived_state_before_publishing_authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_derived_state_before_publishing_authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Publish authority state (DesiredService, DesiredRelease) in a dedicated lane that does not wait for projection or cache pipelines to succeed." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_derived_state_before_publishing_authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Gate authoritative desired-state publication on the success of derived or projection pipelines. Projections are consumers of authority, not prerequisites." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_derived_state_before_publishing_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/derived_state.must_not_block_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_derived_state_before_publishing_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.critical_path_no_non_critical_dependency> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_derived_state_before_publishing_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_dns_for_dns_recovery> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_dns_for_dns_recovery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "All DNS recovery CLI commands must support --addr for direct IP:port fallback; resolve endpoints from /globular/cluster/dns/records when DNS UDP fails." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_dns_for_dns_recovery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Require hostname resolution (DNS) to run DNS repair or recovery CLI commands. DNS recovery must work via direct IP:port fallback." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_dns_for_dns_recovery> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.circular_dependency_must_have_break_glass> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_dns_for_dns_recovery> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/recovery.must_not_depend_on_dns_only> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_dns_for_dns_recovery> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_human_to_restart_controller_for_every_apply> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_human_to_restart_controller_for_every_apply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fix the watcher in code. The recovery runbook at\ndocs/operational-knowledge/runbooks/recover-stuck-topology-apply.yaml\nexists as a transitional aid, not a permanent contract." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_human_to_restart_controller_for_every_apply> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Document \"restart all controllers in sequence after every objectstore\napply\" as the canonical operations procedure, instead of fixing the\nwatcher. Acceptable only as a temporary runbook entry; ossifying it as\nthe design is the forbidden fix." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_human_to_restart_controller_for_every_apply> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/convergence.no_infinite_retry> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_human_to_restart_controller_for_every_apply> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/objectstore.topology_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_human_to_restart_controller_for_every_apply> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_service_discovery_when_discovery_is_unhealthy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_service_discovery_when_discovery_is_unhealthy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Provide --direct-ip or --addr options in all CLI recovery commands; fall back to Tier-0 host lists (GetMinioHosts/GetScyllaHosts) from etcd." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_service_discovery_when_discovery_is_unhealthy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Require service-discovery lookup when discovery itself is part of the failure being recovered from. Recovery paths must support direct endpoint configuration." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_service_discovery_when_discovery_is_unhealthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.circular_dependency_must_have_break_glass> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_service_discovery_when_discovery_is_unhealthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/recovery.must_not_depend_on_dns_only> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_service_discovery_when_discovery_is_unhealthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_systemd_unit_for_command_package> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_systemd_unit_for_command_package> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Check package.kind before requiring a systemd unit; COMMAND packages never require a unit; only SERVICE and INFRASTRUCTURE packages do." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/require_systemd_unit_for_command_package> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Expect COMMAND-type packages (yt-dlp, rclone, sha256sum, globular-cli) to have a systemd unit and flag them as runtime-mismatch if no unit exists." .
