<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/restore_dist_bin_as_long_lived_authority_path> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/restore_format_json_without_topology_fingerprint_guard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/restore_manifest_profiles_as_runtime_placement_authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/restore_manifest_profiles_as_runtime_placement_authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Resolve placement exclusively from the catalog (placementAllows / ProfilesForPackage). Treat manifest profiles as informational; if they must be made trustworthy, DERIVE them from the catalog at build time (a future, explicit policy) — never consume manifest profiles for placement decisions." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/restore_manifest_profiles_as_runtime_placement_authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Make the artifact manifest's `profiles` field a runtime placement input again — e.g. having platform-upgrade evaluate, the drift-reconciler, the release reconciler, or cluster-doctor read manifest.profiles to decide where a package may run. The component catalog (CatalogByName / component_catalog.ProfilesForPackage) is the SINGLE placement authority (E1/E2); manifest profiles are informational metadata only. Reintroducing manifest profiles as a placement input recreates the two-law-books split that caused the torrent orphan (manifest said [core,compute] / null while the catalog said [compute] / [control-plane])." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/restore_manifest_profiles_as_runtime_placement_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/publish.manifest_profiles_must_not_contradict_catalog> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/restore_manifest_profiles_as_runtime_placement_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_day0_import_on_partial_success> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_dependent_services_indefinitely_without_checking_scylla_gate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_install_blindly> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_install_blindly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Before retrying, check whether installed-state already exists in etcd (idempotency check); classify the failure type; apply FailureClass-based retry policy with a capped number of attempts." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_install_blindly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Retry a failed install action on every reconcile tick without checking whether the failure is deterministic or whether the installed state was partially committed." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_install_blindly> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/convergence.no_infinite_retry> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_install_blindly> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/install.result.atomic_commit> .
