<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/retry_sync_with_different_target_platform_to_catch_noarch_entries> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_NotFound_for_yanked_revoked_or_archived_manifests> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_NotFound_for_yanked_revoked_or_archived_manifests> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Return codes.FailedPrecondition with prefix DesiredBuildIdOrphaned\nwhen the manifest exists but is not installable. Include the live\npublish_state / artifact_state in the error message so the caller\n(and doctor) can classify. Reserve NotFound for the case where the\nmanifest is genuinely absent from the catalog." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_NotFound_for_yanked_revoked_or_archived_manifests> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "resolveByBuildID returns codes.NotFound when the manifest exists\nbut its publish_state is YANKED/REVOKED/ARCHIVED/QUARANTINED.\nThe node-agent installer interprets NotFound as \"build absent →\ntry local fallback,\" and installs a pinned tarball even though\nthe repository has explicitly demoted the build. The cluster ends\nup running a build the repository said \"stop on.\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_NotFound_for_yanked_revoked_or_archived_manifests> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.desired_build_id_must_resolve> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_NotFound_for_yanked_revoked_or_archived_manifests> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.fallback_requires_manifest_and_checksum> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_NotFound_for_yanked_revoked_or_archived_manifests> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_all_invariants_for_every_task_without_filtering> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_bare_no_match_without_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_bare_no_match_without_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always return coverage and blind_spots regardless of whether decision paths exist.\nThe consumer must be able to determine WHY there are no paths (not checked vs.\nchecked clean vs. graph unavailable)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_bare_no_match_without_coverage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Return a bare NO_MATCH response from awareness.decision_context without including\nthe coverage map (graph, runtime, code_scan, raw_yaml) and blind_spots list.\nNO_MATCH without coverage context silently implies safety, which is wrong." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_bare_no_match_without_coverage> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.mcp.decision_context_no_bare_no_match> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_bare_no_match_without_coverage> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_bare_no_match_without_coverage> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
