<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_internal_for_legitimate_empty_payload> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_nil_for_err_after_failed_dial> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/return_semantic_path_without_explanation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_build_id_for_new_artifact> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_in_memory_plan_after_leader_failover> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_in_memory_plan_after_leader_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In-memory plans are not durable. They cannot survive failover. The only fix is to persist the plan before execution, not to \"be careful.\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_in_memory_plan_after_leader_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Workflows persist intent in etcd; the new leader picks up the workflow run-id and resumes. No leader-local execution state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_in_memory_plan_after_leader_failover> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Continue executing an in-memory plan after a leader failover" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_in_memory_plan_after_leader_failover> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.competing_writers_must_converge_or_be_fenced> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_in_memory_plan_after_leader_failover> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/reuse_in_memory_plan_after_leader_failover> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
