<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/secret_keyword_check_removed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/select_latest_to_hide_collision> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/sentinel_principle_imposes_situational_gates_on_unrelated_actions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/sentinel_principle_imposes_situational_gates_on_unrelated_actions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The condition.always sentinel grants reach to the FORBIDDEN-MOVE check only. A principle drives the situational gates only when ENGAGED: the caller declared one of its applies_when conditions, OR its forbidden move matched the proposed action. A principle reached only via the sentinel whose forbidden move did not match stays in scope for forbidden-matching (so the universal rule still blocks its own action) but contributes nothing to evidence / authority / risk gates. Compute `governed` from the engaged set, not mere applicability, so an unrelated always-applicable rule being in scope is not reported as governance of this action. See golang/ai_memory/behavioral/core/runtime.go CheckAction (the \"engaged\" set and applicablePromotedPrinciples' declared-vs-sentinel distinction) and tests TestCheckActionSentinelOnlyDoesNotOverBlock / TestCheckActionDeclaredConditionEngagesGates." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/sentinel_principle_imposes_situational_gates_on_unrelated_actions> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Let an always-applicable behavioral principle (one promoted under the condition.always sentinel) drive the situational gates — required-evidence, authority-resolvability, and risk/human-approval — for EVERY action in the domain, because it is \"applicable\". A single high-risk universal rule then forces needs_human_approval (or needs_evidence) on unrelated actions: e.g. a never-hot-swap rule blocking a read-only inspect_service_logs, locking up the AI tier's automated remediation. Observed live after the first principle was promoted (ai-memory 1.2.235): every cluster_operator check_action returned needs_human_approval." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/sentinel_principle_imposes_situational_gates_on_unrelated_actions> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.absence_scope_must_be_explicit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/sentinel_principle_imposes_situational_gates_on_unrelated_actions> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.assertions_must_carry_their_scope> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/sentinel_principle_imposes_situational_gates_on_unrelated_actions> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.failure_response_must_contract_not_amplify> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/sentinel_principle_imposes_situational_gates_on_unrelated_actions> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/service_registered_with_empty_dependencies> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/set_causal_rule_confidence_high_without_verification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/set_causal_rule_confidence_high_without_verification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use confidence: low for first-observed chains, confidence: medium after 2-3\nconfirmed recurrences, confidence: high only after the chain has been validated\nacross multiple independent incidents and multiple operator environments." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/set_causal_rule_confidence_high_without_verification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Set confidence: high on a causal rule that has only been observed once or only\nin a controlled test environment. High confidence rules are presented to operators\nas established fact, not hypothesis." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/set_causal_rule_confidence_high_without_verification> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.knowledge.causal_rules_evidence_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/set_causal_rule_confidence_high_without_verification> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/set_causal_rule_confidence_high_without_verification> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/share_format_json_across_drives_to_simplify_backup> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silence_data_guard_by_deleting_admitted_disk_entry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_on_partial_fetch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_on_partial_fetch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Collect per-source errors and surface them in a typed `PartialResponse{Items, Failures []SourceError}` shape, OR refuse to return any result if any source failed. The choice depends on consumer expectations — but it must NEVER be silent." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_on_partial_fetch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Batched or parallel fetch discards per-source errors with `_, _ := f()` and aggregates the survivors as if all sources succeeded. Consumer cannot tell whether the response is the complete authoritative answer or a partial view minus the failed sources." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_on_partial_fetch> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_on_partial_fetch> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_on_partial_fetch> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_unparseable_authority_entry> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_unparseable_authority_entry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Increment a typed counter (`ListServicesResponse.SkippedCount`, `SkippedReasons []string`) so the consumer can detect the partial response. Log the skipped key + parse error at WARN level so an operator can find and repair the corrupt entry." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_unparseable_authority_entry> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "`json.Marshal`/`json.Unmarshal` failure on a single registry entry is silently skipped from the response set with no error indication. Consumer sees a shorter list with no diagnostic." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_unparseable_authority_entry> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_drop_unparseable_authority_entry> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "At the moment of switchover, emit service.silent_fallback_active\n(degraded severity) with { service, dependency, fallback_mode,\nprimary_error, affected_paths, node_id, since }. The fallback path\nkeeps the request alive; the finding ensures the operator knows." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fall back from a primary dependency (MinIO, repository, DNS, cache)\nto a local / memory / read-only substitute without emitting a\ndegraded finding. The user-facing path stays alive but the cluster\nappears green while replication, indexing, or persistence are silently\nbroken." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/fallback.must_emit_degraded_finding> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback_to_latest_version_when_build_id_is_pinned> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback_to_latest_version_when_build_id_is_pinned> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When a pinned build_id fails to resolve, surface the failure as\nRELEASE_BLOCKED_REPOSITORY_ORPHANED_BUILD_ID. The controller\nhalts the release until either the repository is repaired or\ndesired state is explicitly rolled forward by an operator. No\nsilent version drift." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback_to_latest_version_when_build_id_is_pinned> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The resolver returns \"build_id not found\" so the caller \"helpfully\"\nfalls back to ResolveArtifact with no build_id, picking up the\nlatest published build instead. The cluster silently installs the\nwrong version everywhere; the pinned build_id in desired state\nbecomes a decorative annotation that nobody enforces." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback_to_latest_version_when_build_id_is_pinned> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback_to_latest_version_when_build_id_is_pinned> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.desired_build_id_must_resolve> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silent_fallback_to_latest_version_when_build_id_is_pinned> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_advance_failed_release_to_available_when_child_workflows_succeed> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_coerce_unknown_package_kind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_coerce_unknown_package_kind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A package with a metadata/ dir but no registry entry must FAIL the identity gate (registry is the index — add the entry). Runtime fail-open to SERVICE for genuinely third-party names is allowed ONLY where explicitly documented, and must be logged, never silent." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_coerce_unknown_package_kind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When a package is absent from registry.yaml, silently coerce it to a default kind (e.g. force SERVICE) and proceed, hiding that the package is unregistered." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_coerce_unknown_package_kind> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/package.kind_is_registry_authored_downstream_is_projection> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_coerce_unknown_package_kind> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_fall_back_to_localhost_when_etcd_unreachable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_fall_back_to_temp_directory> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_ignore_illegal_transition_instead_of_reject> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Orphaned artifacts were explicitly demoted. The desired build_id still pins them but they are not installable. Installing from a local cache bypasses the repository's demotion decision, propagates revoked or corrupted code, and hides the fact that desired state needs to be rolled forward." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Return FailedPrecondition with \"DesiredBuildIdOrphaned\" prefix. Surface as a structured release blocker. Operator must roll desired state forward or run repair-index." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Allow an install to proceed using a locally cached artifact when the repository reports the build is orphaned (ARCHIVED/YANKED/REVOKED/QUARANTINED/CORRUPTED)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.desired_build_id_is_hard_reachability_root> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_orphaned_artifact_from_local_fallback> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Frepository%2Frepository_server%2Fresolver.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_install_pinned_tarball_when_manifest_missing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_overwrite_drift_without_doctor_finding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_pick_first_build_id_match> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_prefer_env_var_when_set> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_prefer_env_var_when_set> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "There is no env var override — etcd is the only source. Service config\ncode does not consult the environment for cluster addresses. Period." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_prefer_env_var_when_set> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When BOTH an env var and an etcd key are present for an endpoint, return\nthe env var without logging the divergence. Two nodes with identical\nGlobular config behave differently because one has the env var set, and\nthe difference is invisible until a user reports asymmetric behaviour." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_prefer_env_var_when_set> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_prefer_env_var_when_set> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.endpoint.etcd_address_reachability> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_prefer_env_var_when_set> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_reinstalling_operator_removed_packages> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_remove_flag_on_doctor_finding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_remove_flag_on_doctor_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Day-1 finalize atomically clears the flag as its LAST step. On controller\nstartup, if day1_phase == ready AND flag present: log critical, refuse\nloopback RPCs, emit the finding. Investigation is required — silent\nauto-remediation of a security boundary is not." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_remove_flag_on_doctor_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have the doctor finding bootstrap.flag_persists_post_day_1 trigger an\nautomatic deletion of /var/lib/globular/bootstrap.enabled so the warning\nclears. Hides a security regression behind a self-healing illusion and\nmasks crashes in the day-1 finalize path." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_remove_flag_on_doctor_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.quorum_is_quality_not_constraint> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_remove_flag_on_doctor_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_remove_flag_on_doctor_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_return_actual_hash_as_proof_when_no_expected_was_provided> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_skip_dep_block_writes_when_a_concurrent_dep_active_signal_is_pending> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_swallow_permission_denied_in_audit_log> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_swallow_permission_denied_in_audit_log> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every denied write to a seed entry is logged at WARN with principal id +\nentry id. The audit trail is the only way to discover an attacker\nprobing the immutability layer or a misconfigured tool repeatedly hitting\nthe rejection." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_swallow_permission_denied_in_audit_log> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When a non-seeder principal is denied mutation of a seed entry, return\nthe error to the caller but skip the audit log entry or downgrade it\nbelow WARN — to avoid log noise from \"expected\" denials." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_swallow_permission_denied_in_audit_log> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_swallow_permission_denied_in_audit_log> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ops_knowledge.seed_integrity> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_swallow_permission_denied_in_audit_log> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/silently_upgrade_over_local_override_without_warning> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/single_global_threshold_for_all_action_classes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_apply_request_processing_when_watch_died> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_apply_request_processing_when_watch_died> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Re-establish the watch as described in the apply-watcher recovery\npattern. The drain-on-startup path is for cold start, not for missed\nevents — runtime recovery must not depend on operator restart." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_apply_request_processing_when_watch_died> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When the apply-watcher goroutine has died, leave queued apply_request\nkeys in etcd unprocessed and rely on a future controller restart to drain\nthem. This is the current bug — apply requests sit for hours until a\nhuman notices and restarts the controller." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_apply_request_processing_when_watch_died> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/objectstore.topology_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_apply_request_processing_when_watch_died> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_approval_token_jti_replay_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_approval_token_jti_replay_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Store consumed JTIs in etcd with TTL = token.exp + 5m. CheckJTIReplay must read from etcd (not in-memory only) so the blacklist survives leader failover." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_approval_token_jti_replay_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Without JTI replay checking, an approval token can be replayed after a doctor leader failover. The new leader has no memory of previously consumed tokens and will re-authorize the same action, enabling double-execution or deliberate replay attacks." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_approval_token_jti_replay_check> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Skip the JTI replay guard when validating an approval token, relying only on the token signature and expiry check." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/skip_approval_token_jti_replay_check> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.binding_outlives_evidence_until_invalidated> .
