<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/solve_convergence_by_deleting_desired_pins> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/special_case_keepalived_master_as_an_exception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/special_case_keepalived_master_as_an_exception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One unified helper — StableIP(clusterVIP) — removes the VIP regardless\nof which node holds it. No consumer needs to know about keepalived state;\nthe helper is the abstraction." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/special_case_keepalived_master_as_an_exception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Branch every Ips-consuming code path on \"is this node the keepalived\nmaster?\" and use different selection logic for the master. Doubles the\nsurface area and leaks keepalived state into every consumer." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/special_case_keepalived_master_as_an_exception> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/special_case_late_joining_nodes_without_fixing_state_split> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/staleness_implicit_in_authority_response> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/staleness_implicit_in_authority_response> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Include `ResponseFreshness{ServedBy: leader|follower, SnapshotAt, StaleAfter}` in every authority response. Followers stamp their own `SnapshotAt`; consumers reject answers older than `StaleAfter` for write-side decisions." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/staleness_implicit_in_authority_response> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Authority RPC returns a value plus a `LastSeen` field but no explicit staleness contract on the wire. A follower controller serving from a drifted snapshot returns the same response shape as a leader serving fresh state." .
