<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/substitute_convergence_hash_for_binary_checksum_when_latter_empty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Refuse the operation when expected_sha256 is empty (the upstream pipeline should have stamped it); never alias another subject's identity into it. INC-2026-0014 was the controller-side instance." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/substitute_convergence_hash_for_binary_checksum_when_latter_empty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Same shape, distinct meaning. The empty-identity case is information — it says \"I don't have a binary identity\" — and must be preserved as such." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/substitute_convergence_hash_for_binary_checksum_when_latter_empty> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Substitute a convergence-identity hash for a binary-identity checksum when the binary identity is empty" .
