<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_installer_mirror_assets_as_release_source_of_truth> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always treat packages/registry.yaml and services/webroot as the release source of truth; installer mirrors are downstream projections validated by scripts/validate-package-authority.py, never authored or trusted independently." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_installer_mirror_assets_as_release_source_of_truth> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat globular-installer's mirrored packagecatalog/webroot assets as if they were the source of truth for a release, instead of packages/registry.yaml and services/webroot, which are the real upstream authorities the mirrors are generated from." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_installer_mirror_assets_as_release_source_of_truth> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repo.release_wrapper_is_not_install_execution_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_installer_mirror_assets_as_release_source_of_truth> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_invalid_spec_as_disable_intent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_invalid_spec_as_disable_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reject specs that fail schema or checksum validation; treat them as absent; only a valid ExplicitDisable spec with matching generation and signed reason stops the runtime." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_invalid_spec_as_disable_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Accept a spec that fails schema validation or checksum as a valid disable-intent and stop the runtime. Invalid specs must be ignored; LKG must be held." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_invalid_spec_as_disable_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_state.absence_is_not_destructive_intent> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_invalid_spec_as_disable_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/destructive_actions.require_explicit_guard> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_invalid_spec_as_disable_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.absence_scope_must_be_explicit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_invalid_spec_as_disable_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_absence_as_global_absence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_absence_as_global_absence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Absence has scope (the absence-scope principle, now the negative twin of assertions_must_carry_their_scope). Local-not-found isn't global- doesn't-exist." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_absence_as_global_absence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Before destructive action, consult the owning authority for the cluster-wide view. If the authority is unreachable, the action MUST refuse (not proceed on the local view)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_absence_as_global_absence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat \"this node doesn't see X\" as \"X doesn't exist anywhere\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_absence_as_global_absence> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.absence_scope_must_be_explicit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_absence_as_global_absence> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.assertions_must_carry_their_scope> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_absence_as_global_absence> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_local_override_as_normal_drift> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_env_file_as_authoritative_topology_source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_mirror_as_package_source_under_checksum_guard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_mirror_as_package_source_under_checksum_guard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The architectural rule is about WHICH storage is authoritative for package content, not about whether a particular read happens to be cryptographically safe. Even a perfectly checksum-verified read from MinIO mints a code path where MinIO is a valid package source — exactly the rule MinIO violates. Future contributors look at the checksum guard and conclude \"mirror reads are safe\", entrenching the drift. The integrity check is a separate concern from the authority surface; they must both be satisfied independently." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_mirror_as_package_source_under_checksum_guard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use the upstream-import path (see heal_published_artifacts_from_minio_mirror safe_alternative). Cryptographic verification is necessary but not sufficient — the source must also be an architecturally valid authority." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_mirror_as_package_source_under_checksum_guard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Argue that reading package bytes from MinIO is acceptable as long as the bytes are verified against the manifest's expected checksum before write." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_mirror_as_package_source_under_checksum_guard> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.minio_is_not_valid_package_source> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_mirror_as_package_source_under_checksum_guard> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_minio_mirror_as_package_source_under_checksum_guard> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Frepository%2Frepository_server%2Fpublish_reconciler.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_expected_checksum_as_success> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_key_as_delete_intent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_key_as_delete_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When a desired-state key is absent, restore from registry-defined default or LKG; emit a doctor alert; never delete the runtime based on key absence alone." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_key_as_delete_intent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Interpret the absence of a desired-state key as an intention to delete the corresponding runtime state. Missing key must trigger restoration, not deletion." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_key_as_delete_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_state.absence_is_not_destructive_intent> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_key_as_delete_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_state.deletion_requires_audited_intent> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_key_as_delete_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.absence_scope_must_be_explicit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_key_as_delete_intent> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_missing_receipt_as_implicit_success> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_no_match_as_safe_for_high_risk_files> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_no_match_as_safe_for_high_risk_files> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "When decision_context returns NO_MATCH: check coverage.graph (not_checked vs.\nchecked_clean), check blind_spots, and if the graph is fresh, check whether the\ninvariants governing those files have forbidden_fixes and required_tests defined." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_no_match_as_safe_for_high_risk_files> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat a NO_MATCH result from awareness.decision_context as evidence that an edit\nis safe for high-risk files. NO_MATCH means the graph has no paths — it does NOT\nmean no risk exists. The graph may be stale, the files may be unindexed, or the\nrelevant invariants may not have been added yet." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_no_match_as_safe_for_high_risk_files> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.mcp.decision_context_no_bare_no_match> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_no_match_as_safe_for_high_risk_files> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_no_match_as_safe_for_high_risk_files> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_node_scoped_finding_as_cluster_scoped> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_node_scoped_finding_as_cluster_scoped> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Split the cache by scope (lookup-cache accepts any scope; delta- authority is cluster-wide only). See cluster_doctor commit c574dfe5." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_node_scoped_finding_as_cluster_scoped> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The cache contract is scoped to cluster-wide changes; node-scope findings violate the contract and amplify into noise." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_node_scoped_finding_as_cluster_scoped> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Feed node-scoped doctor findings into a cluster-wide delta cache" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_node_scoped_finding_as_cluster_scoped> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.assertions_must_carry_their_scope> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/treat_node_scoped_finding_as_cluster_scoped> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
