<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_all_artifacts_from_known_cluster_without_digest_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_archive_entry_names> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_gate_bypassed_in_live_execution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_installed_state_without_hash> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_installed_state_without_hash> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "After payload extraction and before WriteInstalledPackage(Status=installed),\nsha256 the deployed binary and compare to expected_sha256 from the\nartifact manifest. On mismatch / missing, write Status=failed_binary_hash_mismatch\nwith structured evidence (expected/actual/path/build_id/apply_run_id) and\nreturn Ok=false to the workflow. See verifyInstalledBinaryHash in\napply_package_verify.go." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_installed_state_without_hash> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mark a package \"installed\" in etcd before verifying that the deployed\nbinary on disk hashes to the expected artifact manifest digest. The\napply path may have extracted nothing, extracted the wrong bytes, or\nskipped the replace step — none of which fail systemctl restart." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_installed_state_without_hash> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/diagnostics.must_measure_reality> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_installed_state_without_hash> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_inventory_for_version_health> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_inventory_for_version_health> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Require all four layers to agree before emitting OK: desired build ==\ninstalled binary hash == running process hash == runtime version.\nIf any part is unavailable for a required service, the result is\nUNKNOWN (degraded), not OK." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_inventory_for_version_health> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Report `version:<service> ok=true` from a desired-vs-inventory\ncomparison alone. Both values are CLAIMS recorded by the apply path\nand the controller — neither proves the running process is the\nexpected build." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_inventory_for_version_health> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/health.must_not_use_inventory_as_runtime_truth> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_inventory_for_version_health> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_inventory_for_version_health> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_node_by_ip_without_certificate_check> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemctl_show_without_diffing_template> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemctl_show_without_diffing_template> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ServiceRuntimeProof.SystemdUnitSha256 is the hash of the on-disk\nunit file. Compare it to the rendered template hash recorded at\ninstall time; on drift, emit systemd.effective_config_drift." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemctl_show_without_diffing_template> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Use `systemctl show` to read effective unit properties and assume\nthey match the rendered template without diffing. The unit file on\ndisk may have been edited out-of-band; the rendered template hash\nis the source of truth." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemctl_show_without_diffing_template> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/systemd.effective_unit_must_match_rendered_unit> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemctl_show_without_diffing_template> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemd_active_as_healthy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemd_active_as_healthy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Read the MainPID from systemctl show, deref /proc/<pid>/exe, sha256\nthe resulting path, and compare to the artifact manifest digest. Use\nGetServiceRuntimeProof (node_agent) for this — do not roll your own." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemd_active_as_healthy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Treat `systemctl is-active = active` as proof that the service is\nrunning the expected build. systemd reports active for any process\nthat completed its ExecStart, regardless of which binary's bytes are\nactually executing — including a process that escaped its cgroup and\nholds the old port, or a process whose binary on disk was replaced\nafter the last restart." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemd_active_as_healthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/diagnostics.must_measure_reality> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemd_active_as_healthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/rollout.convergence_requires_runtime_proof> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trust_systemd_active_as_healthy> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/trusting_tcp_connect_as_proof_of_service_identity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ui.fix.accept_last_arriving_response_as_latest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/ui.fix.ai_invents_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
