<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_global_circuit_breaker_for_all_services> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_global_shared_hmac_secret_for_jwt_validation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_installable_latest_resolver_for_repair> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_localhost_server_name_for_cluster_dial> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_loopback_for_minio_endpoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_loopback_for_minio_endpoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Loopback is not routable across the cluster. Remote MinIO clients cannot reach the endpoint, config becomes machine-local instead of cluster-coordinated, and etcd-stored configuration becomes node-specific. minio_config.go explicitly refuses loopback (\"rule: no 127.0.0.1/localhost, ever\")." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_loopback_for_minio_endpoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Use cluster FQDN or stable cluster IP that resolves correctly from all nodes." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_loopback_for_minio_endpoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Configure MinIO endpoint as 127.0.0.1 or localhost for any cluster-visible connection." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_loopback_for_minio_endpoint> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_loopback_for_minio_endpoint> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fconfig%2Fminio_config.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_node_scope_findings_for_cluster_delta> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_node_scope_findings_for_cluster_delta> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Node-scoped findings vary per-node per-call. Feeding them into the cluster-delta cache causes them to appear \"new\" on every sweep, generating phantom events at 100+/min. Root cause of INC-2026-0004 (100+ false doctor incidents). Commit a821e0fa fixed production; cache separation is the architectural invariant." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_node_scope_findings_for_cluster_delta> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Only cluster-scoped findings (with cluster_id set) contribute to lastEmittedFindings and delta computation. Node-scoped findings are stored in lastFindings for lookup only." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_node_scope_findings_for_cluster_delta> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Include node-scoped findings in the lastEmittedFindings cache used for cluster-level delta event computation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_node_scope_findings_for_cluster_delta> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_node_scope_findings_for_cluster_delta> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fexecutor.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_node_scope_findings_for_cluster_delta> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_doctor%2Fcluster_doctor_server%2Fserver.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_primaryip_for_etcd_endpoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_primaryip_for_pool_membership> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_primaryip_for_scylla_hosts> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_raw_artifact_digest_as_desired_hash> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_string_prefix_as_authority_boundary_without_cleaning> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Two acceptable implementations: (a) Use /proc/<pid>/exe mtime (os.Stat) as the anchor when constructing the\n    record — this is what self_hosted_runtime_proof_writer.go does for the\n    services on the selfHostedServiceNames allowlist (node-agent,\n    cluster-controller, cluster-doctor, repository).\n(b) When a downstream writer (e.g. heartbeat.go Phase 2) merges into an\n    existing record for a self-hosted service, PRESERVE existing.UpdatedUnix\n    — do not overwrite the proof writer's anchor with time.Now(). The proof\n    writer is the authority for these fields; the heartbeat must be observer-\n    only with respect to the timestamp anchors." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wall-clock anchoring causes permanent service.old_pid_after_upgrade findings. The verifier compares the installed timestamp against the running PID's mtime. If InstalledUnix > process start time, the verifier concludes the running binary is older than the installed record — which looks like an upgrade that didn't restart. This was INC-2026-0016. The proof-anchor-stomp variant (heartbeat Phase 2 overwriting the proof writer's PID-anchored UpdatedUnix with time.Now()) was observed 2026-06-04 on cluster-controller after the v1.2.151 deploy and is the same forbidden fix — different write site." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Anchor InstalledUnix or UpdatedUnix in the installed package proof to wall-clock time (time.Now()) instead of the process start time from /proc/<pid>/exe mtime." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/infra.heartbeat_observer_only_not_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fnode_agent%2Fnode_agent_server%2Fheartbeat.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/use_wall_clock_for_installed_unix_timestamp> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fnode_agent%2Fnode_agent_server%2Fself_hosted_runtime_proof_writer.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/using_non_root_pkill_without_plus_prefix> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/validate_globular_annotations_inside_test_fixtures> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/validate_globular_annotations_inside_test_fixtures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Skip all _test.go files in the annotation scanner; in non-test files, exclude annotations inside raw string literals identified via AST traversal." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/validate_globular_annotations_inside_test_fixtures> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The annotation validator must not treat //globular: strings inside _test.go fixtures or raw test strings as production annotations." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/validate_globular_annotations_inside_test_fixtures> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/awareness.annotation_scanner.production_source_only> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/validate_globular_annotations_inside_test_fixtures> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.assertions_must_carry_their_scope> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/validate_globular_annotations_inside_test_fixtures> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/verification_skipped_on_override> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wake_resets_defer_counter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/watcher_queries_scylla_directly_or_auto_promotes_probe_finding> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/watcher_queries_scylla_directly_or_auto_promotes_probe_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Source group0 truth from the owning authority — the infra-probe truth plane (and, longer term, a first-class group0 voter count exposed there). The watcher interprets that truth as a DIAGNOSTIC_CLAIM finding that cites the truth-plane ref; it never owns truth-plane authority. Probe findings enter behavioral-memory as RAW_SIGNAL + evidence only and are promoted, if ever, through the human-gated promotion path." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/watcher_queries_scylla_directly_or_auto_promotes_probe_finding> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Make ai_watcher detect Scylla group0 quorum by querying Scylla directly (gocql / nodetool / system.raft_group0_members), or have a watcher probe finding auto-promote into an AWG invariant or behavioral principle without human review." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/watcher_queries_scylla_directly_or_auto_promotes_probe_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/watcher_queries_scylla_directly_or_auto_promotes_probe_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/scylla.group0_stale_voter_blocks_schema_mutations> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/watcher_queries_scylla_directly_or_auto_promotes_probe_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/scylladb.group0_voter_quorum_must_hold> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/watcher_queries_scylla_directly_or_auto_promotes_probe_finding> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_bootstrap_ttl_to_avoid_re_creation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_bootstrap_ttl_to_avoid_re_creation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The TTL is intentionally tight — bootstrap mode authorises unauthenticated\nloopback RPCs and must close fast. Fix the slow path that recreates the\nflag instead of widening the window. If a join truly needs > 30 min,\nthat's a separate failure mode to triage." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_bootstrap_ttl_to_avoid_re_creation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Extend the 30-minute bootstrap-flag TTL to hours or days so the flag\ndoesn't get re-created during slow joins. Trades a real-time security\nboundary for cosmetic convenience." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_bootstrap_ttl_to_avoid_re_creation> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.quorum_is_quality_not_constraint> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_bootstrap_ttl_to_avoid_re_creation> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_seeder_role_to_admin> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_seeder_role_to_admin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Reject every write to seed entries unless principal is exactly \"seeder\".\nAdmin sessions that need to alter operational knowledge re-author the\nYAML in the bundle, rebuild, reinstall, and re-run the seeder workflow." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_seeder_role_to_admin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grant the 'admin' role permission to UPDATE/DELETE entries with\nprovenance.source=seed, so admin-driven workflows can mutate seed\nentries directly. Removes the immutability boundary that protects\noperational knowledge from poisoning." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_seeder_role_to_admin> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_seeder_role_to_admin> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/ops_knowledge.seed_integrity> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_seeder_role_to_admin> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_to_other_env_vars_to_be_consistent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_to_other_env_vars_to_be_consistent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Consistency is achieved by removing every env-var fallback, not adding\nmore. There is one path: etcd. New services follow that pattern; the\nexisting offender is the bug to fix." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_to_other_env_vars_to_be_consistent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Once one service uses os.Getenv() for its address, \"for consistency\" make\nall the others do the same. Compounds a single rule violation into a\ncluster-wide drift surface." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_to_other_env_vars_to_be_consistent> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.endpoint.etcd_address_reachability> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/widen_to_other_env_vars_to_be_consistent> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_minio_sys_without_approved_transition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_minio_sys_without_approved_transition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Only wipe .minio.sys through a controller-approved workflow transition with an explicit generation-matched approval marker; verify quorum viability before proceeding." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_minio_sys_without_approved_transition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wipe the MinIO .minio.sys directory or reset erasure-coded pool metadata without going through an approved cluster transition workflow." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_minio_sys_without_approved_transition> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_minio_sys_without_approved_transition> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/objectstore.topology_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_minio_sys_without_approved_transition> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_scylla_data_automatically> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_scylla_data_on_verified_healthy_node> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_scylla_data_on_verified_healthy_node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Only wipe nodes that have never successfully joined (ScyllaWasEverVerified=false). For verified nodes, use scylla-manager decommission workflow instead." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_scylla_data_on_verified_healthy_node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Verified nodes have replicated cluster data. Wiping destroys that data and causes unavailability. The scylla_members.go wipe gate is explicit: wipe only when ScyllaJoinRestarts >= 1 AND ScyllaWasEverVerified=false. \"This node was previously verified — ScyllaWasEverVerified will gate the wipe and prevent data loss.\"" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_scylla_data_on_verified_healthy_node> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wipe /var/lib/scylla/data on a node that has ScyllaWasEverVerified=true." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_scylla_data_on_verified_healthy_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_scylla_data_on_verified_healthy_node> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fcluster_controller%2Fcluster_controller_server%2Fscylla_members.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_state_without_approved_transition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_state_without_approved_transition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wipe persistent state only through a controller-approved workflow with a transition record matching the current generation; node-agent verifies before proceeding." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_state_without_approved_transition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Wipe persistent state (MinIO .minio.sys, ScyllaDB data directory, etcd snapshots) without a controller-approved transition record for the correct generation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_state_without_approved_transition> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/destructive_actions.require_explicit_guard> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_state_without_approved_transition> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_state_without_approved_transition> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/topology.reconciler_must_respect_safety_contract> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/wipe_state_without_approved_transition> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.restart_before_control_plane_stable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.restart_before_control_plane_stable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Stabilize in order: etcd, then controller, then workflow. Restarting workflow before the control plane is ready will immediately re-fail." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.restart_before_control_plane_stable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Restarting the workflow service or retrying workflow steps while etcd and controller\nare unstable causes immediate re-failure: the new dispatch attempt also times out\nbecause the control plane cannot serve it. Resolve etcd → controller → then workflow." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.restart_before_control_plane_stable> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.restart_before_control_plane_stable> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.treat_as_root_cause> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.treat_as_root_cause> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Treat workflow timeouts as a symptom, not the root cause; diagnose etcd and controller first; workflow recovers automatically once the control plane is healthy." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.treat_as_root_cause> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Workflow dispatch timeouts are always a terminal symptom of control-plane instability.\nThe correct fix order is: etcd → controller → workflow. Fixing or restarting the\nworkflow service first will not unblock it — it will re-fail immediately because the\nunderlying etcd/controller issue is unresolved." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.treat_as_root_cause> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.silence_is_not_valid_for_unexpected> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow.treat_as_root_cause> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow_disagrees_with_doctor_on_threshold> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow_run_id_dropped_at_doctor_boundary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow_succeeded_when_finding_still_active> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/workflow_succeeded_without_verify_step_running> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_critical_key_without_registered_owner> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_critical_key_without_registered_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Register all critical-key owners in critical_state_registry before writing; validate writer identity via ValidateCriticalKeyOwner() on every write." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_critical_key_without_registered_owner> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Write to a critical etcd key from code that is not the registered owner in critical_state_registry. Unknown writers must be rejected." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_critical_key_without_registered_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/critical_state.registry_ownership_required> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_critical_key_without_registered_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.storage_is_not_semantic_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_critical_key_without_registered_owner> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_minio_config_from_local_state_without_etcd_source> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_minio_contract_fields_in_separate_transactions> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_service_version_empty_string_to_struct> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_service_version_empty_string_to_struct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Always: srv.Version = Version (the package-level var). Never srv.Version = \"\"." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_service_version_empty_string_to_struct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Version variable is set by ldflags at build time. Writing \"\" clobbers it. The running service then reports version=0.0.0-dev regardless of what was actually built, making version drift undetectable. This causes permanent service.running_version_mismatch findings." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_service_version_empty_string_to_struct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Write an empty string to srv.Version in service main() instead of assigning the package-level Version variable (from zz_version_generated.go)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_service_version_empty_string_to_struct> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_service_version_empty_string_to_struct> <https://globular.io/awareness#protects> <https://globular.io/awareness#sourceFile/golang%2Fglobular_service%2Flifecycle.go> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/write_stream_data_before_resolving_authorized_path> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_desired_state_via_grpc_only_during_bootstrap> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_desired_state_via_grpc_only_during_bootstrap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Bootstrap writes seed initial state; all subsequent desired state must flow through the BOM release pipeline. Never rely on a one-time gRPC bootstrap for ongoing desired state management." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_desired_state_via_grpc_only_during_bootstrap> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Write desired state records only through the bootstrap gRPC call at cluster init time, without ensuring the BOM pipeline runs on every subsequent upgrade." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_desired_state_via_grpc_only_during_bootstrap> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_desired_state_via_grpc_only_during_bootstrap> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/service.desired_state.bom_completeness> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_desired_state_via_grpc_only_during_bootstrap> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_new_port_to_etcd_before_listener_is_confirmed_reachable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/writing_service_desired_version_directly_from_cli> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/zero_value_response_on_authority_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ForbiddenFix> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/zero_value_response_on_authority_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Distinguish at least three outcomes per typed RPC: (1) authoritative success with the value, (2) authoritative absence (NotFound) when the backing store confirms the row does not exist, (3) Unavailable when the backing store could not be consulted. Repository's `ResolveArtifact` (resolver.go) is the exemplar — three failure modes, three response shapes." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/zero_value_response_on_authority_unavailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Authority RPC returns `&Response{}, nil` (zero value, no error) when the backing store errors. Caller cannot distinguish \"no data\" from \"the authority couldn't check\"." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/zero_value_response_on_authority_unavailable> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.authority_must_express_uncertainty> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/zero_value_response_on_authority_unavailable> <https://globular.io/awareness#affects> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/meta.fallback_must_degrade_semantics> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#forbiddenFix/zero_value_response_on_authority_unavailable> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/forbidden_fixes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#guardrail/activation_empty_policy.behavior_change_in_high_risk> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#Guardrail> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#guardrail/activation_empty_policy.behavior_change_in_high_risk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Edit changes behavior in a high-risk directory or authority surface. This is the case that originally required the full awareness template." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#guardrail/activation_empty_policy.behavior_change_in_high_risk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Empty briefing policy: behavior_change_in_high_risk" .
