<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ImplementationPattern> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Cluster-doctor rules are the canonical answer to \"what is the current\ncross-layer health state\" — they observe all four layers and produce\nfindings, but produce no state. A rule that writes etcd, runs a process,\nor executes remediation inside Evaluate collapses the observe/mutate\nboundary that keeps the control plane deterministic: the same observation\npass must be safe to run on every node, on every tick, with no side\neffects. The two hard traps are (1) concluding FAIL from a partial\nsnapshot — snap.Errors must gate the verdict — and (2) emitting a\nnon-deterministic FindingID, which makes the same condition look like a\nnew finding every sweep and floods the event stream. Anchoring this recipe\nmeans an agent asked to \"add a cluster-doctor rule\" gets the shape and the\ntwo traps surfaced before writing, not an \"it compiles\" green light." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Diagnostic-only cluster-doctor rule" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "add a new cluster-doctor rule" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "adding a cluster-doctor rule" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "detect a new finding in cluster-doctor" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "implement a cluster_doctor rule" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "new cluster-doctor rule that detects" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "writing a cluster-doctor invariant rule" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#assertionMethod> "declared" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/implementation_patterns/doctor_rule_diagnostic_only.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "clientv3.Delete" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "clientv3.Put" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "exec.Command" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "exec.CommandContext" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Build Evidence from the snapshot (source service / rpc / observed key-values) for every Finding — a finding without the facts it was derived from cannot be trusted for remediation." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Consult snap.Errors before drawing conclusions: a partial snapshot must yield CHECK_ERROR / UNKNOWN, never a false FAIL (invariant:doctor_rule_evaluate_must_consult_snap_errors)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Distinguish FAIL from CHECK_ERROR and UNKNOWN — missing evidence is not evidence of failure (invariant:evidence.missing_is_not_known_bad)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Emit a deterministic FindingID via FindingID(invariant, subject, summary) so the same condition produces the same finding id across every sweep — non-deterministic ids defeat the doctor's delta/cache logic." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Implement the rules.Invariant interface: ID() returns a stable dotted identifier (e.g. \"artifact.integrity\"), plus Category(), Scope() (\"cluster\" | \"node\" | \"service\"), and Evaluate(snap *collector.Snapshot, cfg Config) []Finding." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Return findings only. Never mutate cluster state inside Evaluate — the doctor observes, the workflow mutates (invariant:cluster_doctor.observer_only_never_writes_etcd)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "canonical_rule:golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/rules/artifact_integrity.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "interface_contract:golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/rules/invariant.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "FindingID" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ImplementationPattern> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Globular service clients must share the central bootstrap so TLS,\nmesh routing, reconnect behavior, call-depth, cluster id propagation,\nand cached connection reuse stay consistent across every service. Any\nclient that dials gRPC directly or builds its own TLS config drifts\nfrom the cluster's mTLS contract silently — the call may succeed in\none environment and fail in another with no clear cause.\n\nReal incident captured 2026-06: a fresh awareness_graph_client was\nwritten with a custom Option / WithInsecure / direct grpc.Dial\npattern. It built and tests passed, but the CLI could not reach the\ncluster service because the client cert install hook never ran. The\nfix was to refactor to mirror echo_client / rbac_client — the same\nrecipe documented in this pattern. Anchoring this recipe in awareness\nmeans the next agent reading a briefing for a new client task gets\nthe recipe surfaced, not just an \"it compiles\" green light." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Standard Globular gRPC service client" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "adding client package for a new service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "creating a new Go client for a Globular gRPC service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "implementing service client for awareness-graph or similar" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "new gRPC client wrapper for a Globular service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "refactoring service client connection logic" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "wrapping a protobuf client with Globular helpers" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#assertionMethod> "declared" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/implementation_patterns/grpc_client_standard.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "credentials.NewClientTLSFromFile" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "credentials.NewTLS" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "grpc.Dial" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "grpc.NewClient" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Client struct exposes Get/Set Address, Domain, Port, Mac, State, Name, Id, and TLS Get/Set methods so it satisfies the globular_client.Client interface." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Close() closes the stored client.cc connection." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Constructor calls client.Reconnect() before returning so the client is ready." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Constructor calls globular.InitClient(client, address, id) — never duplicate its address normalization, cluster id propagation, or TLS bootstrap." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Constructor is named NewXxxService_Client(address string, id string) and returns (*Xxx_Client, error)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "GetCtx() returns globular.GetClientContext(client) so the auth token + call-depth metadata propagate." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Invoke(method, rqst, ctx) delegates to globular.InvokeClientRequest(client.c, ctx, method, rqst)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Reconnect() assigns the typed protobuf client: client.c = pb.NewXxxServiceClient(client.cc)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Reconnect() calls globular.GetClientConnection(client) and stores the *grpc.ClientConn on the client struct." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Typed RPC wrappers build the protobuf request struct and call client.c.<Rpc>(ctx, req) — never reach past the typed client." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "canonical_minimal:golang/echo/echo_client/echo_client.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "richer_reference:golang/monitoring/monitoring_client/monitoring_client.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "globular.GetClientConnection" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "globular.GetClientContext" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "globular.InitClient" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "globular.InvokeClientRequest" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.grpc_client_standard> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ImplementationPattern> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "RBAC is a deny-wins system. Explicit deny is the strongest signal in the\nmodel: it must beat allow, ownership, and every service-account or\nbootstrap shortcut, and it must propagate down a resource path so a deny\non a parent covers its children. The forbidden shape is an authorization\npath that evaluates owner/allow/service-account first and only checks deny\nafterward (or not at all on a bypass branch) — that lets a shortcut grant\naccess the operator explicitly revoked. The companion trap is trusting the\ntransport (peer cert / proxy header) instead of the originating principal,\nwhich lets a front door speak for a subject it never authenticated.\nvalidateAccessDenied runs first, ancestor-aware, on every path including\nthe bootstrap fallback." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RBAC explicit-deny precedence" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "add an rbac permission check" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "authorize a subject against a resource path" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "change RBAC access validation" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "change how rbac resolves permissions" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "modify rbac access checks" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "rbac deny or allow precedence" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#assertionMethod> "declared" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/implementation_patterns/rbac_explicit_deny_precedence.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Authorize against the originating principal (JWT claims / signed metadata), never the peer certificate or a proxy/user header alone (invariant:backend_must_check_originating_principal_not_only_peer_cert)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Bootstrap / service-account fallbacks must not bypass an explicit deny — the deny gate runs before the shortcut, not after." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Check explicit deny first via validateAccessDenied before any allow, owner, or service-account shortcut — an explicit deny overrides allow, ownership, and bootstrap fallbacks." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Walk path ancestors when checking deny: a deny on a parent resource path denies the child; validateAccessDenied must not stop at the leaf." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "canonical:golang/rbac/rbac_server/rbac_access.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "deny_override_reference:golang/rbac/rbac_server/rbac_deny_override_test.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "validateAccessAllowed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "validateAccessDenied" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ImplementationPattern> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every meaningful cluster mutation flows through the Workflow Service:\nthe controller decides, the workflow coordinates, node agents execute.\nRemediation is the most dangerous mutation surface in the system, so it\nhas the strictest gate — leadership, evidence trust, approval-token\nbinding, risk class, dry-run, and a hard block on ETCD_PUT/ETCD_DELETE/\nNODE_REMOVE. The forbidden shape is a remediation handler that reaches for\nos/exec or an etcd write directly because \"it's just a restart\": that\nbypasses the gate, leaves no replayable workflow record, and can act on a\nfinding whose evidence has gone stale. Delegating through\nStartRemediationWorkflow keeps remediation idempotent, audited, and\nre-runnable, and keeps convergence verification in the loop." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Remediation via workflow delegation" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "add a remediation handler" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "auto-remediate a cluster finding" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "change cluster-doctor remediation execution" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "execute a remediation action" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "remediation handler for a finding" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "wire cluster-doctor remediation to a workflow" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#assertionMethod> "declared" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/implementation_patterns/remediation_via_workflow.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "clientv3.Delete" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "clientv3.Put" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "exec.Command" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#forbidsCall> "exec.CommandContext" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "After execution, verify convergence before declaring the finding resolved — execution is not proof of repair." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Bind the approval token to action, target, evidence digest, and finding id; stale or unverifiable evidence must block execution (invariant:doctor.approval_token_binding_prevents_replay)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Delegate actual execution to the workflow service via StartRemediationWorkflow and actor callbacks — the doctor decides, the workflow coordinates, node agents execute. No direct mutation in the doctor process." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Preserve risk class, approval, and dry-run semantics. HARD_BLOCKED actions (ETCD_PUT, ETCD_DELETE, NODE_REMOVE) must never auto-execute (invariant:doctor.hard_blocked_actions_never_execute)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Require the authoritative (elected leader) cluster-doctor instance before authorizing or executing remediation (invariant:doctor.remediation_requires_leader)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Resolve the finding from the last-known findings by its FindingID — never act on a finding the doctor cannot currently observe (invariant:doctor.evidence_trust_must_be_authoritative_for_execution)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "canonical:golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/handler_remediation_workflow.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "gate_reference:golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/remediation_gate_test.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "runner_glue:golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/workflow_runner.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "StartRemediationWorkflow" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ImplementationPattern> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Installability is a lifecycle fact, not a storage fact. The recurring\nrepository incidents (INC-2026-0012 skeleton manifests, INC-2026-0013\nmislabeled pinned bytes) all share one shape: object presence was trusted\nas installability authority, or an authoritative metadata write and the\nblob write were not treated atomically. The Globular-shaped way is that\npublish_state in Scylla is the column of record; IsInstallable() reads\nthat, the transition is durable before resolvers can see it, and a\npost-write object-store failure becomes a finding rather than a silent\ndowngrade of authority. Desired build IDs are hard deletion roots so GC\nand repair can never strand a build the cluster still wants. This pattern\nkeeps the four-layer model intact: Repository answers \"does this version\nexist and is it installable?\" from metadata it owns, not from a bucket\nlisting." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Repository metadata is the installability authority" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "change repository publish workflow" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "decide whether an artifact is installable" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "modify artifact publish state" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "repository artifact garbage collection or repair" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "repository publish workflow installability" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "repository resolve or installability logic" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#assertionMethod> "declared" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/implementation_patterns/repository_metadata_authority.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Derive installability from lifecycle metadata — ArtifactPipelineState.IsInstallable() / isRowInstallable() — never from object presence in MinIO or the CAS alone." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Gate every state change through IsTransitionAllowed(from, to) + transitionArtifactState; the durable publish_state must be committed before installability is exposed to resolvers (invariant:meta.state_mutations_must_be_durably_committed_before_side_effects)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "If the object store fails AFTER the authoritative metadata write, emit a finding (markPipelineMissingBlob / markBrokenForReason) — do not silently rewrite the authoritative publish_state back to an earlier value (invariant:derived_state.must_not_block_authority)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Treat desired build IDs as hard roots for deletion / revocation safety — never GC or revoke a build that a DesiredService record still references (invariant:cluster.desired_state_authority_over_installed_state)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "publish_state is the column of record; discovery reads Scylla first. Object presence is corroborating evidence, not the source of truth." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "publish_path:golang/repository/repository_server/publish_workflow.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "reachability_guard:golang/repository/repository_server/reachability_guard.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "resolve_path:golang/repository/repository_server/resolver.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "state_authority:golang/repository/repository_server/artifact_state.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "IsTransitionAllowed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "transitionArtifactState" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#ImplementationPattern> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Workflows must be idempotent and safe to replay, and they must reach a\nterminal state. The durable step receipt is what makes replay safe: it\nrecords that a side effect already completed so a resumed run skips it\ninstead of doing it twice. The forbidden shape is a resume path that\nre-executes a step purely because the run is being replayed, without first\nconsulting readStepReceipt — that double-applies side effects (double\ninstalls, double etcd writes, double restarts). The second trap is a\nreceipt written from intent rather than completion, which lets a canSkip\npredicate treat a half-done step as done. Receipts plus a failure\nclassifier (class + reason + retry policy + unblock signal) give resume\nthe information to converge instead of looping." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Durable workflow step receipt" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "add a workflow step that has side effects" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "change workflow step execution" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "handle workflow step failure classification" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "make a workflow step idempotent on replay" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "modify workflow resume" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "workflow resume after a failed step" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#assertionMethod> "declared" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/implementation_patterns/workflow_durable_step_receipt.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "A half-done step must not look done: the receipt must reflect actual completion, not intent, so canSkip predicates do not satisfy a partial state (invariant:meta.half_done_must_not_look_done)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "For failed or blocked steps, record failure class, reason code, retry policy, and unblock signals via classifyStepFailureForReceipt so resume can choose retry vs. wait deterministically." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Keep reconciliation bounded and idempotent — no infinite deterministic retry (invariant:convergence.no_infinite_retry)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "On resume, call readStepReceipt before re-executing a step. A present receipt means the side effect already happened — skip it, never replay (invariant: a completed side effect must not repeat without checking the durable receipt)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustFollow> "Write a durable receipt via writeStepReceipt after a step completes or after a classified blocking failure — the write IS the completion obligation for the side effect (invariant:meta.write_creates_completion_obligation)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "canonical:golang/workflow/workflow_server/step_receipts.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "failure_classifier:golang/workflow/workflow_server/receipt_failure_classifier.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#referenceFile> "resume_path:golang/workflow/workflow_server/executor_resume.go" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "classifyStepFailureForReceipt" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "readStepReceipt" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresCall> "writeStepReceipt" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
