<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.remediation_hard_blocked_etcd_delete> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedKnowledgeNode> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/doctor.hard_blocked_actions_never_execute> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.remediation_hard_blocked_etcd_delete> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedPreflightStatus> "OK" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.remediation_hard_blocked_etcd_delete> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedRiskClass> "DATA_LOSS_RISK" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#OutcomeFeedback> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Root cause was an architecture seam, not data loss: all 236 blobs were\nintact on ryzen. The repository's blob authority is node-local POSIX CAS\n(/var/lib/globular/repository/artifacts); Scylla metadata is cluster-wide;\nday-1 joins staged archives to /var/lib/globular/packages (node-agent\ncache) but nothing populated the new repository instance's own CAS — so\ndell/nuc instances truthfully reported \"missing HERE\" as 57 scope-blind\ncluster-sounding errors. A MinIO blob \"mirror tier\" existed in code as the\nimplied cross-node transport, contradicting the hard rule that packages\nnever live in MinIO.\n\nOperator decision (Dave, 2026-06-12): enforce the hard rule. Fix shipped in\nservices v1.2.210 (commit 4b3173ab): (1) initStorage no longer constructs\nthe MinIO blob mirror — local POSIX CAS is the sole blob tier; (2) new\nday-1 seeder (blob_seed.go) materializes PUBLISHED blobs into the local CAS\nfrom the staged join packages, digest-gated against the Scylla manifest\nchecksum via atomic verified writes — metadata is authority, staged files\nare evidence, filenames never decide identity. Regression tests\nTestBlobSeed_* encode the contract. Day-0→day-1 reinstall test pending." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "57 missing_blob findings after multi-node joins — node-local CAS never seeded on day-1; fixed in code (v1.2.210) plus MinIO blob mirror removed by policy" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/outcomes/inc-repository-blob-locality-multinode.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#decision> "applied" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#forFinding> "repository.identity.missing_blob_for_published_manifest ×57 (dell + nuc repository instances, scope-blind summaries)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#forTask> "explain why /var/lib/globular/repository/artifacts is empty on day-1 joined nodes and ensure packages never end up in MinIO" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#observedAt> "2026-06-12" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeStatus> "success" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#reasonCode> "day1_join_never_seeded_repository_local_cas" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedKnowledgeNode> <https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedKnowledgeNode> <https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedKnowledgeNode> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.artifact.installable_compound_predicate> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedPreflightStatus> "OK" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#outcomeFeedback/outcome.repository_blob_locality_multinode_57_findings> <https://globular.io/awareness#usedRiskClass> "ARCHITECTURE_SENSITIVE" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RepairPlan> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This is a release-boundary repair: the source change is inert until both the\nhost service and the xDS/gateway redeploy. Direct-port access is diagnostic /\ndegraded-mode evidence only and must never become the permanent client path\n(see forbidden_fix clients_must_not_permanently_bypass_gateway_for_cohosted_services)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Restore gateway routing for a co-hosted gRPC service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "a co-hosted gRPC service returns HTTP 200 text/html through the gateway" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "a second gRPC service on an existing process is unreachable via the gateway" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "backend healthy on its direct port but the gateway route is missing" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "native-gRPC calls to a service fail with unexpected content-type text/html" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/repair_plans/declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "Globular/internal/xds/watchers/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/ai_memory/ai_memory_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasBlastRadius> "service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasConfidence> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Declare the co-hosted service in the host service's registration metadata (HostedServices) so it is serialized into the etcd service config." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Ensure xDS route generation emits a prefix route for each declared hosted name targeting the host service's cluster (Globular internal/xds/watchers/watcher.go)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Rebuild and redeploy BOTH the host service (so it re-registers with HostedServices) and the xDS/gateway (so it reads the field and regenerates the route table)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRollbackStep> "Removing the HostedServices declaration and regenerating xDS reverts to the prior route table; no destructive state change is involved." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/gateway.cohosted_grpc_services_must_be_declared> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#producesOutcomeFeedback> "update the runtime finding's behavioral signal runtime_status to RESOLVED once the gateway probe confirms the co-hosted RPC succeeds" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "gateway.cohosted_grpc_service_route_missing_returns_html" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresApprovalGate> "review_required" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The backend serves the co-hosted gRPC service on its direct port (confirm with a direct-port reflection/RPC probe)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The gateway failure is the distinctive content-type signal (HTTP 200 text/html), not a plain Unavailable." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresRuntimeEvidence> "memory_* (or another registered-service RPC) succeeds through the gateway while the co-hosted service returns text/html over the same endpoint — proving path-based route absence, not a down backend." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresTest> <https://globular.io/awareness#test/xds_emits_routes_for_hosted_services> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Do NOT close the runtime finding on source-merge or green tests — close it only after the gateway probe confirms the co-hosted RPC succeeds at runtime." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Through the gateway: the co-hosted service RPC now succeeds (no text/html), the registered service RPC still succeeds, and the direct-port probe still succeeds." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.declare_hosted_services_and_regenerate_xds_routes> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RepairPlan> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The observe/mutate split is the boundary that keeps every doctor sweep\nside-effect free: the doctor observes and delegates, the workflow gate\nexecutes. Remediation is the most dangerous mutation surface, so it carries\nthe strictest gate — leader, evidence trust, approval-token binding, risk\nclass, dry-run, and a hard block on ETCD_PUT/ETCD_DELETE/NODE_REMOVE." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Remediate a cluster-doctor finding that requires a mutation" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "auto-remediation was blocked, how to proceed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "doctor wants to delete an etcd key" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "execute a remediation the doctor proposed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "remediate a cluster finding safely" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "the doctor found a finding that needs a mutation" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#appliesToAuthorityDomain> <https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/repair_plans/doctor_finding_requires_remediation.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasBlastRadius> "cluster" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasConfidence> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Bind the approval token to action + target + evidence digest + finding id; preserve risk class and dry-run." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Build the remediation plan in the doctor — never mutate cluster state inside Evaluate or any doctor handler." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Delegate execution to the workflow service via StartRemediationWorkflow and actor callbacks — the doctor decides, the workflow coordinates, node agents execute." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRollbackStep> "Remediation rolls back through its own workflow run / actor Verify path; the doctor never reverses state directly." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster_doctor.observer_only_never_writes_etcd> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/doctor.hard_blocked_actions_never_execute> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/doctor.remediation_requires_leader> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#producesOutcomeFeedback> "record an OutcomeFeedback for the finding with decision (executed/blocked/rejected) and the convergence result" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "doctor.finding_requires_mutation" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "doctor.remediation_needed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresApprovalGate> "human_approval_required" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The action is not HARD_BLOCKED (ETCD_PUT, ETCD_DELETE, NODE_REMOVE never auto-execute)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The finding is still observable in last-known findings and its evidence is fresh and trusted (stale/unverifiable evidence must block execution)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "This cluster-doctor instance is the elected leader (only the leader may authorize or execute remediation)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresRuntimeEvidence> "The finding re-resolved from last-known findings with a fresh evidence digest bound to the approval token." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "After the workflow completes, re-run the doctor check for the finding and confirm it clears." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Confirm convergence before declaring the finding resolved — execution is not proof of repair." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.doctor_finding_requires_remediation> <https://globular.io/awareness#usesImplementationPattern> <https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.remediation_via_workflow> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RepairPlan> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "RBAC is deny-wins: explicit deny beats allow, ownership, and every\nservice-account or bootstrap shortcut, and propagates down resource paths.\nThe companion trap is trusting the transport (peer cert / proxy header)\ninstead of the originating principal." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Repair an RBAC permission regression without weakening deny" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "a user suddenly cannot access a resource" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "access allowed that should have been denied" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "deny rule not taking effect" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "permission denied unexpectedly after a change" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "rbac permission regression" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#appliesToAuthorityDomain> <https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.rbac_permissions> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/repair_plans/rbac_permission_regression.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/rbac/rbac_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasBlastRadius> "security" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasConfidence> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Apply the permission change through the RBAC typed RPC only; never write the permission store directly." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Confirm explicit deny is evaluated first and flat (validateAccessDenied) before any allow, owner, or service-account shortcut." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Walk path ancestors for deny — a deny on a parent path must deny the child." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRollbackStep> "Revert the permission change through the RBAC typed RPC; an explicit deny added during repair stays until removed via RPC." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/backend_must_check_originating_principal_not_only_peer_cert> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#producesOutcomeFeedback> "record an OutcomeFeedback noting whether deny precedence held after the change" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "rbac.access_allowed_unexpected" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "rbac.access_denied_unexpected" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "rbac.permission_regression" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresApprovalGate> "human_approval_required" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The regression is reproduced through the RBAC permission-evaluation path (ValidateAccess/ValidateAction), not inferred from a header or proxy claim." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The subject id is normalized (matchID) so a format mismatch is not masquerading as a permission bug." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresRuntimeEvidence> "An RBAC permission evaluation result for the (subject, path, permission) tuple — header/proxy/user-claim is not permission truth." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Confirm the bootstrap / service-account fallback does not bypass the explicit deny." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Re-evaluate the (subject, path, permission) tuple and confirm explicit deny still wins over allow/owner/bootstrap." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.rbac_permission_regression> <https://globular.io/awareness#usesImplementationPattern> <https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.rbac_explicit_deny_precedence> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RepairPlan> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Deleting the state key and hand-running ALTERs are RECOVERY stopgaps, not the\nfix. The durable fix is the disjoint key layout + version-bumped backfill ALTERs\nin code (forbidden_fixes: nest_a_data_key_under_an_etcd_mutex_prefix,\nadd_column_only_to_create_table_without_backfill_alter)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Recover a stuck/incomplete behavioral_memory schema migration" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "ai_memory blocks ~3 minutes on restart at 'behavioral schema migration: waiting for lock'" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "behavioral schema migration never reaches 'complete' for the current version" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "behavioral writes fail with CQL 'Unknown identifier <col>' (e.g. cluster_id)" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "behavioral_memory tables are missing columns the running handler writes" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/repair_plans/recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/ai_memory/ai_memory_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasBlastRadius> "service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasConfidence> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "DURABLE fix: land the code change — disjoint mutex/state key layout (mutex at .../lock) and backfill ALTERs guarded by a bumped schema version (services PR #46) — so no manual step is needed on the next upgrade." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Restart ai_memory once and confirm 'behavioral schema migration: complete' at the current schema_version." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "STOPGAP recovery (only if the code fix is not yet deployed): if the migration mutex prefix is poisoned by a nested state key, delete the state key (etcd del /globular/migrations/scylla/behavioral_memory/state) so the mutex prefix is empty; the migration re-runs and re-creates state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "STOPGAP recovery: for any column the handler writes that is missing from the live table, run an idempotent ALTER TABLE ADD on signals/evidence (cluster_id, condition_ref, severity, authority_level)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRollbackStep> "ALTER TABLE ADD is additive and idempotent; deleting the state key only forces an idempotent re-migration. No destructive rollback is required." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/etcd.mutex_key_must_not_prefix_non_lock_keys> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/scylla.added_column_requires_backfill_alter_for_upgrades> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#producesOutcomeFeedback> "record an OutcomeFeedback / behavioral signal noting the recovery (state key cleared and/or columns ALTER-added) and whether the durable code fix is deployed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "behavioral.migration_mutex_prefix_poisoned_by_state_key" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "behavioral.schema_column_missing_on_upgrade_no_backfill_alter" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresApprovalGate> "review_required" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "ai_memory backend is reachable on its direct gRPC port (the service is up, even if behavioral writes fail)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "etcd and ScyllaDB are reachable for inspection and DDL." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresRuntimeEvidence> "etcd get --prefix on the migration mutex prefix shows a non-lock key (e.g. /state) nested under it, and/or system_schema.columns shows the expected column missing from the live table." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresTest> <https://globular.io/awareness#test/TestBehavioralMigrationMutexKeyNotPrefixOfStateKey> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresTest> <https://globular.io/awareness#test/TestBehavioralSchemaPR9ColumnsHaveBackfillAlter> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "A behavioral write (RecordSignal) succeeds through the gateway (returns a signal id), not just on the direct port." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "ai_memory restart no longer blocks on the migration lock (acquire completes immediately)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.recover_stuck_behavioral_schema_migration> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "system_schema.columns shows the previously-missing columns present on signals and evidence." .
