<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RepairPlan> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "INC-2026-0012 (skeleton manifests) and INC-2026-0013 (mislabeled pinned\nbytes) are the canonical instances. The whole plan rests on one rule:\ninstallability is a lifecycle fact owned by the repository, not a storage\nfact. Object presence is corroborating evidence, never authority." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Repair a stuck repository artifact lifecycle / installability" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "an artifact is stuck and won't become installable" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "artifact lifecycle state looks wrong" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "nodes refuse to install a published artifact" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "publish state stuck in BLOB_VERIFIED or MANIFEST_WRITTEN" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "repository says the package exists but install fails" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#appliesToAuthorityDomain> <https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.repository_artifact_metadata> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/repair_plans/repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/repository/repository_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasBlastRadius> "cluster" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasConfidence> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "If the metadata write and the blob diverged, drive a single durable transitionArtifactState gated by IsTransitionAllowed; commit the durable publish_state before exposing installability." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "If the object is genuinely missing after an authoritative write, mark the artifact repair-needed (markPipelineMissingBlob) — do not silently rewrite publish_state back to an earlier value." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Read the authoritative lifecycle state via the repository resolver — never infer installability from MinIO/CAS object presence." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRollbackStep> "Quarantine or mark repair-needed through the repository-owned RPC path — never delete the blob directly." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster.desired_state_authority_over_installed_state> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/repository.artifact.installable_compound_predicate> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#producesOutcomeFeedback> "record an OutcomeFeedback linking repository_metadata_authority + installable_compound_predicate with the resolved/blocked status" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFailureMode> <https://globular.io/awareness#failureMode/identity.field_semantic_drift_across_writers> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "repository.artifact_state_stuck" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "repository.installability_mismatch" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "repository.publish_state_not_installable" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresApprovalGate> "review_required" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "Confirm a DesiredService still references the affected build id (a desired build is a hard deletion/revocation root)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "Confirm the repository owner RPC is reachable and reporting the artifact's lifecycle metadata (publish_state, artifact_state)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresRuntimeEvidence> "Authoritative publish_state/artifact_state from the repository owner RPC — object-store/POSIX presence is supporting evidence only." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Confirm no desired build id is left orphaned by the transition." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Re-resolve the artifact: IsInstallable() must agree with the durable publish_state." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.repository_artifact_lifecycle_stuck> <https://globular.io/awareness#usesImplementationPattern> <https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.repository_metadata_authority> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RepairPlan> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Runtime evidence informs findings and convergence but owns no desired\ntruth. Freshness and scope are part of every assertion's meaning: missing\nevidence is not evidence of failure, and stale evidence must degrade to a\nhint, never to a PASS or a definitive failure verdict." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Handle stale, missing, or conflicting runtime evidence" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "a finding is based on a partial snapshot" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "evidence is stale or conflicting" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "health verdict from missing evidence" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "nodes report contradictory health states" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "two probes disagree about runtime state" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#appliesToAuthorityDomain> <https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.runtime_evidence> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/repair_plans/runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/cluster_doctor/cluster_doctor_server/collector/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/node_agent/node_agent_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasBlastRadius> "node" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasConfidence> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Classify the verdict as UNKNOWN / CHECK_ERROR / DEGRADED — never PASS — when evidence is stale, missing, or from a non-owner path." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Consult snap.Errors before drawing any conclusion: a partial snapshot must not be consumed as complete." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Request fresh owner-path evidence before making any convergence or health claim." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRollbackStep> "No state was mutated — this plan only re-classifies and re-requests evidence; there is nothing to roll back." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/evidence.missing_is_not_known_bad> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#producesOutcomeFeedback> "record an OutcomeFeedback noting the evidence classification and whether a PASS was correctly withheld" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "evidence.conflicting" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "evidence.from_non_owner_path" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "evidence.missing" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "evidence.stale" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresApprovalGate> "review_required" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The evidence in question carries (or is missing) source service, observed time, and trust level." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The owner path for this evidence is known (e.g. node-agent heartbeat, doctor collector snapshot)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Confirm no convergence/PASS claim was made on stale or conflicting evidence." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Confirm the finding now carries fresh, owner-path evidence with a trust level, or remains explicitly UNKNOWN." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.runtime_evidence_stale_or_conflicting> <https://globular.io/awareness#usesImplementationPattern> <https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.doctor_rule_diagnostic_only> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RepairPlan> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The durable receipt is what makes replay safe. The forbidden shape is a\nresume path that re-executes a step purely because the run is being\nreplayed, without first consulting the receipt — that double-applies side\neffects (double installs, double grants, double restarts)." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Resume a blocked or failed workflow step safely" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "a step keeps erroring and the run is stuck" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "a workflow run never finishes" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "resume a stuck workflow run safely" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "workflow run blocked on a failed step" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#activationTrigger> "workflow stalled mid-run after a crash" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#appliesToAuthorityDomain> <https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.remediation_execution> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/repair_plans/workflow_resume_blocked_step.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#coversPath> "golang/workflow/workflow_server/" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasBlastRadius> "service" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasConfidence> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Consult readStepReceipt first. A present receipt means the side effect already happened — skip it, never replay." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "For a failed/blocked step, read its failure class, reason code, retry policy, and unblock signals (classifyStepFailureForReceipt) and apply the step's ResumePolicy." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRepairStep> "Re-execute only steps that are RUNNING-at-crash or have no durable receipt; treat SUCCEEDED/FAILED/SKIPPED as terminal." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasRollbackStep> "There is no blind rollback — a completed step stays completed; correction flows through a new bounded workflow run." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustNotViolateInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/convergence.no_infinite_retry> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#producesOutcomeFeedback> "record an OutcomeFeedback for the run with the resume decision and whether replay was avoided" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFailureMode> <https://globular.io/awareness#failureMode/workflow.orphan_lease_slow_step_double_claim> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "workflow.resume_blocked" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "workflow.run_stalled" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#repairsFindingClass> "workflow.step_failed" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresApprovalGate> "review_required" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The durable step receipt for the affected step has been read (readStepReceipt) before any re-execution decision." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresPrecondition> "The run is owned by a single executor (orphan-claim fencing is intact) so resume cannot double-claim." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresRuntimeEvidence> "The step receipt: presence means the side effect already completed; absence/failed means it is eligible for the resume policy." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Confirm no step's side effect was applied twice." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#requiresVerification> "Confirm the run reaches a terminal state (SUCCEEDED or FAILED) — workflows must be bounded." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#status> "active" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#repairPlan/globular.repair.workflow_resume_blocked_step> <https://globular.io/awareness#usesImplementationPattern> <https://globular.io/awareness#implementationPattern/globular.pattern.workflow_durable_step_receipt> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://globular.io/awareness#RuntimeEvidence> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Desired state must be read through the owner service path. Direct storage\nreads are diagnostic evidence only." .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cluster desired-state evidence" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#authoredIn> "docs/awareness/runtime_evidence.yaml" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#cannotPromoteToPassWhenStale> "true" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#evidenceForAuthorityDomain> <https://globular.io/awareness#authorityDomain/authority.cluster_desired_state> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#evidenceForInvariant> <https://globular.io/awareness#invariant/cluster.desired_state_authority_over_installed_state> .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasFreshnessWindow> "must reflect the latest controller-committed desired state" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#hasTrustLevel> "high" .
<https://globular.io/awareness#runtimeEvidence/evidence.cluster_desired_state> <https://globular.io/awareness#mustComeFromOwnerPath> "true" .
